{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.542918Z","id":"32f2a2bb176b311efceeb273587a72804117cc77007d5876c5663683cdee03f4","body":{"detail":"_cancel pops the screen and drops the attempt's result, but the Future from Launcher.make keeps running, so the agent still calls createArtifact and the app appears in the launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart _onEvent) after the person cancelled. The make signature in the plan (Future<String> Function(String request)) carries no cancel signal, and AgentLoop.newApp(String) (plan Task F4b) takes none either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"7ca33a2900a53644f52b5ff4b0a9d74da288bfdc558a7833cd30a0aaf16c1e1c"},"suggested_fix":"Give make a cancel signal (for example a Future<void> the screen completes on Cancel) and pass it to the backend as AgentRequest.cancelled, so a cancelled run creates nothing.","summary":"Cancel on the making screen abandons the run but does not stop it: the new app still lands","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543019Z","id":"fdb9b26782663b9fa19f2d5b0be6ff925455111c36edbbbb91062a8eba1524ee","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 6.1 starts the say-usable timer on submit and stops it on the new app's first ready. Launcher has no Timings, so the make callback is the only place that sees the submit. Whoever builds Launcher (AppRoot, plan Task F9) must call timings.start(sayUsable) inside make before AgentLoop.newApp, or no say-usable record is ever written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"5bd238290e24231180b1f26a2e922e0187c1ad6e815a0027c834fc1cf8bc3e69"},"summary":"Submit does not start the say-usable timer here; the make passed in has to","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:32:46.543053Z","id":"782d52488d2d36a10c5e4249160db6eb9fa7369c5b7ff7a27c0347579f2b84cb","body":{"detail":"The tile list is listArtifacts once at start plus version and artifact_deleted events. Stream errors are ignored, and nothing reloads after a daemon restart, where events missed while the daemon was down (or IDs a new daemon does not resume from Last-Event-ID) leave the grid stale until a pull to refresh.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"eeb475356a5701b9b777821c904ef2c55a2f9496e769d48a18dc6d3d9a843c24"},"suggested_fix":"Reload with listArtifacts when the event stream reconnects or the daemon endpoint changes (AppRoot knows both).","summary":"The launcher never reloads its list after the event stream drops events","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972098Z","id":"5d09634475a2480647d4de7478890b5a505a18d9ab03720a5d446bcac7c223ad","body":{"detail":"Failure: tap New app, submit any request, tap Cancel (or system back) while 'Making' shows; AgentLoop.newApp keeps running, calls createArtifact, and the launcher's version event adds the tile the person cancelled. Launcher.make (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart:30) is Future<String> Function(String) and carries no cancel signal, although AgentLoop.newApp(request, {Future<void>? cancelled}) (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:114) and AgentRequest.cancelled now exist. _cancel (making_screen.dart:95) and the PopScope (making_screen.dart:110) only bump _attempt. No test covers cancel stopping the run.","kind":"blocker","references":"32f2a2bb176b311efceeb273587a72804117cc77007d5876c5663683cdee03f4","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"7ca33a2900a53644f52b5ff4b0a9d74da288bfdc558a7833cd30a0aaf16c1e1c"},"suggested_fix":"Change make to Future<String> Function(String request, Future<void> cancelled); MakingScreen owns a Completer<void> per attempt, completes it on Cancel, back, Open Settings, Edit, dispose and Retry-of-a-stale-attempt, and treats AgentError.cancelled as a silent end. Widget test: Cancel completes the future make received, and a make that honours it never calls open.","summary":"Cancel and back on the making screen do not stop the run: the cancelled app is still created and appears in the launcher","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972568Z","id":"7a14c0c260ca5cda20193669a49725b134abd00d7faefe8dd92c329c272acf67","body":{"detail":"Failure: open the launcher, let the daemon restart (app resume after Android kills it, or a new daemon epoch) and create or delete an artifact in the gap; ClaxApi.events (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart:102-107) delivers ready{resumed:false} or resync, which _onEvent drops because they carry no artifact_id, so the new app is missing (or the deleted one still shown) until a manual pull to refresh. The initial ready is also ignored, so a version event that lands between listArtifacts and the stream opening can be lost. No test pushes ready/resync.","kind":"blocker","references":"782d52488d2d36a10c5e4249160db6eb9fa7369c5b7ff7a27c0347579f2b84cb","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"37e3197b5ffc01331c4c3414fe9feda8fac1a55f0e0fc1137bcf2c83730bd9bf"},"suggested_fix":"In _onEvent, call _load() on resync and on ready whose data.resumed is not true; test with FakeClaxApi that a resync after an out-of-band seedArtifact shows the new tile.","summary":"The launcher ignores the event stream's ready{resumed:false} and resync, so its grid stays stale after a daemon restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/new_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.972902Z","id":"5ef533b41b5df2b991505e8efb31f6e518890159e0ba2bf9d282cb39f1ee158b","body":{"detail":"VoiceDenied/VoiceUnsupported disable the mic and put the reason in the Tooltip (new_sheet.dart:202); status (line 147) shows only a voice error or 'Listening…', so on touch the person sees a greyed mic-off icon with no explanation unless they long-press it. The launcher's FAB carries a mic icon (launcher.dart:133), so the promise of voice silently fails. Android stops re-prompting after a second refusal, so retrying availability() is not enough; rendered at 412x892 the denied sheet shows no text at all about why.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"f89c8438ceb8b8ce9392fb966d5cfdc1ffa7b8451332804e7ace010cacf99e73"},"suggested_fix":"Show micReason in the status line when the mic is unavailable, and for VoiceDenied offer an action that opens the app's system settings (e.g. the permission_handler or app_settings plugin's openAppSettings).","summary":"With the mic denied the reason is only a tooltip, invisible on a phone, and nothing leads to the permission setting","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973028Z","id":"4fd5aa1d184a730e40041249421322c6dc6c7226f7d3cbacacba23c3e48ff437","body":{"detail":"On a fresh phone install the backend is the Messages API with no key. The person taps New app, dictates, taps Make it, and only then sees 'Add your Claude API key in Settings' (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:106) on the failure screen. Launcher has no way to know a key is missing.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"b80eb65d6027f3d4b3d2ef812b226a35d4b4fb6bdb84bf3610e02a6f5529f920"},"suggested_fix":"Give Launcher an optional 'needsSetup' message (AppRoot computes it from SecureKey and the backend) and show a banner or the empty state 'Add your Claude API key to start' with an Open Settings button.","summary":"With no API key the first New app runs to a failure; the launcher could say so before the person speaks","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973179Z","id":"c6bfa8ec9de151dd6ce2207f53528e0caf71d9acebdf56768aee8b0ba2f8e512","body":{"detail":"On a phone the field reads 'Claude API key' with helper 'Kept in this device's secure storage'; nothing says the key is created at console.anthropic.com (Settings, API keys) or that it starts with sk-ant-, and there is no paste button, which is the realistic way to enter it on a phone.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"7bc79cfcdabb4ea0d93c625a92aca9b36ca4fc798787959b40ebadec5d87ce46"},"suggested_fix":"Helper text 'Create one at console.anthropic.com, then paste it here', a paste suffix action reading Clipboard, and a light format check (sk-ant- prefix) before Save key.","summary":"The key field does not say where a key comes from","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:02.973291Z","id":"44f41716054407ea3700b8ffc53bd1b6dee1ccfe4f8fc58a90fece0318ca08bb","body":{"detail":"Rendered at phone size it shows the sparkle icon, 'Making “a run tracker with weekly”…', an indeterminate bar and '7 s'. Generation takes tens of seconds; nothing says what is happening (writing, checking, publishing) or what is typical, and the five-word cut ends mid-phrase.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"a1f0e5ae0c8da6b83ff7fbbb7835326ecce852a028b2c61cc3baed440e898839"},"suggested_fix":"Let make report phases (the loop knows: prompt sent, result validated, resend after a validation failure, publishing) through an optional ValueListenable<String> and show it under the bar; after ~20 s add 'Usually under a minute'.","summary":"The making screen is an indeterminate bar and a seconds count; it has no sense of stage","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.584306Z","id":"2e8f2be32154154ed431ed7ac09e9a8855c8893a46834497c8ea910820dcae4a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"MakeApp takes a per-attempt cancel future, completed on Cancel, back, Edit, Open Settings, Retry and dispose. Tests 'Cancel stops the run: no app is created and nothing opens', 'system back on the making screen stops the run too' and 'Retry runs with a fresh signal; Edit stops the old one' pass. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"5d09634475a2480647d4de7478890b5a505a18d9ab03720a5d446bcac7c223ad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.584670Z","id":"ece9140e7a57e73c788249e430520361335bfbeb7f88991ce168d0eb230cd3de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed with blocker 5d096344: make now receives a cancel signal to pass to AgentLoop.newApp(request, cancelled: …); 'Cancel stops the run' passes. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"32f2a2bb176b311efceeb273587a72804117cc77007d5876c5663683cdee03f4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.584906Z","id":"1a2a246f46e25f3639307e55eb59de04a3a33158dc4a25467feacaa7639f3a96","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"_onEvent reloads listArtifacts on resync and on ready whose resumed is not true. Test 'resync and a fresh ready reload the list; a resumed ready does not' passes. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"7a14c0c260ca5cda20193669a49725b134abd00d7faefe8dd92c329c272acf67","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.585129Z","id":"0be83494ddb99fd614592a19c28b73f31fe683ff8cd6fdd52d77af17524f32d8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed with blocker 7a14c0c2: the launcher reloads on resync and on a ready that did not resume, so missed events are caught up. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"782d52488d2d36a10c5e4249160db6eb9fa7369c5b7ff7a27c0347579f2b84cb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/new_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.585497Z","id":"bc8519e3ad8475ff52f6be95cff0d83efb12d3ff6ce71b6891dce5c59407e64b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The reason shows as text under the field; VoiceDenied adds Open settings (VoiceInput.openPermissionSettings: Android MainActivity openAppSettings, macOS the Privacy_Microphone pane), and the sheet re-checks availability on resume. Tests 'a denied voice shows why, links to settings, keeps typing' and 'an unsupported voice shows why, with no settings link' pass; flutter build apk --debug builds the Kotlin change. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"5ef533b41b5df2b991505e8efb31f6e518890159e0ba2bf9d282cb39f1ee158b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.585743Z","id":"82e6882d54664c993a94b29d0c2d9b6013f7141df50a473c2b8dfd8c7e2313ad","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Launcher.needsKey shows 'Add your Claude API key to start making apps' with Add key opening Settings. Test 'without a key the launcher says so and links to Settings' passes. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"4fd5aa1d184a730e40041249421322c6dc6c7226f7d3cbacacba23c3e48ff437","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.585970Z","id":"67fae54935f10eaa1702e088a567ff0967100ff5823f1d7554ef930411596280","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Helper 'Create one at console.anthropic.com, then paste it here', a Paste action, and a refusal without the sk-ant- prefix. Tests 'the key field says where a key comes from', 'Paste fills the key field from the clipboard' and 'a key without the sk-ant- prefix is not saved' pass. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"c6bfa8ec9de151dd6ce2207f53528e0caf71d9acebdf56768aee8b0ba2f8e512","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:35:03.586601Z","id":"ae27eda6e85f7013f2497435c27d78c6718cfa5ca9a2fbed59fbbbae2e90277a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The making screen shows MakeStage (starting, writing, retrying, publishing) reported through make's stage callback, which StagedBackend drives from real backend runs; 'Usually under a minute' after 20 s; makingTitle cuts at a word boundary. Tests 'the making screen shows the stage make reports', 'StagedBackend reports writing, then publishing, under its own name', 'a second run is a retry' and 'the making title ellipsizes a long request at a word boundary' pass. flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart test/ui/new_sheet_test.dart test/ui/settings_test.dart test/ui/making_screen_test.dart: +50, All tests passed","supersedes":"44f41716054407ea3700b8ffc53bd1b6dee1ccfe4f8fc58a90fece0318ca08bb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:56:44.153164Z","id":"5d9e655dc6fec145851b4dad82943b903cba43fb137c7381665d112fe4ee6dec","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a 412 dp wide phone the grid (maxCrossAxisExtent 176, childAspectRatio 0.92) makes 3 columns of about 119 x 129 dp; a tile needs 16+52+(Spacer)+2 lines of titleMedium+16, about 132 dp, so any title that wraps (rendered with 'Mood journal' and the real Roboto font) throws 'A RenderFlex overflowed by 3.0 pixels on the bottom' at launcher.dart:246 and clips the second line. Agent-made titles often wrap ('Weekly run tracker'), and a larger system text scale makes it worse. The existing launcher tests use one-line titles only.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":202},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"5e869d09446019a6af7758c0913e683aca1088fd8bcc0dc0175214f72d54a58a"},"suggested_fix":"Use a grid with a mainAxisExtent derived from the text scale (or SliverGridDelegateWithMaxCrossAxisExtent(mainAxisExtent: ...)) instead of a fixed aspect ratio, and test a two-line title at 412 dp and at textScaler 1.3 with tester.takeException() isNull.","summary":"A tile whose title wraps to two lines overflows its fixed-aspect cell at phone width","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:56:44.153299Z","id":"64af9a54ec99b1d704e11407e78de22ef5c984351fe775cb151d0933cb965350","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop takes one backend factory at construction (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:115-127), while the stage callback belongs to one make call. Whoever builds Launcher.make (AppRoot, plan Task F9) must run each new app through a loop whose factory returns StagedBackend(base(), stage), and pass cancelled to AgentLoop.newApp; otherwise only MakeStage.starting is ever shown and Cancel stops nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"6f80fde4d394e5951186b81f1857c58b636034366dda59088e8507ed9085581f"},"suggested_fix":"In F9, build make as (request, cancelled, stage) => AgentLoop(..., backend: () => StagedBackend(backendFor(settings, key), stage)).newApp(request, cancelled: cancelled), and test in app_test.dart that a scripted backend's run moves the screen to 'Writing your app'.","summary":"Nothing wires StagedBackend yet; without it the making screen says 'Starting the agent' for the whole run","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:30:46.105271Z","id":"6b13e3911215e46d9310f2d6da71b0b4c74d72304d8104245e70e58393b7ea45","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The grid uses mainAxisExtent from _AppTile.extent (padding, badge, gap and two title lines at the current textScaler) instead of childAspectRatio. New tests in test/ui/launcher_test.dart 'tile layout at 412 dp': 'two-line titles fit at text scale 1.0' and '1.3' (Mood journal, Weekly run tracker; takeException isNull) and 'a very long title ellipsizes on two lines' (didExceedMaxLines) pass, flutter test test/ui/launcher_test.dart +26 all passed; with childAspectRatio 0.92 restored the same tests fail with 'A RenderFlex overflowed by 3.0 pixels' (1.0) and 'by 17 pixels' (1.3). Rendered at 412x892 with Roboto at scales 1.0 and 1.3: both titles wrap to two lines inside their tiles and the long title ends in an ellipsis.","supersedes":"5d9e655dc6fec145851b4dad82943b903cba43fb137c7381665d112fe4ee6dec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.096883Z","id":"f7450944998a14d6174355abac90aafd80fe04fccd8b184f9031a0db9a2f6df2","body":{"detail":"Flutter allows one active PlatformMenuBar (DefaultPlatformMenuDelegate locks to one context). AppScreen builds the whole macOS menu (app menu with About/Hide/Quit plus App > Comments with Cmd-K) while it is shown; when it is popped the delegate is unlocked and the launcher has no menu bar of its own. A PlatformMenuBar added higher up (lib/app.dart, Task F9) would conflict with this one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":713},"end":{"line":755},"content_hash":"5902a21655bc21ac3bfa7ea873a7421f1e0367581da4eac258bc0dd7dfdb3be1"},"suggested_fix":"F9: own one app-level PlatformMenuBar and pass App > Comments in from the app screen (for example a callback or a ValueNotifier the screen registers), and drop _menus here.","summary":"AppScreen installs the app's only PlatformMenuBar on macOS; leaving the screen clears the menu bar","tags":["needs-f9","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.096950Z","id":"098fa2674ee5a04b2ce6ddf57ff7b631804febce9c41fb4a03c79151f1c3e1bc","body":{"detail":"Escape is a CallbackShortcuts binding in the Flutter focus tree. After a tap in the page the platform WebView takes the keyboard focus on macOS and Flutter sees no key events, so Escape does nothing; Cmd-K still works there because it is the native menu item's key equivalent (app_screen.dart _menus). Unverified on the built macOS app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"fe6a8e274b583c4b7891ba68e4c8f4e65fa5a755312dcf6802e5337c9529ed26"},"summary":"Escape closes the panel only while Flutter has keyboard focus, not while the WebView does","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.096985Z","id":"86741946a5822ff25f5c663de4f4cd2c8da49498616a5114f2d54d3e54c9634c","body":{"detail":"Each pointer down and up over the page calls claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase, x, y}) by runJavaScript, after the WebView already handled the touch. The page converts physical pixels by window.devicePixelRatio, visualViewport.scale and its offset (host_protocol.dart AttestPointer). Widget tests check the Flutter side only (FakeAppSurface records the call); nothing has run a long-press in an Android WebView to confirm the shell takes the pick (record 8cc89df6 in web/bridge/src/.qual).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"5d9c867d152c668d138df3684aac52c290421da6ae5dfb65eff976cd5e0b9c3a"},"suggested_fix":"Task F10 or a device run: long-press an element in app mode on Android and macOS and confirm the pick, with the attestation in place and without it.","summary":"Finger attestation and its CSS pixel conversion are unverified in a real WebView","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.097019Z","id":"4c2bfc9063e576c6ad98007072b6dbf8a6220e880b7f2f3a7dbff7feb3c6fecb","body":{"detail":"The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.7) describes the panel as a sheet over the lower 45%. Here the page is resized to the space above the panel instead, because the shell docks its composer at the bottom of the WebView (web/shell/src/app/app.css): an overlay would hide the composer and its Send button. The cost is a page relayout when the panel opens or shrinks to the peek.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"6636a353ec41619e81cfd8736d4c0f364ea40ff422c31c969c4b6c8585891b3a"},"summary":"Narrow-screen panel laid over the lower 45% of the page","tags":["revisit:the shell's composer stops docking at the WebView's bottom, or the relayout on panel open proves janky on a device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.097050Z","id":"1aec3afc02b7529e673fa0e94fa45287e99cdc1f4bc64b01bf06fc11b205332e","body":{"detail":"The timing starts at the pick only when no sent change is waiting for its version (_armed). A second comment picked and sent before the first change lands is measured from the first pick, and the first landed frame stops the timing for both. Timings keys intervals by name only (lib/agent/timings.dart), so overlapping changes cannot be timed separately without a keyed interval.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"d8043da203ecc354cd70c0b1a492200ae872c2ff66e1d45c0e8352f463458b27"},"summary":"A second pick while a change is in flight does not restart the long-press-landed timing","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.097077Z","id":"1ee688df3a5b126d6b15fab47a78837d45e08c5943d36b8f7789b2153056221e","body":{"detail":"Spec section 7 asks for a reload when the WebView process goes away. WKWebView's web content process ending arrives as a main-frame WebResourceError (webview_flutter_wkwebview), which this handles; webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 exposes no render-process-gone callback through NavigationDelegate, and Android's default for an unhandled renderer crash kills the app process.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"75d5781179f9d7c4cf7459b4a4191a6edb316c95d1d8ddb905b594de58ada132"},"suggested_fix":"Handle onRenderProcessGone through webview_flutter_android's platform controller (AndroidWebViewController) if a later version exposes it, or in the app's Kotlin MainActivity.","summary":"An Android WebView renderer crash is not handled","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:38.097100Z","id":"608e2cd4893cb93d2beba61b372be38a73a3c0b6f92957a11fd0699406aea752","body":{"detail":"A top-level navigation to an off-device web or mail link is refused and handed to WebViewAppSurface.openExternal. The app has no url_launcher dependency, so nothing opens it yet; F9 must wire openExternal (for example through the MethodChannel dev.empathic.clax/native in android/app/src/main/kotlin/dev/empathic/clax_app/MainActivity.kt and NSWorkspace on macOS).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"8c6bdad417c705cea75786368daa1eacf5454512f0fa06f79317ff3e18a6fad3"},"summary":"Links out of the app go nowhere until F9 passes openExternal","tags":["needs-f9","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.531800Z","id":"169065af2eb9b1fac75846c661bcb7444ad8963778fb0bd601a8c4720bf0eb37","body":{"detail":"Failure: an artifact with a second page (index.html links to about.html). The frame navigates; the shell greets and setUrl()s the top level to /a/<id>/about.html?app=1 (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1114, shellPath in web/shell/src/route.ts:38). onUrlChange -> ShellSession.urlChanged: isShellUrl is false because _shellPath is ^/a/[^/]+(/v/[1-9][0-9]*)?$, so _shell and _nonce are cleared: every later HostMessage is dropped and every HostCall is skipped (canCall false) -- no comment mode, Send, landed or threads until a full reload, and urlChanged never turns the session back on even when history returns to the index URL. A reload (Reload button, fault retry, F9's resume reload) at that URL is refused by WebViewAppSurface.decide and, if it loads anyway, documentLoaded gives it no nonce, so the page stays covered. Also refused: /a/<id>/v/<n>/<file>?app=1 and /a/<id>/?app=1. Probe run in this worktree: isShellUrl(base, /a/abcdefghjkmn/about.html?app=1) = false, decide = prevent; ShellSession canCall true -> false after urlChanged to that URL. The committed shell installs its host for /a/<id>[/v/<n>][/<file>] with app=1 (web/shell/src/app/host.ts header and installHost via parseShellPath); the app's rule must accept the same shape (parse like parseShellPath: the ID segment, optional v/<digits>, any file segments) and urlChanged should keep the nonce for a same-document URL change that stays a shell URL. Tests in test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart and webview_surface_test.dart cover only the index URL.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":372},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"6535d07181f9b823caf4f358177a53a82bb8170caaf1c42fbe3f05207e1432ed"},"summary":"The shell-URL rule refuses the shell's own page URLs (/a/<id>/<file>), so the channel dies when the app shows any page but index.html","tags":["review","f8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.532012Z","id":"ada45b5fa32006f5e6a52391eb3477b7e86477db16ef1ff255e25fa2309eb0e2","body":{"detail":"(1) A WorkerFailed/WorkerReplied that arrives before the shell's `sent` (the worker's long poll wakes on the send and a refused key fails at once, while `sent` waits for sendToAgent's HTTP response and the JS channel) is overwritten by Sent -> Working, which nothing ends; the chip offers no Dismiss while working (dismissable = _chip != working, line 630). (2) WorkerLanded on an unpinned view relies on the shell's `landed`, which host.ts posts only when its auto-follow loads the version (landing set in follow()); if the WebView reloaded mid-change (fault retry at webview_surface.dart:134, or Reload) the fresh shell opens the new latest directly and never posts `landed`, so Working stays. Clearing on WorkerLanded when _ready.version >= version would close this. (3) A Restore's ReloadLatest (line 336) yields a `landed` that clears the Working chip and stops the long-press-landed timing of an unrelated change in flight, recording the restore's version. Keying the chip and timing by the thread IDs WorkerWorking carries (lib/agent/worker.dart:18) and the Sent thread would make each path end its own chip once. No test in test/ui/app_screen_test.dart covers these orders.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":277},"content_hash":"d2e0b18709ca216f1fc724e8612e5f195326df7a91ba5962c0038eb576f4a00c"},"summary":"The Working chip is one flag for every change, so some orders of events leave it stuck on Working (which cannot be dismissed) or end another change's chip and timing","tags":["review","f8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.532065Z","id":"f306ec4603277ddcd75c9962d4b0bb7ab5a94ccecff02a411eb68bede94b5a86","body":{"detail":"A pick opens the panel (_open = true) and the shell sets commenting false with resumeAfter = pickId (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1189-1190). Closing the panel (swipe right, back, Escape, Cmd-K) calls ExitCommentMode, a no-op because commenting is already false, and leaves the draft open; when that draft later closes the shell turns comment mode on again (draftChanged, artifact-controller.ts:507-512) with the panel closed, so the next tap on the page picks instead of acting. Reopening the panel while the draft is still open calls EnterCommentMode unconditionally, and the shell's toggleComment turns commenting on mid-draft (artifact-controller.ts:1381), so a tap on the page starts a new pick over the draft. The Ready handler guards with `_draft == null` (line 180) but _setOpen does not. Either cancel or keep the draft explicitly on close, skip EnterCommentMode while _draft != null, and send ExitCommentMode when a StateMsg reports commenting with the panel closed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":301},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"c7f6569bd505732b954714a73f8d4fee9bd4daa37c052dcd88b26be849f89aec"},"summary":"Closing the panel with a composer open, then reopening it, turns comment mode back on mid-draft; closing it leaves the shell's resume-after-pick armed","tags":["review","f8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.532113Z","id":"df013f912ea4d6123b93c641b2e141db14a70a6a26843c3bc6e7a93988d3efd9","body":{"detail":"The peek shows `On \"${d.label}\"`, and the label is the shell's composerQuote (web/shell/src/app/host.ts postState), which falls back to anchor.selector when the pick has no quote (web/shell/src/view/composer-model.ts:45). Render target/f8-render/peek_light.png from tool/app_screen_render_test.dart shows `On \"div.run\"` for a tapped run card. In the app the label should describe the element as a person would: a quote of its text (prefer anchor.quote, cut short), else a short element description (\"the Mon run card\", \"an image\", \"a button\") derived from the anchor's quote/tag/role -- never a selector. The anchor carries no tag or role today (kind, selector, quote, rect, custom_name), so a fix needs the shell to send a human label in the state message (or the bridge to add a description to the anchor), and the Flutter peek to drop the wrapping quotes when the label is not a quote.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"07debf2c0f5bdf5188c160d8764ccca9922ccafbd23902f918754e6501ae644c"},"summary":"The composer peek names the picked element by its CSS selector (On \"div.run\"), not in human terms","tags":["review","f8","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.532152Z","id":"bac748e19f4f436f5845c731be1d8ae7e88630885b19a8026761b745539fe1e0","body":{"detail":"Each row shows the first comment, the version, the comment count and the send status (render target/f8-render/threads_light.png). The `threads` HostMessage carries no anchor (web/shell/src/app/host.ts, threads mapping in onState), so a person scanning the list cannot tell which part of the app a thread is about. Add a human anchor label (the same human description the composer peek needs, never a selector) to each thread in the message and show it in the row's subtitle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":278},"content_hash":"b513ae1e86e2dc210869e30a438328ac89099aa3f1adf68148510796301388db"},"summary":"Thread rows say nothing about what the thread is anchored to","tags":["review","f8","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:52:49.532193Z","id":"74cdfc55e3b1f8b58f00ca0e1cc102194bebeaeb31dcd66a782755f7854b871c","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 6.2 step 3 says `sent` starts the long-press-landed timer, and lib/agent/timings.dart:7 documents longpressLanded as \"Send in the composer to the new version's frame load\". The screen starts it when the composer opens (StateMsg picked) and only arms it on Sent, so a comment dictated for 40 s adds 40 s to the number the app defends, and the measure varies with how long the person talks rather than with the system. Either start at Sent as specified, or record pick-to-send separately and change the spec and timings.dart; the choice belongs to the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"d62dc6d113c9857e752f2092f130273cdd5007d4672d597218da22a0f854831d"},"summary":"long-press-landed starts at the pick, so it includes the person's dictation and typing time; the spec and the Timings doc start it at Send","tags":["review","f8","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.653772Z","id":"2be03e70b4eef158644bc2942d4c96cd22b74c0e9c66a3f353acac06deefd278","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: ShellSession.isShellUrl follows parseShellPath/appQuery (/a/<id>[/v/<n>][/<file>], app=1 first), urlChanged keeps the nonce inside a document, only a new document is re-nonced. Tests 'the shell URL is any app view path on the daemon origin', 'a multi-page app: moving between pages keeps the channel, a reload on a page re-nonces', 'a same-document URL change never clears the session' (host_protocol_test.dart) and 'the top level may load the shell app view' (webview_surface_test.dart). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+86: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"169065af2eb9b1fac75846c661bcb7444ad8963778fb0bd601a8c4720bf0eb37","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.654144Z","id":"53d3a1531d7b548092ac8a7e261fd63adf81edca0931bce39c9a97e6f1bfa245","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: lib/ui/change_tracker.dart keeps changes per thread. Tests in change_tracker_test.dart cover each order (failure before Send, frame before the worker's landing, reload mid-change, a Restore's frame, two changes, pinned view, dismiss), and app_screen_test.dart 'a failure that comes before Send still ends Working', 'a page reloaded mid-change ends Working on the newer version', \"a Restore's landing leaves another change Working and timed\", 'Working can be dismissed, and comes back with new work'. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+86: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"ada45b5fa32006f5e6a52391eb3477b7e86477db16ef1ff255e25fa2309eb0e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.654432Z","id":"a14d6268c1cc5c2c858721f6bd3947709d0d5857380bfe0972ab5a813c8f5584","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: _setOpen sends no comment-mode call while a draft is open (the draft stays), and a StateMsg reporting commenting with the panel closed and no draft gets ExitCommentMode. Tests 'reopening the panel mid-draft leaves comment mode to the shell' and 'a composer closed while the panel is closed leaves comment mode off' (app_screen_test.dart). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+86: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"f306ec4603277ddcd75c9962d4b0bb7ab5a94ccecff02a411eb68bede94b5a86","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.654714Z","id":"0d1374036ae52d1b7b72512c7bd909a94829afa84fa2d5d1ea10c76c48dc6765","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 as the spec binds: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 6.2 step 3 (`sent` starts the long-press-landed timer) and lib/agent/timings.dart:7. ChangeTracker.sent starts it; a pick does not ('a pick shrinks the panel to a peek and dictates into the draft; the timing waits for Send', 'Send, working, the worker lands, then the frame: timed from Send'). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+86: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"74cdfc55e3b1f8b58f00ca0e1cc102194bebeaeb31dcd66a782755f7854b871c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.654991Z","id":"a2154a845b2a4d53f52e60fd52cb150daa6f3e542dd12bfc7fc0b41d410108ad","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Obsolete after f1c07f346b12: the timing starts at Send and ChangeTracker times one change at a time, so a later Send while one is timed is untimed and each record is one change's ('only one change is timed at a time; each record is its own', change_tracker_test.dart). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+86: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"1aec3afc02b7529e673fa0e94fa45287e99cdc1f4bc64b01bf06fc11b205332e","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.655260Z","id":"363ced4fc5b4efe6c6e26398e0a4386937bba8dc95aee530977a29e5c6e4f63b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"df013f912ea4d6123b93c641b2e141db14a70a6a26843c3bc6e7a93988d3efd9","summary":"Flutter side ready in f1c07f346b12: the peek shows the draft's `label` as is, without quotes, and 'New comment' when empty. Still open: the shell's composerQuote falls back to the selector (web/shell/src/view/composer-model.ts:45); the shell (web/shell/src/app/host.ts postState) must send a human description as `label`.","tags":["depends-on-shell","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:59:45.655285Z","id":"05e690b39e55683af36029e66f2736f49b607ca4d1b2656d879bf71ba80600fd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bac748e19f4f436f5845c731be1d8ae7e88630885b19a8026761b745539fe1e0","summary":"Flutter side ready in f1c07f346b12: ThreadSummary reads an optional `label` from the threads message and shows it first in the row's subtitle (test 'the Threads tab lists the shell threads and opens one'). Still open: web/shell/src/app/host.ts must add a human anchor `label` to each thread in the `threads` message.","tags":["depends-on-shell","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:01:06.310448Z","id":"6c8fcd338f49cea703cf16d08b7e25f0eb8c04315f0e77e5d325006f150ad326","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed on the shell side: state draft.label is web/shell/src/app/label.ts anchorLabel (quote, else the element's role/tag/name from the bridge's pick desc, else 'this spot'), never a selector; the shell's own composer shows the same words in app mode. Tests: label.test.ts 'is never a selector', host.test.ts 'labels a draft from the pick's element description...' (no 'div.run' in any host message), e2e app-mode 'a long-press picks and Send...' (label “Quarterly goals”); the Flutter peek renders label as given","supersedes":"df013f912ea4d6123b93c641b2e141db14a70a6a26843c3bc6e7a93988d3efd9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:01:06.359450Z","id":"2b9ed8132d2549af563ebdb0d065c9e8e706d9b26a7947b912adc937921378b7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed on the shell side: each thread in the threads host message carries label (anchorLabel; 'Whole app' for an artifact anchor). Tests: host.test.ts 'labels a draft ... and a thread on the whole app', e2e app-mode checks the sent thread's label “Quarterly goals”","supersedes":"bac748e19f4f436f5845c731be1d8ae7e88630885b19a8026761b745539fe1e0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:59.768136Z","id":"e53ed6641f6a6c9a9c8569134be2220c27c11f2d82a2ae009761dd62c93a483a","body":{"detail":"sent() returns early when the thread is already in _changes, and workerWorking() adds it with timed: false. The worker's long poll wakes on the send and emits WorkerWorking in-process right after pollFeedback returns (lib/agent/worker.dart _poll -> _enqueue -> _runChange), while `sent` waits for sendToAgent's HTTP response, the shell's JS and the JavaScript channel, so WorkerWorking can come first. Probe run in this worktree: shown(3), workerWorking(['t1']), sent('t1'), workerLanded(4), frame(4) -> Timings log [] (no start, no stop). change_tracker_test.dart covers failure-before-sent but not working-before-sent for a change that lands. Fix: in sent(), when the thread is already tracked, untimed, not finished, and no other change is timed, mark it timed and start the timing (a few milliseconds late beats no record).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"74049e600f712095bf11d4336e0cef136d5b333c6e9b99c85c96667ed65d19ca"},"summary":"A change whose worker start arrives before the shell's `sent` is never timed, so long-press-landed goes unrecorded in a likely order","tags":["review","f8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:59.768221Z","id":"7d1d4b0d04fcbfe360ae1c5f28a1117c93aba2bf0e7794488b6a8e05b7285849","body":{"detail":"frame() treats any newer version not in _restored as the running change's landing and stops its timing (the chip correctly stays until workerLanded). _restore (app_screen.dart) calls restored() only after restoreVersion's response, but the shell may auto-follow the restored version from its own event stream first; and a version published by another client (an MCP agent, a browser) is never in _restored. Only the timing record is wrong (early stop, wrong version); consider crediting a frame to the running change only once the worker has landed it, and using the reload-mid-change rule only for a ready (new document), not for `landed`.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"447aa8a919bd161cf1464fc8d411ddb25b4c873cf86086a1dc7b6ba92cbc5933"},"summary":"A newer frame the worker did not report is credited to the running change, so a restore whose frame beats its HTTP response, or a version published by anything else, ends that change's timing early","tags":["review","f8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:02:59.768295Z","id":"8d423cf3df5e15639b187b767a7c6ff718da31615ae31edc28e51e22bd480e69","body":{"detail":"macOS/iOS: webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0 reports webViewWebContentProcessDidTerminate as a main-frame WebResourceError with code 2 (webkit_webview_controller.dart:1177-1190), so _onError covers and reloads it once. Android: webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 exposes no onRenderProcessGone hook (no match for RenderProcessGone in the package). Its WebViewClient keeps the default, which returns false, and Android then kills the app's whole process. So a renderer crash takes down the app, it does not leave it blank. Handling it means native code: a plugin fork, or a WebViewClient subclass in the app that delegates to the plugin's client, then disposing and recreating the WebView. It cannot be added through the Dart API.","kind":"comment","references":"1ee688df3a5b126d6b15fab47a78837d45e08c5943d36b8f7789b2153056221e","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"75d5781179f9d7c4cf7459b4a4191a6edb316c95d1d8ddb905b594de58ada132"},"summary":"Checked against the locked plugins: macOS is covered, Android needs native code","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:48.113320Z","id":"b7dbd7eeb071ce84bef81b921a6ea91770566af94cf4ef934341f5cf8a2fe2d7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: ChangeTracker.sent times a tracked, untimed, unfinished change when nothing else is timed. Tests 'the worker starting before the shell reports Send is still timed' (working, sent, landed, frame -> start, stop v4), 'Send then the worker start, landing then frame, is timed once', 'a late Send is not timed while another change is' (change_tracker_test.dart). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+90: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"e53ed6641f6a6c9a9c8569134be2220c27c11f2d82a2ae009761dd62c93a483a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:48.113731Z","id":"5033a9622af8a5662e5dd45d2fa826e78ff52d9bfa0b0b85395b7e72e231e121","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: frame() only advances the shown version; a change lands (and its timing stops) only once the worker reported its version and a frame shows it. Tests 'a frame before the worker reports its version waits for the report', \"another client's version does not end the running change's timing\", \"a Restore's frame does not end another change or its timing\" (frame before any restore response) in change_tracker_test.dart. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/swipe_test.dart test/platform/timings_test.dart -> \"+90: All tests passed!\"","supersedes":"7d1d4b0d04fcbfe360ae1c5f28a1117c93aba2bf0e7794488b6a8e05b7285849","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808084Z","id":"163bfc38119096d2e866292a7667a0abbca94d066c5e58b6e904e72e93544410","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppRoot._make (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) runs each new app through its own AgentLoop with backend () => StagedBackend(backend, stage) and passes the making screen's cancelled to newApp. Tests 'New runs the agent with its stages, then opens the app screen for the new ID; say-usable runs from Make to its first ready' (shows 'Writing your app' while the backend is held) and 'Cancel stops the run and nothing is made' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart pass. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"64af9a54ec99b1d704e11407e78de22ef5c984351fe775cb151d0933cb965350","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808495Z","id":"bf96747c822f9c9889011ac247de4b49653e75b162cee6a4ebd96f2ddd9a8cdf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppRoot._make starts sayUsable before AgentLoop.newApp; AppRoot._onReady stops it on the made app's first ready (with artifact, model and backend in extra) and ignores later readies. Test 'New runs the agent with its stages, then opens the app screen for the new ID; say-usable runs from Make to its first ready' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"fdb9b26782663b9fa19f2d5b0be6ff925455111c36edbbbb91062a8eba1524ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.809474Z","id":"515297b06c3590a0456c39bac3b48b5f8dd06481529fa2189df39dbf38a5bcaf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"platformServices passes ExternalLinks.open (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/external_links.dart) as openExternal: http, https and mailto URLs go to the openExternal method of dev.empathic.clax/native, answered by an ACTION_VIEW intent in MainActivity.kt and NSWorkspace.shared.open in MainFlutterWindow.swift. apps/clax_app/test/platform/external_links_test.dart passes (3 tests); flutter build apk --debug and flutter build macos --debug build the native code. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"608e2cd4893cb93d2beba61b372be38a73a3c0b6f92957a11fd0699406aea752","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.809789Z","id":"9fc86c93497108c6282f8bd135a63aca5c56e81445b00052b8356789bc1a2922","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppRoot installs the one ClaxMenuBar (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart) above MaterialApp on macOS; AppScreen registers its panel toggle with the app's CommentsCommand and installs its own bar only when given none. Test 'on macOS the app owns the menu bar; App > Comments works only with an app open' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart (disabled on the launcher, toggles the panel with an app open, disabled again after leaving) and the app screen's own Cmd-K test pass. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"f7450944998a14d6174355abac90aafd80fe04fccd8b184f9031a0db9a2f6df2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:04:56.245779Z","id":"7cbb2ab1609c8c479b74cf1b091f5a62ad27a9c86a0f1080423ff00774bd56d6","body":{"detail":"Observed in apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart with NSEvent clicks handed to the WKWebView (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift test input): attestPointer down before the click lets the shell take the pick (CSS pixel conversion correct at devicePixelRatio 2). With attestPointer up sent by runJavaScript right after the click, the page saw navigator.userActivation.isActive true in mousedown and false from pointerup on, and the shell answered clax:pick-refused; without it, isActive stayed true and the pick was taken. WebKit queues the mouseup behind the mousedown's acknowledgement, so the script runs between them. Whether the Flutter Listener over the platform view receives real macOS mouse events (so _attest runs mid-click) is not verified; if it does, clicks on macOS may be refused. Android (Chromium) is unaffected by this observation.","kind":"comment","references":"86741946a5822ff25f5c663de4f4cd2c8da49498616a5114f2d54d3e54c9634c","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"dd6b2a451e451c6eeef1114ff1acb4ff264e489d765a40481665096662b8ac7f"},"summary":"On macOS WKWebView a press attestation counts (the pick is taken); a release attestation run between WebKit's mousedown and mouseup clears the shell's user activation and the pick is refused","tags":["macos","webkit","f10","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:14:00.151560Z","id":"d128991bc04b0a21bf3f525cb51addbaeca070c2b920065afec004753acdd910","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7cbb2ab1609c8c479b74cf1b091f5a62ad27a9c86a0f1080423ff00774bd56d6","summary":"Checked: on macOS the app screen's Listener receives no pointer down or up for a mouse click over the WKWebView, so _attest (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:403-415) never runs during a real desktop click and this refusal cannot happen there. AppKit hands mouseDown/mouseUp to the hit view, which is WebKit's view inside FlutterMutatorView; only FlutterViewController's mouseDown:/mouseUp: (engine shell/platform/darwin/macos/framework/Source/FlutterViewController.mm, the FlutterView responder) send down/up to the engine, and its NSTrackingArea delivers only moves and enter/exit. Probe (debug Runner, Flutter 3 engine at the installed SDK): NSEvent down/up handed to the WebKit view under a Listener-wrapped WebViewWidget reached the page (pointerdown/mousedown/pointerup/mouseup/click, isTrusted true, userActivation active throughout) while PlatformDispatcher.onPointerDataPacket received no packet; the same events at a point over the FlutterView produced add/down/up packets. A real click's pick therefore depends on the shell counting the pointer's mouseover in the frame (record c0375dfc), not on attestation.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:14:05.575773Z","id":"b20638338d6632e36d6fe8ad2d8f1a6861c503edb7d1a5e52193235cc10bd9a2","body":{"detail":"Attestation exists for a finger's long-press (Android). Today a mouse click over the WKWebView never reaches this Listener on macOS (reply d128991b), but an attestation of a mouse up sent by runJavaScript between WebKit's mousedown and mouseup clears the shell's user activation and the pick is refused (7cbb2ab1). Returning early when e.kind == PointerDeviceKind.mouse keeps that from surfacing if the engine ever routes platform-view mouse events to the framework, and keeps tests that drive the Listener with tester gestures (kind touch) unchanged.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"5d9c867d152c668d138df3684aac52c290421da6ae5dfb65eff976cd5e0b9c3a"},"summary":"Attest only touch and stylus pointers, not mouse","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:18:57.723450Z","id":"0d0decb3f052ac04bb5445e032107eb421f79fc411c929ca7f4218362a3918c7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: _attest returns for PointerDeviceKind.mouse. test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'a mouse on the page is not attested; a stylus is' failed before (Expected: empty, Actual: two AttestPointer) and passes after; flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart: +35 all passed.","supersedes":"b20638338d6632e36d6fe8ad2d8f1a6861c503edb7d1a5e52193235cc10bd9a2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:56:47.117297Z","id":"c800cf6bf4413cd1f07fd60a1346b1ac4cca7c41c3129f50d9a84a5b4bd3a95a","body":{"detail":"Failure: the app is paused or covered when the shell document finishes loading (documentLoaded builds Init with visible: false baked into its script, and canCall turns true at once), then resumes before the lazy host chunk has installed window.claxHost. visibilityChanged(true) returns SetVisible(true), whose script 'window.claxHost?.setVisible(true)' does nothing while claxHost is undefined; Init's poll then finds claxHost and calls init and setVisible(false). The shell counts itself hidden while the app shows it, releases the artifact's topics after HIDDEN_MS (web/shell/src/stream.ts), and no change lands until the next lifecycle or route change: the live-run failure of record 4ae44372 again. The reverse order leaves the shell visible while the app is paused. On Android a quick app switch during the first load is enough. No test covers a change between documentLoaded and the shell's init.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"32a9133144984ebed5c757859f6ece39954fb906e1a68077422da2c8b1ff6139"},"suggested_fix":"Make the latest value win at apply time: SetVisible's script stores the value in a global of the shell's main frame when claxHost is not there yet (e.g. window.__claxAppVisible = v), and Init's script passes that global (falling back to its baked value) to setVisible; or have SetVisible wait for claxHost as Init does, with a sequence number so only the latest applies. Add a host_protocol_test for a change between documentLoaded and init.","summary":"A visibility change while the shell's host module is still loading is lost, and Init then applies the stale value","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:00:15.095850Z","id":"32638a5f56c65ac91fe3c45f8f3172d762ecbd9c94fdd9e4ff0d5f562e8a3a52","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: Init and SetVisible keep the latest visibility in a page global (window.__claxHostVisible) and Init applies it right after init, so a change made before the shell's host exists is kept and only the latest applies. The JavaScript itself is run in node with a fake window and timers (host_protocol_test.dart group 'visibility in the page': a change while the host loads, resumed to paused and paused to resumed; only the latest of several changes; host present). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test -> '+426 ~3: All tests passed!'; the two window tests failed before the fix.","supersedes":"c800cf6bf4413cd1f07fd60a1346b1ac4cca7c41c3129f50d9a84a5b4bd3a95a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:34:02.000730Z","id":"906678312b290c4822b840b60ff37456454bb4ab9318b3ece0497e6478accaae","body":{"detail":"VersionsTab opens a VersionPage only when given a client (versions_tab.dart:25-26). apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:763-771 builds VersionsTab without `api:`; app_screen.dart is owned in turn by tasks U3, U4 and U2 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md, so the one-line wiring is left to the first of them. Until then the version page is reachable only in tests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"1f446bc45b44c42c5f5e4cf41fe69ae091671f5b0350b5a6fa5f2667d9c2dc54"},"suggested_fix":"Add `api: widget.api,` to the VersionsTab(...) call in app_screen.dart.","summary":"The app screen does not pass `api` to VersionsTab yet, so in the app a Versions row still previews instead of opening the version page","tags":["follow-up","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/line_diff.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:34:02.000803Z","id":"8dc7aade4dd1db45a55829165c4ba2ac980281506c4c473ed973f0ef55b7b779","body":{"detail":"The kept Myers trace grows with the square of the edit distance; the bound keeps it near 1M ints (4 MB). A file rewritten beyond that (after the common prefix and suffix) shows every middle line as removed and added. Files above 4,000 lines or 256 KiB never reach lineDiff (version_page.dart diffMaxLines/diffMaxBytes). The diff also runs on the UI isolate when the version page loads, once per changed text file; at these bounds it is tens of milliseconds per file.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"da48a169635acb003ab1f9894ef635f5fa65d6ac31ea97074afd2ad04b9528bd"},"summary":"Past 1,000 edits the middle of a diff is shown as removed then added whole: exact but not shortest","tags":["revisit:a version page visibly stalls on load, or people ask for shortest diffs of rewritten files","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:34:02.000859Z","id":"d512d8f31c039794a24071619e4a86bd0dc0e7862d3b8eeea7b1d10ffe167c95","body":{"detail":"_load reuses _detail after the first read, so a version that lands while the page is open is not the 'current' a later toggle compares against, and the page still offers Restore on what has become an older latest. Retry after a failed first read does fetch again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"b8c0e78988ff1207e8593be2ffd7cb3a5ab5a5c0621bc71a23a0ed6fce2926a4"},"suggested_fix":"Re-read getArtifact when Compare with current is toggled on, or listen to version events.","summary":"The version page reads the artifact once; Compare with current keeps the latest it saw when it opened","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:47.861602Z","id":"cd3642c5f8661c1601590b8ee67d2ba1d6fad71d6d8c8d3c84d3f702bef0e92a","body":{"detail":"_load calls readFiles for both versions (version_page.dart:194-199), and HttpClaxApi.readFiles (lib/clax/http_api.dart:93-109) fetches the full body of every text file, including files whose sha256 is unchanged and files over diffMaxBytes that will only show sizes. compareFiles (version_page.dart:59-118) then UTF-8-encodes each text and runs lineDiff on every changed file synchronously inside setState. Measured in flutter test (JIT, desktop): one 4,000-line pair with 1,000 edits takes 4-10 ms; 20 such files take 78-136 ms, several frames on a phone. Typical artifacts (a few small files) are unaffected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"4811169fb67d232b99f95d238665d2659cc8e371b76d58b6beaefc125f9cf2f2"},"suggested_fix":"List changes from FileMeta first (sha256, then size), fetch bodies only for changed text files at or under diffMaxBytes, and diff a file when its row is tapped (or run compareFiles through compute() when the total line count is large).","summary":"The version page downloads every text file of both versions and diffs every changed file on the UI isolate before it shows anything","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:47.861690Z","id":"a868b02a52b0321ca95cd9b106c8a6c7701839befe1a9cdb1e4c2a48e59362e8","body":{"detail":"ListView(children: _lines(...)) constructs every row before the first frame. Past line_diff.dart's 1,000-edit bound a rewrite renders as all-removed then all-added, so a 4,000-line file opens as one 8,000-row hunk. Measured in flutter test: opening a 60-to-1,200-line rewrite (1,260 rows) took 72-80 ms to settle.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":543},"end":{"line":548},"content_hash":"32003ab9e417fd15dd9d966b5a793ddd0e1267eecae12b5b7acf23ad2d59dfea"},"suggested_fix":"Flatten hunks and folds into a row list and render with ListView.builder (itemCount, itemBuilder), so only visible rows are built.","summary":"FileDiffPage builds a widget for every diff line up front; a rewritten 4,000-line file is 8,000 rows","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:47.861737Z","id":"90bbbf851aa40d9cc6e7a9921f3cc59fb98854c7832febc7f99aca3c621bb878","body":{"detail":"compareFiles marks a file changed when the raw texts differ (version_page.dart:78-79), but splitLines (line_diff.dart:43-50) drops a trailing \\r and the final newline, so 'a\\r\\nb' vs 'a\\nb' or 'a\\nb' vs 'a\\nb\\n' give no hunks: the row shows '+0 -0' and FileDiffPage shows only an 'N unchanged lines' fold.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":78},"end":{"line":102},"content_hash":"a487b06877a2de9bebf281a32525360c9ea590966b52833cb838b2df3dc705ba"},"suggested_fix":"When the texts differ but lineDiff returns no hunks, say so ('Only line endings or the final newline changed') in the row and on the diff page.","summary":"A file whose only change is line endings or the final newline is listed as Changed +0 -0 and opens an empty diff","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:47.861773Z","id":"567ca5ed611ac25718ba0d04c9898c78efe66bea76dea229050979b62c00b89a","body":{"detail":"_FileRow and FileDiffPage's app bar (version_page.dart:535-539) use TextOverflow.ellipsis on the whole path, so 'src/components/very/deeply/nested/.../with-a-long-file-name.component.tsx' shows as 'src/components/very/deeply/…' at phone width (rendered to target/n3-review/v2_light.png).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":460},"end":{"line":464},"content_hash":"1d2aef4fffca55ecddbc0e3a30d0c4dd28c754f38104f6b4bec9ead0f126aecf"},"suggested_fix":"Show the base name as the title and the directory as a dimmer second line, or ellipsize the start of the path.","summary":"A long path is cut at its end, hiding the file name","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:45:15.329561Z","id":"4ba99ad32f4675562e849a74dfd869649dc1350491ec32ad5fcfeb17595f4e07","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: changes are listed from FileMeta (sha256, then size); texts are read only for same-size files without hashes, and for a file when opened, once per version; diffs over 1,000 lines run through compute(). Test: reads no file until one is tapped when the metadata settles. flutter test test/ui/version_page_test.dart: 14/14 pass (scratch copy with HEAD lib/clax)","supersedes":"cd3642c5f8661c1601590b8ee67d2ba1d6fad71d6d8c8d3c84d3f702bef0e92a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:45:15.330153Z","id":"f52b9a88e8953c52a91b6c35fe8676f958b39a10b4f31d84c34628ee15f8efa9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: FileDiffPage flattens hunks and folds into rows rendered by ListView.builder. flutter test test/ui/version_page_test.dart: 14/14 pass (scratch copy with HEAD lib/clax)","supersedes":"a868b02a52b0321ca95cd9b106c8a6c7701839befe1a9cdb1e4c2a48e59362e8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:45:15.330621Z","id":"f7a61785adc51c945e3c86e4839aa23eec0639abe0bb3e58762638ce8acd3bd9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a diff with no hunks between differing texts shows \"Only line endings or the final newline changed.\" Test: a change of line endings or final newline only says so. flutter test test/ui/version_page_test.dart: 14/14 pass (scratch copy with HEAD lib/clax)","supersedes":"90bbbf851aa40d9cc6e7a9921f3cc59fb98854c7832febc7f99aca3c621bb878","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:45:15.331077Z","id":"e0efc68d85a045b6200f41cf20b348ac4f1d96f1f798ca320b2edd35c681bc96","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: rows and the diff app bar show the file name (up to two lines) over its directory. Test: a long path shows its file name over its directory; render target/n3-render/page_light.png. flutter test test/ui/version_page_test.dart: 14/14 pass (scratch copy with HEAD lib/clax)","supersedes":"567ca5ed611ac25718ba0d04c9898c78efe66bea76dea229050979b62c00b89a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:45:15.331523Z","id":"bf184f43739b8dc76b52a9c5721a11971df4dc47d4be93c5a4f57b7620dc6380","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: every load, including the Compare with current toggle, re-reads getArtifact. flutter test test/ui/version_page_test.dart: 14/14 pass (scratch copy with HEAD lib/clax)","supersedes":"d512d8f31c039794a24071619e4a86bd0dc0e7862d3b8eeea7b1d10ffe167c95","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:50.091373Z","id":"a613a874c917baeb40f6052f656a75e074baa3943c0889ac8c81a363c08b0859","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts attestPointer accepts phase 'cancel' (since 647958f22844): it ends the pointer's press and attests nothing. Without it, a cancelled touch (a system gesture, the app paused mid-touch) stays an attested held press in the shell until HELD_MAX_MS (30 s) after its press, so hostArrival.pending() stays true and a refused pick start waits PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS meanwhile, and the held press counts as the frame's arrival for that time (bounded by the shell's 5 s transient activation).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":528},"end":{"line":537},"content_hash":"2a8a2ad31e7852701a831a22a8d8c851fa3e767c79a10b83f2e08d78f729094e"},"suggested_fix":"Add onPointerCancel to the Listener, calling claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase: 'cancel', x, y}) as onPointerUp does; test it with the fake surface in test/ui/app_screen_test.dart.","summary":"The app attests a finger's down and up to claxHost but not an OS-cancelled touch: attest onPointerCancel as phase 'cancel'","tags":["owner:U3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:20:54.266120Z","id":"9221bb779242ab1d90f622b38202c2f1268c75ef0f2e285d990efb7820a20f97","body":{"detail":"lib/app.dart builds Launcher without either hook, so _openItem (launcher.dart:144) falls back to widget.open(aid). Wiring onOpenTarget to the app screen's openThread/loadVersion belongs in lib/app.dart (Task U6 in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md), and onOpenQuestion to QuestionWebSheet on /inbox?q=<qid> (Task N2).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"897aff2351bf0a04f370e7dbec192e982873865479a10dc16dee4fae83981eba"},"summary":"Launcher.onOpenTarget and onOpenQuestion are not passed by lib/app.dart yet: an inbox item opens only its app (Launcher.open), not the reply's thread or the version, and a question opens its app rather than the question sheet","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:20:54.266208Z","id":"bb2e8625d8f1e21fd0bdb505d00839bf133aea8ad147ede45d617178900bc1a1","body":{"detail":"Each ClaxStream is one SSE connection. Once lib/app.dart holds one stream subscribed to inbox and questions for the app's life (Task U6), the launcher and InboxScreen could take events from it instead of calling ClaxApi.stream() themselves; that needs a shared fan-out (ClaxStream.events is single-subscribe per topic set today).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"b55fe4eb34318ec421a197b56538652b7bd4f4662f6b33b3d5c6b8f3512141c8"},"summary":"The launcher opens its own /api/stream for the unread badge, and InboxScreen another while open; with U6's app-lifetime stream the app holds up to three connections","tags":["revisit:U6 lands an app-lifetime ClaxStream in lib/app.dart","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:20:54.266264Z","id":"2ecff98ba13f64555d8e885cde3877e7b995fa7b5767d8fe38bb2d67898cad25","body":{"detail":"Matching a new item locally would mean reimplementing the daemon's inbox search (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs) in Dart, and a mismatch would show items the search excludes. A new matching item shows on the next refresh, pull to refresh, or query change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"4d882195078793650e23e61351dd2550453035de2483ce0df21f2aa572c5afba"},"summary":"While a search is active, live inbox_item events update rows already shown but never add new ones","tags":["revisit:the owner expects searches to update live","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:21:01.984201Z","id":"e43c349dd88f0c9de7b00218b7172982b9a575c0b53037699439e54df0363680","body":{"detail":"Each ClaxStream from ClaxApi.stream() is one SSE connection. Once lib/app.dart holds one stream subscribed to inbox and questions for the app's life (Task U6), the launcher and InboxScreen could listen to that stream's broadcast events instead of opening their own; their subscribe-then-fetch order then rests on the shared stream having subscribed first.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"b55fe4eb34318ec421a197b56538652b7bd4f4662f6b33b3d5c6b8f3512141c8"},"summary":"The launcher opens its own /api/stream for the unread badge, and InboxScreen another while open; with U6's app-lifetime stream the app holds up to three connections","supersedes":"bb2e8625d8f1e21fd0bdb505d00839bf133aea8ad147ede45d617178900bc1a1","tags":["revisit:U6 lands an app-lifetime ClaxStream in lib/app.dart","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:25:02.185575Z","id":"04321111a915ce261e79124187987d0daa088cb3a14eea8c216413b0c263b4d0","body":{"detail":"inboxLine returns replyBody.trim() and InboxRow shows it with maxLines: 2. Agents' replies are often several paragraphs (and may carry Markdown such as **bold**, shown as is). Render: a reply body 'Done.\\n\\nA reply with **markdown** and\\nnewlines…' shows only 'Done.' over an empty line at text scale 1.0, 1.3 and 2.0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":483},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"9beadb4e1f56b991ea17f86a2aaaee1e1cff73d3a708d785200bb6762d1b3fbe"},"suggested_fix":"Collapse runs of whitespace (newlines included) to one space in inboxLine for reply, version note and finished message; add a test that a body with a blank line shows its second paragraph on the row.","summary":"A reply's row shows its body's text as written, newlines included, so a reply that opens \"Done.\\n\\n…\" shows \"Done.\" and a blank second line and hides the rest","tags":["severity:minor","owner:N1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:25:02.185689Z","id":"fe014982e5a4caa2aca5ab71f34c96d4ff688095e46c874d602e2d905a154ccd","body":{"detail":"SseClaxStream (lib/clax/stream.dart:253, restoreAttempts = 6, 0.5 s doubling) drops a topic with 'unsubscribed' when its re-subscription on a new stream keeps failing for want of an answer, and removes it from the wanted set (stream.dart:319); its doc says to subscribe again to retry. The launcher lives for the app's life. InboxScreen._onEvent (inbox_screen.dart:176-177) does the same, though only for as long as the inbox is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"3b056161374abf75d7850b62abdf3e5b4cdfefccf47bb620577ae908845d9a39"},"suggested_fix":"On 'unsubscribed' for inbox, call subscribe(['inbox']) again (with a backoff, or on the next resync / app resume), then refetch; test it with FakeClaxApi's stream emitting 'unsubscribed'.","summary":"An 'unsubscribed' event refetches the unread count but never subscribes to inbox again, so after a long enough outage the badge stops being live (and the app stops counting as an owner surface) until the app restarts","tags":["severity:minor","owner:N1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:25:02.185789Z","id":"bbc9693390bddead7dfdd5e9ba84e3d92f74642e81e1f2550668ba88bebb6c73","body":{"detail":"Counted connections: launcher.dart:84 api.events (/api/events), launcher.dart:99 api.stream() (/api/stream on inbox), inbox_screen.dart:96 api.stream() while the inbox is open; U6 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md, Task U6) adds one more. HttpClient has no per-host connection cap, so none starves the others; the cost is one socket and one 15 s keep-alive per connection, and a daemon stream held 60 s after each close of the inbox. The gallery topic of /api/stream carries version and artifact_deleted (docs/contract.md, Topics), so one app-lifetime ClaxStream on gallery, inbox and questions, with a broadcast fan-out, can serve the launcher list, its badge and the inbox screen. Extends e43c349d.","kind":"concern","references":"e43c349dd88f0c9de7b00218b7172982b9a575c0b53037699439e54df0363680","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"9f467f3af74b7575dd15eefc4e50b79562cc839531dfe2ff3275693edddd091c"},"suggested_fix":"In U6, hold one ClaxStream on gallery, inbox and questions in lib/app.dart and hand it to Launcher and InboxScreen (which then do not close it); move the launcher's list refresh from /api/events to the gallery topic.","summary":"The launcher also holds GET /api/events for version and artifact_deleted, so with the inbox open the app holds three SSE connections today, and four once U6 adds its app-lifetime ClaxStream","tags":["revisit:U6 lands an app-lifetime ClaxStream in lib/app.dart","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:25:02.185851Z","id":"dc337693456929d757435458259080753ab7a28e604a063e1f32fa536c7204d7","body":{"detail":"inbox_screen_test.dart checks that subscribe precedes the fetch, and that events after the load upsert, but none holds the fetch open, emits an inbox_item (a new item, or an item read meanwhile), then completes the fetch with the older page and checks the row shows the event's state.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"36e28d0159a2e6e06244d746aca0bf30cd1a982cc45b34895b0afa81da1abce0"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test with a FakeClaxApi inbox call gated on a Completer: emit the event, complete the page, expect the event's item and read state on screen.","summary":"No test covers an inbox_item event that arrives while the first page is being fetched (the _duringLoad replay), the case subscribe-then-fetch exists for","tags":["owner:N1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:04.390121Z","id":"84f86cda80eb8da834fd12f5da9a72d67c33a13edded92565aa893dbf41839b0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"fixed: 'an item event during the first fetch is applied on its result' holds the fetch after reading the page, pushes an item, completes, and finds the row; it fails with the _duringLoad replay removed and passes with it (+59 All tests passed)","supersedes":"dc337693456929d757435458259080753ab7a28e604a063e1f32fa536c7204d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:04.391299Z","id":"2cfb455cae56fd49b626b75ccf6548d788547ecc0bbba5f0beebea51114900dc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"fixed: inboxLine collapses whitespace for every kind and plainPreview strips Markdown from replies; 'previews read as one line of plain text' and 'a reply row shows its Markdown as one line' pass in apps/clax_app/test/ui/inbox_screen_test.dart (flutter test test/ui/inbox_screen_test.dart test/ui/launcher_test.dart: +59 All tests passed)","supersedes":"04321111a915ce261e79124187987d0daa088cb3a14eea8c216413b0c263b4d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:29:04.392330Z","id":"6d64c813b25e17fb83767ea06bb7cda9f5f9ae6ff3e7c874f0ff5007942a6859","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"fixed: an unsubscribed event subscribes the topic again (resubscribe in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart, 1 s doubling to 60 s) in both the launcher and the inbox screen, then refetches; 'an unsubscribed inbox is subscribed again with backoff' (launcher_test) and 'an unsubscribed topic is subscribed again with backoff' (inbox_screen_test) pass: +59 All tests passed","supersedes":"fe014982e5a4caa2aca5ab71f34c96d4ff688095e46c874d602e2d905a154ccd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:16.962165Z","id":"f2abe3a554c4bf0a080e2eec785dc86a3e389a68782de9f054f46a12b38a93e5","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design R§9.1 keeps the button's vertical position in settings. AppScreen takes the starting height (commentButtonDy) and reports drags (onCommentButtonMoved), but AppSettings (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/settings_store.dart) has no field for it and apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart does not wire either, so each app screen starts at CommentButton.defaultDy. The left/right side is held only in the button's state.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"8b574efaa3a8c482825a0c13e9e6fab213372f4043a787a37678e7ff95a8ae1b"},"suggested_fix":"Add a comment_button_dy field to AppSettings, pass settings' value as commentButtonDy where app.dart builds AppScreen, and save it from onCommentButtonMoved.","summary":"The comment button's dragged height is not kept across app screens: nothing passes commentButtonDy or onCommentButtonMoved yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:16.962270Z","id":"cfd9e233e857857f8678d1298c6047ebe831b08ae8d46aaacfb864439c6ce8a5","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart parses {type: \"questions\", open} and renders openQuestions(); the shell side (web/shell/src/app/host.ts) did not post or install them when this was written. The app screen drops QuestionsMsg, so the comment button carries no question badge (spec R§10.2).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":318},"content_hash":"1d7861a7aa3b8a5cb8b182a15659190a43e0cbc67b2f35ec6e126b531083f513"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the open count from QuestionsMsg, badge the comment button with it, and call OpenQuestions when a new question about the shown app arrives in front.","summary":"The shell's questions count (QuestionsMsg) is parsed but not shown: no badge, and OpenQuestions is never called","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:16.962323Z","id":"0fb89b9e1f117ba102288b32dfd546a12bd4d5399b61782e6fb34714b7ccb2b9","body":{"detail":"The bar is laid out under the page instead (the WebView shrinks by its height, and it takes the bottom inset), and the floating button hides while it is up, its close standing in for a second tap. Over the page, the bar and the button would cover the page's bottom bar and lower-right corner exactly while the person is trying to hold on things there. The cost: the WebView resizes once when comment mode turns on and off.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":597},"end":{"line":626},"content_hash":"7f33007fae3f24ebafd27dcaa1cb81f7564bad8d3cd789c5754ff1300dcbb6a3"},"summary":"Comment bar laid over the page, with the floating button kept above it","tags":["revisit:a page re-lays out badly or loses its scroll position when the bar appears","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:16.962380Z","id":"edf023b93216b3d619af24c00fd0a2d68955b25f3fc14e80a15f25e8657ed846","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"onPointerCancel now attests PointerPhase.cancel (app_screen.dart:647-650); test 'an OS-cancelled touch on the page is attested as cancel' and 'AttestPointer passes an OS-cancelled touch as phase cancel' pass (flutter test test/ui: 228 passed)","supersedes":"a613a874c917baeb40f6052f656a75e074baa3943c0889ac8c81a363c08b0859","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:16.963085Z","id":"9f4ace7d649f9dc1bf9f748ec2c425c993cb1a5229e7dd4ff7aa82c6bd6b6876","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppScreen passes api: widget.api to VersionsTab (app_screen.dart:884); 'the Versions tab previews and restores versions' now opens the version page and previews from it, passing (flutter test test/ui: 228 passed)","supersedes":"906678312b290c4822b840b60ff37456454bb4ab9318b3ece0497e6478accaae","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:48:56.820665Z","id":"bcf61f7bb12d1c6583aeea71d13941ac32d8fe6bb2c4c38b2698d2fc2e4dd6ba","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a phone, tap the comment button (the CommentBar shows under the page), then press system back: PopScope's canPop is !_open, which is true while only _bar is set, so the route pops and the person is thrown out of the app they were commenting on. Back is how an Android user ends a transient mode. canPop should be !_wantComment (or !_open && !_bar), with onPopInvokedWithResult closing the bar first (then the panel), and a test in test/ui/app_screen_test.dart that back with the bar up keeps the screen and sends ExitCommentMode.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":587},"end":{"line":592},"content_hash":"60a994e98a398781260f22e9231894ee83dfcd1decf84d3ca24953b49c6e3786"},"summary":"Android back with the comment bar up leaves the app screen instead of ending comment mode","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:48:56.820762Z","id":"3eff33a2b12810976f5b215f3f83cf62d8fbdbaba6567d3dd646a79f15c7fdf7","body":{"detail":"The Escape binding calls _setOpen(false) and _toggleOpen toggles the panel; with only the bar up (_bar true, _open false) Escape does nothing and Cmd-K opens the panel instead of ending comment mode. On a wide macOS window the bar is the visible mode, so Escape should end it like the bar's close button (_setBar(false)).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":576},"end":{"line":580},"content_hash":"a1d412021e25f96514f9bd0620a3634f328bf63ac6591b2fa010cb0242399b28"},"summary":"Escape and the Comments command (Cmd-K) close only the panel, never the comment bar","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_button.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:48:56.820800Z","id":"af281deaa2ccbc013d231b4a6f8458938c4086359af53a47007c0320c05000da","body":{"detail":"The hint is Expanded and both actions are Flexible (flex 1 each), so each takes a third of the free width whether it needs it or not. Rendered at 1100x760 (target/u3-review-render/wide_bar_light_13.png) the Whole app / Threads (2) / close group ends at about 1100 of 2000 px with empty bar to its right. At 390x844 and text scale 1.3 (phone_bar_dark_13.png) the Threads label reads 'Threads (…' and the hint 'you want cha…'; at 320x640 and 1.3 (small_bar_13.png) it is 'Whole …', 'Threa…' and 'what you …'. Give the actions their intrinsic width and let only the hint flex (or drop the hint to a second line / a shorter 'Hold to comment' when narrow), and add a 1.3 text-scale case to test/ui/comment_button_test.dart that finds the full labels.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"eab9621c78dfe18080f6e6f8e71d928ebe47db6b10c4294260a955d515264c7d"},"summary":"The comment bar's Row splits its width in three equal parts: on a wide window the actions and close sit mid-bar, and at text scale 1.3 the labels truncate","tags":["review","ux","a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:48:56.820848Z","id":"c8ab5357471699050fc4e337483140c0d28a767951a844dcca6719c51181fd6a","body":{"detail":"bar is false whenever _draft != null or _open, so on a phone a long-press pick removes the 56 dp CommentBar (page grows), opens the 76 dp peek (AppPanel.peekHeight, page shrinks), and Send or Cancel reverses both. Each is a layout-viewport resize of the platform view (innerHeight changes, 100vh layouts and fixed bottom bars jump). Shrinking for the bar itself is the right call over overlaying (the page's own bottom navigation stays reachable and nothing is covered while picking), but the peek could take the bar's slot without first releasing it, so the page height changes once per pick instead of twice. Worth checking on the device for a visible jump.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":597},"end":{"line":600},"content_hash":"9dc939395b4ad2bf3ff9ea82143c20d91d64ffe79bfe2b2d0e371039cb6f618c"},"summary":"A pick from the bar resizes the WebView three times on a narrow screen: bar off, peek on, then peek off and bar back","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:54:31.811434Z","id":"53bf01d43a82d82789d89b6b65529900de5b66e43f5f79b2d78bb72a5332ac13","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"canPop is !_wantComment and a refused pop closes the top layer (_closeTop: the panel, else the bar). Tests 'back with the bar up ends comment mode and keeps the screen' and 'back closes the panel opened from the bar, then the bar' pass (flutter test test/ui: 238 passed). Back closes the panel before the bar because the panel is the layer shown over it.","supersedes":"bcf61f7bb12d1c6583aeea71d13941ac32d8fe6bb2c4c38b2698d2fc2e4dd6ba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_button.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:54:31.812209Z","id":"e7740d5bf8062e577d9a3516260b5fbc394098684a0a4c656f1ee1c3a041936b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The actions take their measured width at the bar's end and only the hint flexes; when two lines beside them would not hold the hint, it takes a line above them. 'the comment bar fits' tests at 320, 390 and 1100 dp, text scale 1.0 and 1.3, with Roboto, find no label cut and the close button at the bar's end (flutter test test/ui/comment_button_test.dart: 14 passed).","supersedes":"af281deaa2ccbc013d231b4a6f8458938c4086359af53a47007c0320c05000da","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:54:31.812855Z","id":"03ea7e9d9f9ef86d25a53ef3e77be131590fc06ab62a784aa11c9f608ffd8524","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Escape calls _closeTop, and the Comments command (Cmd-K) ends comment mode when the panel or the bar is up, else opens the panel. Test 'Escape and the Comments command end comment mode from the bar' passes (flutter test test/ui: 238 passed).","supersedes":"3eff33a2b12810976f5b215f3f83cf62d8fbdbaba6567d3dd646a79f15c7fdf7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:54:31.813510Z","id":"0c66d2120ede7bab167686b365c67b002fd4da28f01fdb55aa70987be50543f7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"CommentBar.height is AppPanel.peekHeight and both hold the bottom inset, so a pick from the bar swaps them in one frame at the same height. Test 'a pick from the bar puts the peek in its place: the page keeps its height' passes (flutter test test/ui: 238 passed).","supersedes":"c8ab5357471699050fc4e337483140c0d28a767951a844dcca6719c51181fd6a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:56:40.606493Z","id":"299abd68531da46e5a81e1a869029f276654e159ebd5aae216cbb63efc52b829","body":{"detail":"Rendered at 320x640, text scale 2.0, light and dark, with a draft labelled 'The Mon run card': 'A RenderFlex overflowed by 38 pixels on the bottom' from the Column at threads_panel.dart:182 (a 1-line label plus a 2-line status in a 76 dp peek). CommentBar.height is now AppPanel.peekHeight (comment_button.dart), so the bar and peek share the fixed height; at 1.0 and 1.3, and at 2.0 on 390 dp, both fit. Cap the status at one line when the scaled text would not fit, or let the peek grow with the text scale (and the bar with it, to keep the one-resize swap).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":181},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"99ff83a69bdd32f01e27facf1f15dcc0e80d6d73290af54ed6d892b5418a0cfc"},"summary":"The composer peek's label-and-status column overflows its fixed AppPanel.peekHeight at text scale 2.0 on a 320 dp wide screen","tags":["review","a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:58:34.157187Z","id":"797ee449689a740f1edf422aaec6aca843ec63b106b34984ef78d2eb50767b46","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844 web/shell/src/app/host.ts has claxHost.openQuestions({question?}), claxHost.closeQuestions(), and posts {type: 'questions', open, showing}. host_protocol.dart:59 parses only open, and OpenQuestions.toJs() calls openQuestions() with no ID, which shows the cards there are and never waits for one the shell has not heard yet. The app needs OpenQuestions({String? question}), a CloseQuestions call (for the back gesture while the sheet shows) and QuestionsMsg.showing before it opens the sheet for its own agent's new question.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":424},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"6084a708718522284d4f3dc8357e040b29e5c2b8a35e10eedfe0332e85fd13a9"},"summary":"The Dart host protocol still has the shell's first questions interface: OpenQuestions takes no question ID, there is no CloseQuestions, and QuestionsMsg drops showing","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:05:39.631305Z","id":"744fb01ddb4247361432c3cb0dc2abafe5f19e0f8b42613962fdb22277c7681c","body":{"detail":"R§9.7's Settings change also lists the last runs' turns and cost. The agent records (lib/agent/timings.dart, FileTimings at <support>/agent-timings.jsonl) carry no turns, tokens or cost until the AgentLoop rewrite adds them, and SettingsScreen is built in lib/app.dart with timings: _s.timings.recent(10) only. Once agent records carry those keys, SettingsScreen needs an agentTimings list and app.dart must pass _s.agentTimings.recent(10).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"0fcdccf5e1a429a54766956c22155edef644f77bbe568030bd3ea469e42d65e1"},"summary":"Settings does not yet show the last runs' turns and cost from the agent timings","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:06:17.976187Z","id":"1af44ec64a051ddd10a82aa5a74eaff29d4f9850fac2e7eaf23b63cd1b64a5b4","body":{"detail":"ThreadDetail offers Retry only when AppScreen.onRetry is non-null (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart, the failed status card). FeedbackWorker.retry(aid, tid), which re-queues a failed change's comments without posting (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§9.5), is planned in Task A7, and the Working chip's Retry in Task U2. Until lib/app.dart passes onRetry: (aid, tid) => worker.retry(aid, tid), a change that failed (a dropped connection included) shows its failure reply and reason on the thread page but no way to run it again other than replying.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"31f6d7c2c55d78f6af259c06191f37cdd62e7086fcc4548d6710c833255b11f8"},"summary":"The thread page's Retry is never shown in the running app: lib/app.dart builds AppScreen without onRetry, and FeedbackWorker has no retry(aid, tid) yet","tags":["deferred","retry","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:06:17.976282Z","id":"1e60c0f04717e348988da8d9a775285bb5697e16de30356febd176ad858c3f0a","body":{"detail":"ThreadView.stranded (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart) is the same condition: the app's worker took the change and never answered, for example after the app was killed mid-run. While the app runs, the worker reruns stranded threads at start, so 'Clax is working on it' is right then; but the thread page cannot tell a running change from one whose run died until the worker picks it up again. If stranded threads are ever left unrecovered, the page should read the worker's running threads (the change tracker's) instead of inferring from the feedback state.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"9cb27c090b97eb3bcf1088546e71c42792ee8040da861ba09cf45eb4a26ae69a"},"summary":"threadStatus reads a sent thread whose feedback is acknowledged and unanswered as working, also when no worker is running it (a stranded thread)","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:06:17.976351Z","id":"9294097deb73d958f120382fc4f51b8655943f6f1de6969dd8183176f372490e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppPanel.peekFit picks label plus two status lines, label plus one, or the status alone by the scaled line heights, and the Send button drops its label above a 22 px body size. flutter test test/ui/threads_panel_test.dart: 3 passed (1.0, 1.3, and 2.0 on 320 dp with no overflow); tool/thread_detail_render_test.dart rendered peek-320-{light,dark}-{1.0,1.3,2.0} with real Roboto without an overflow.","supersedes":"299abd68531da46e5a81e1a869029f276654e159ebd5aae216cbb63efc52b829","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:10:54.729732Z","id":"6bc7093db81ec450cbfe0afd0fb9d796831c1682d9760143a7c36a8c2a55c812","body":{"detail":"Failure: an owner who never set a display name, on the real daemon: every comment they post (from the app's reply box via postOwnerComment, or from the shell's comment bar, both owner credentials) carries author_name 'Viewer', so the thread page labels the owner's own words 'Viewer' and the 'You' fallback at lines 674-676 never fires. An owner who sets a name later gets 'Viewer' on older comments and the new name on newer ones in the same thread. Probe on a scratch daemon (target/u4-review-home, port 7613, token): two token-posted comments -> author_name 'Viewer', author_public_id u_26556f97...; PUT /api/viewers/me {display_name: Alex}; third comment -> 'Alex', same author_public_id; the first two stay 'Viewer'. docs/contract.md (\"What the person sees\") says each comment keeps the author_name it was posted with, so the daemon is behaving as specified and the display has to key on identity. Both owner paths resolve to the one owner viewer row (crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs:109-126 author(), Identity::ensure_viewer -> Store::owner_viewer), so author_public_id is stable. ThreadComment (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart:458-488) drops author_public_id. The render target/u4-render/thread-replied-light-1.0.png showing 'Alex' and 'Owner' for the same person comes from FakeClaxApi: seeded comments default author 'Alex' (fake_api.dart:123, 228) while postOwnerComment hard-codes 'Owner' with no public ID (fake_api.dart:896-913), so the tests cannot catch this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":668},"end":{"line":676},"content_hash":"95ceda3328651868e6026702e9a1c5c5e7561fe4f48541feb27b4d2efcf42deb"},"suggested_fix":"Parse author_public_id into ThreadComment (models.dart, C1's file). Read the owner's public ID once (GET /api/viewers/me with the token answers the owner row) and show every comment whose author_public_id equals it as 'You' (other viewers keep author_name). Make FakeClaxApi give seeded owner comments and postOwnerComment the same owner name and public ID, and add a test: a thread with a seeded owner comment and a postOwnerComment reply shows one name for both.","summary":"The thread page names each comment by its frozen author_name, so the owner shows as 'Viewer' (never named) or under two names (renamed mid-thread); show the owner's comments under one name by author_public_id","tags":["review","u4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:10:54.729833Z","id":"930f7c272e733db02151c864c692621e9184210714d0fe446637d9c1183caa3e","body":{"detail":"isFailureReply matches body text only. The same literal is written independently in lib/agent/loop.dart:339 and :608, lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:657 and lib/ui/change_tracker.dart:133; rewording any producer silently removes Retry. It also matches a reply from another session (an MCP agent with harness 'claude' answering the same thread) or a model-written reply that starts with the phrase, and Retry would then ask the app's FeedbackWorker.retry to re-run a change it never failed. The worker's R§9.5 rebuild of _failed from threads (Task A7) uses the same text rule, so the two must stay identical.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"3041ee0528a117da1555e58be9ad125b681a811da01cf7499b82461f57f0d675"},"suggested_fix":"For A7: one exported constant (and predicate) shared by the producers, the worker's _failed rebuild and this page; also require c.viaHarness == 'app' (the app session's harness, lib/clax/http_api.dart:165). Better still, let the page ask the worker whether it holds a failed entry for the thread (FeedbackWorker.retry's own source of truth) and offer Retry only then.","summary":"Retry keys on reply text: any agent comment opening \"Couldn't make that change:\" counts, from any harness, and the phrase is copied in five places with no shared constant","tags":["review","u4","revisit:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:10:54.729883Z","id":"05925ec0526971e91108da05d22b2e3be2075a6de48ed57a6281c87b7d65383c","body":{"detail":"_retry sets _retriedAt and calls onRetry, which returns void. If FeedbackWorker.retry has no failed entry for the thread (for example a restart before A7's rebuild, or a failure reply from another harness, see the isFailureReply record), nothing runs and the page keeps reading 'Trying again / Clax is working on it' while it stays open.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":310},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"05d8d56c006c6510d2ac9ee9cbeb364d3c3a630d2832f9ced69e06cb826e4110"},"suggested_fix":"Make onRetry return Future<bool> (queued or not) and keep the failed card with a note when it was not queued; or drive the working state from the worker's running threads rather than a local flag.","summary":"After Retry the page shows 'Trying again' until the comment count changes, even when the retry did nothing","tags":["review","u4","revisit:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:10:54.729933Z","id":"80c4a1be6ea125d9d638a5e4df8418e682d007babae93e8006fb78091a51f8ca","body":{"detail":"The comment row has no MergeSemantics, so TalkBack/VoiceOver step through author, relative time and body as separate nodes, and a failure reply is distinguished only by its error colour. The anchor title (line 448) also shows the shell's lowercase label as is ('the run card “Mon”' in target/u4-render), while _sentence (line 74) exists for this.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":685},"end":{"line":756},"content_hash":"20abf76b6694d3f907a8cfe58fd0942a3d9ff0764f5fe98f5ba97a26bc37c8bc"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap each comment in MergeSemantics (or Semantics(label: '<name>, <time>: <body>')) and add 'failed' to the agent's failure reply; pass the label through _sentence.","summary":"Each comment reads as three separate screen-reader stops (name, time, body); merge them, and say 'failed' for a failure reply","tags":["review","u4","a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:15:04.868579Z","id":"fab9ada511f17266b3bfa16f08beeddcc640782004d6286f242dfb65ef121230","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"ThreadComment parses author_public_id; ClaxApi.ownerPublicId reads GET /api/viewers/me with the token (read again after the first reply while null); every comment whose author_public_id is the owner's reads 'You'. FakeClaxApi posts seeded and owner comments with one owner name (ownerName) and public ID (u_owner). flutter test test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart test/clax/http_api_test.dart: 94 passed, including 'the owner is You under every name, other viewers by theirs' (comments posted as 'Viewer' and then 'Alexandra' both read You; Sam keeps his name) and 'ownerPublicId reads the owner from viewers/me with the token'.","supersedes":"6bc7093db81ec450cbfe0afd0fb9d796831c1682d9760143a7c36a8c2a55c812","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:15:04.869671Z","id":"8419fc7a523378aadc06540cb9f09b6f6b6f101efa8c0810c1cb4c04871f738d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"onRetry (ThreadDetail and AppScreen) returns Future<bool>; Trying again shows only when it answers true, else the failure card and Retry stay with 'There was nothing to run again. Reply to ask once more.' Test 'Retry that queued nothing keeps the failure and says so' passes (flutter test test/ui: all passed).","supersedes":"05925ec0526971e91108da05d22b2e3be2075a6de48ed57a6281c87b7d65383c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:15:04.870517Z","id":"249cb9cd19a109e9b7f1f22b28777f3ad20a478b804d6f9db9943536ca08209b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Each comment is a MergeSemantics node; a failure reply shows and reads 'failed'; the anchor title goes through _sentence. Test 'each comment reads as one node; a failure reply says failed' passes; target/u4-render/thread-*-{light,dark}-{1.0,1.3,2.0}.png show 'The run card “Mon”'.","supersedes":"80c4a1be6ea125d9d638a5e4df8418e682d007babae93e8006fb78091a51f8ca","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.807344Z","id":"fee18481123776d500202f424d7178f6bce0ec34fc01685f6a5976a707705cb3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: apps/clax_app/lib/agent/failure.dart holds failurePrefix, failureReply and isAppFailureReply (agent comment, via_harness 'app', the prefix with either apostrophe); finish.dart and loop.dart write failureReply, and the worker's failedComments and thread_detail.dart's threadStatus and bubble use isAppFailureReply. The Working chip's summary in lib/ui/change_tracker.dart is display text nothing matches. Tests: 'each state' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart (another harness's reply reads replied), 'failedComments …' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"930f7c272e733db02151c864c692621e9184210714d0fe446637d9c1183caa3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.808067Z","id":"298b54182426cc4b64e41d7feb82423e64a542cb39cd8c6f3aff1eb072c3bedc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: FeedbackWorker.retry(aid, tid) returns Future<bool> (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart) and lib/app.dart passes onRetry: _runtime.worker.retry to AppScreen. Tests: 'the app screen's Retry goes to the worker' (apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart), group 'retry' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"1af44ec64a051ddd10a82aa5a74eaff29d4f9850fac2e7eaf23b63cd1b64a5b4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.816297Z","id":"14d2ae32f6d7c68d0fd19ba684431ffcf74ad8ca507137687ddec9e7cefd78f8","body":{"detail":"ThreadView.stranded (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart) is the same condition: the app's worker took the change and never answered, for example after the app was killed mid-run. While the app runs, the worker reruns stranded threads at start, so 'Clax is working on it' is right then; but the thread page cannot tell a running change from one whose run died until the worker picks it up again. If stranded threads are ever left unrecovered, the page should read the worker's running threads (the change tracker's) instead of inferring from the feedback state.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"f31831902144f5b57d367a5eb2b5139fe537fcb39e4b02be5b93ba6bb21fb9cf"},"summary":"threadStatus reads a sent thread whose feedback is acknowledged and unanswered as working, also when no worker is running it (a stranded thread)","supersedes":"1e60c0f04717e348988da8d9a775285bb5697e16de30356febd176ad858c3f0a","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:08:55.184989Z","id":"15fafe1f351244c19bda835ec7d6bcb3a9233d21b4cb9ee87b575e911510eafe","body":{"detail":"sendFirstStep ('send-first-step', R§6.5 send→first-step) is defined in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart:9 rather than beside sayUsable and longpressLanded in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/timings.dart, and timingLabel in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:334-338 has no case for it, so Settings' recent timings list shows 'send-first-step' as the label. The record is written to the same Timings store as the defended numbers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"858f3d1ae694d0b843f4a136ea7196e2728c667b9f9bcd1c24db2589066c6e2c"},"suggested_fix":"Move the constant to lib/agent/timings.dart next to the other two names and add 'Send → first step' to timingLabel.","summary":"The send-first-step timing name lives in the UI and Settings shows it raw","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:08:55.224307Z","id":"708cf82e8842748a383d4e906cc888e0b959721e84b69f817397b4031a9d8357","body":{"detail":"_expandedView (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart:215) is a Column under a Positioned with only top set (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart, _pageStack). Three two-line steps plus the 108 px thumbnail measure about 500 logical px at text scale 2.0 (renders: target/flutter-app/u2/expanded-*-2.0.png from CLAX_RENDER_DIR=... flutter test test/ui/working_chip_test.dart --plain-name renders). On a 780 px phone in portrait it fits; on a landscape phone (about 360 px tall) its lower part runs off the page with no way to scroll to it. The collapsed chip and Dismiss stay reachable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":215},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"9a3d66fc3eda3259bc9c473daccb349f8e6172427b21acc0ce9230810de5a45c"},"suggested_fix":"Bound it to the page height (LayoutBuilder or a bottom on the Positioned) and wrap the steps in a SingleChildScrollView, or hide the thumbnail when the height is short.","summary":"The expanded Working chip has no height bound and does not scroll","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:10:55.874891Z","id":"a648cc7ed637989e9154f5d35c6f5ee48d6402285dcb762ce90b006f633918ef","body":{"detail":"MakingScreen gets the run's AgentProgress only as MakeProgress through MakeApp's report callback, and records say-first-output only on its timings parameter. AppRoot._make in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart still declares its third parameter as void Function(MakeStage) and passes newApp's onProgress events only to BackgroundRuns.step; MakingScreen is built without timings in app.dart (_offerLostMake) and in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart (_newApp). MakeApp still accepts _make as it is, so everything compiles, but the live preview, narration, the inspection screenshot and say-first-output stay dark until those three places change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":28},"content_hash":"57537c68d007f26d2bc11dddb2006d5d7d3b1d6a649d63b016d3c0ac31099998"},"suggested_fix":"In app.dart, type _make's third parameter void Function(MakeUpdate) and add stage(MakeProgress(p)) in its progress function; pass timings: _s.timings to MakingScreen in _offerLostMake, and give Launcher a timings parameter it hands to MakingScreen. Test in app_test.dart that a ScriptedRunner write_file reaches the making screen's preview.","summary":"Nothing yet sends progress or Timings to the making screen: it shows only MakeStage labels and never loads a preview","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:10:55.875013Z","id":"3bdc33348d0e37f079ec8435b6d05059a76e5e275959c9149981277dd2dd721d","body":{"detail":"On success the making screen pops Made(aid); Launcher._newApp (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart) then calls open(aid), which pushes the app screen as a new MaterialPageRoute (AppRoot._open in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart). The making route animates out over the launcher while the app route animates in, and the app screen's WebView shows its background until the page's first load. The making screen holds the last preview or screenshot, but nothing carries it across, so the page the person watched being built disappears before the real one appears.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":386},"content_hash":"39897054687ed9c047970ee9895597754fbb7ea1a821d5d75cbbc9903aad9813"},"suggested_fix":"Replace the making route with the app route (pushReplacement from the navigator that pushed MakingScreen, or a MakingScreen onMade hook that does it) and let the app screen keep an opaque cover showing the last preview frame or inspection PNG until its first ready.","summary":"The hand-over from the making screen to the new app passes through the launcher and a blank app WebView","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:10:55.875061Z","id":"c92f75e6d32cb353ff4fa5f3b5d0e8689da2043da6bc98eb8799b18b9e309970","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/ui/making_screen_test.dart drives MakingScreen with a fake PreviewView; the streamed page images in apps/clax_app/test/ui/making_screen_shots_test.dart are Chromium screenshots with JavaScript off. Unverified on device: that WKWebView's loadHTMLString navigations (about:blank) pass previewAllows and later loads are not refused; that loadHtmlString four times a second does not flash white between documents (setBackgroundColor is ignored on some platforms); and that IgnorePointer over the platform view leaves the making screen's own gestures working.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"276a79963a171f155c4b209818537d93b5eae334a471bd789d2dd03cd6846682"},"suggested_fix":"Once the progress wiring lands, run a make on the macOS debug build and the phone (integration test I1 or the live check) and look at the preview while index.html streams.","summary":"WebViewPreview is exercised only through a fake: JavaScript off, the about:/data: navigation rule and the CSP meta are unchecked on a real Android or macOS WebView","tags":["verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:10:55.875104Z","id":"99f09dc6ecca581b95fc45c9672d68c5155405b88eda3c2de19f3aebeae94bac","body":{"detail":"MakingLog sets asking on ToolStarted('ask') and the screen stops its elapsed seconds and says 'waiting for you'. The question has no artifact, and its sheet (the shell's question card at <base>/inbox?q=<qid>) is planned as QuestionWebSheet with its presenter in app.dart (plan Task N2). Until that presenter runs while the making screen is on top, the person sees that a question waits but has nowhere on this screen to answer it, and the ask waits up to its 300 s timeout.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"f98ffe6f69b2359df0ed2f7e520a45edf214907c477c8d4dd0c7b7cbd2f67801"},"suggested_fix":"When N2's presenter lands, check that a question about no artifact opens its sheet over the making screen, and that Cancel on the making screen withdraws it (AgentLoop.newApp withdraws open questions on every end).","summary":"A new app's question shows on the making screen only as the step 'Asking you a question' with the seconds stopped; the question card itself is not shown here","tags":["depends-on-n2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:12:56.290321Z","id":"3f0fa021918df8f21115714be73e9cc6473fe2276bbcfe5c5669c9cb8ef85099","body":{"detail":"Failure: TalkBack (or VoiceOver) on, any change running for more than a second: _workingView wraps the whole chip in Semantics(liveRegion: true) (working_chip.dart:160), and the chip-elapsed Text (working_chip.dart:186-196) merges into that node's label. A widget test with ensureSemantics, one step 'Changing index.html' and the clock advanced a second per pump reads the live node's label as 'Changing index.html\\n1s', then '...\\n2s', then '...\\n3s'; Android announces a live region on each label change, so the reader repeats the step once a second for the whole run and drowns out everything else. The announcement should change only with the step (and Loading the new version / Trying again).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"97dec5805c895872149d0bcbf0d7f8b2c47b9f7092011b4eca4e77bc6f4a33eb"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the live region on the step text only (or wrap the elapsed Text in ExcludeSemantics and give the chip a label of the step), and add a semantics test that advances the clock and asserts the live node's label is unchanged. While there: the expandable chip's tap has no semantic hint (an onTapHint such as 'Show steps' via Semantics(onTapHint:) or a tooltip), so a reader user does not learn it expands.","summary":"The working chip's live region carries the ticking elapsed seconds, so a screen reader announces the chip every second","tags":["review","u2","a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:12:56.290485Z","id":"1a508a2fb48d99bc4f121360d3fa3c7a5266f7b3c9d5052a2a3a5f215360f1af","body":{"detail":"A widget test with the working_chip_test.dart rig at 780x360 logical px, top padding 24, three steps and a render, expanded: the chip spans y 32-306 at scale 1.0, 32-368 at 1.3 (RenderFlex overflowed by 19 px on the bottom) and 32-506 at 2.0 (overflowed by 94 px). The lower part (the thumbnail's error count) is clipped in release and draws overflow stripes in debug; the header with collapse and Dismiss stays reachable. A maxHeight from MediaQuery (for example the view height minus the chip's top and a margin) with the steps and thumbnail in a SingleChildScrollView is a few lines, and a landscape case in the 'fits a phone' test would hold it.","kind":"comment","references":"708cf82e8842748a383d4e906cc888e0b959721e84b69f817397b4031a9d8357","span":{"start":{"line":215},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"9a3d66fc3eda3259bc9c473daccb349f8e6172427b21acc0ce9230810de5a45c"},"summary":"Measured: a 780x360 landscape phone (24 px status bar) overflows at text scale 1.3, not only 2.0; fix with this round","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:12:56.290562Z","id":"9312b7abc6cd611ebe0b64e89ffa74f67893fc30a92872e8ca31457cb638f3fe","body":{"detail":"Two lines in lib/agent/timings.dart (beside sayUsable, longpressLanded) and one case 'Send → first step' in timingLabel (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:334-338), plus the import change in change_tracker.dart. settings_screen.dart was U5's file this round; U5 has landed, so the change does not collide.","kind":"comment","references":"15fafe1f351244c19bda835ec7d6bcb3a9233d21b4cb9ee87b575e911510eafe","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"858f3d1ae694d0b843f4a136ea7196e2728c667b9f9bcd1c24db2589066c6e2c"},"summary":"Cheap to fix now: move sendFirstStep to lib/agent/timings.dart and add its label to timingLabel","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:12:56.290619Z","id":"287cd716ee56ce6aff649efb229d3ca554610d5ca8b31c6782e63234a68e4c11","body":{"detail":"_retryChange calls onRetry once per failed thread, awaiting each. FeedbackWorker.retry (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:577) queues a job and calls _kick, and _drain dequeues it synchronously (_next, worker.dart:332), so the second thread's job cannot be merged into the first: a change that was one run for threads [a, b] becomes two runs. When the first starts while the second retry is still awaiting the threads list, WorkerWorking([a]) clears the Retry (ChangeTracker._newWork), retried() then does nothing, and b is not tracked until its own WorkerWorking, so after a lands the chip goes idle and comes back. The usual failed change has one thread; a FeedbackWorker.retryAll(aid, tids) that queues every thread before kicking would keep the change whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":400},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"6dacb3084c3543cb0eb1a282bffc229cdbf67940ae6ecafd27feaf4ba64aedfc"},"summary":"Retry of a failed change that answered several threads runs them as separate changes, and the chip can go idle between them","tags":["review","u2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:16:58.494324Z","id":"af6c02abd181dee7c73e043538e3261b388cd251f5d10716f980d4f209b607ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 (test cleanup f1c07f346b12): _workingView in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart puts liveRegion only on the step Text's own container node, excludes the elapsed Text from semantics, and gives the chip's tap the hint 'Show steps' when it can expand. Test 'the live region is the step alone: elapsed time is silent' (apps/clax_app/test/ui/working_chip_test.dart) advances the clock three seconds, one pump each, and asserts the live-region labels stay ['Changing index.html'], change to the new step on a new step, and that the tap action carries onTapHint 'Show steps'; it failed before the fix (the live label carried the seconds). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/ui/working_chip_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/change_tracker_test.dart: +106 ~48, All tests passed; flutter analyze on both files: No issues found.","supersedes":"3f0fa021918df8f21115714be73e9cc6473fe2276bbcfe5c5669c9cb8ef85099","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.859516Z","id":"6a02da4e63a17498f0541bd288ab47e88df003de761051c7859f8321e99b605c","body":{"detail":"On macOS a debug build (f1c07f346b12, CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT runner script str_replace, render, finish) took a change on a real daemon to v2 with renders: 1 and outcome finished in agent-timings.jsonl, so WKWebView under InspectorHost's cover loaded the inspect view and answered inspect. No Android device or emulator was attached, so the Android platform view (webview_flutter's default texture-layer composition) laid out under InspectorHost's ColoredBox is not checked. Failure would show as every render ending in 'The page did not load: it did not load within 10 seconds' or 'did not answer', and finish refusing every change. If it fails: keep a 1x1 logical pixel of the WebView uncovered at a screen corner, or move the cover so the platform view is on screen but under the app's opaque route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"73111d21a466cae114ae761f5db1895021be33d642102aab24361a3a1f231fa0"},"summary":"The inspector's WebView under the opaque cover is checked on macOS only; that a covered Android WebView keeps rendering (so the shell's inspect settles and the clip renders) is unverified","tags":["android","inspector","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.859768Z","id":"a231fee8d19bf1beec1ab0ed82be2d297802c79f49abaf8d52eff1c46503963a","body":{"detail":"Renders of one run reuse the draft's artifact ID, and WebViewAppSurface.call is a no-op until the new document's Init (ShellSession.canCall). A previous inspect document that reloads its frame (a page calling location.reload) between the load request and the new document's start would post a ready that passes the artifact check. The inspection then waits its answer limit (settle + 10 s) and returns InspectorError 'did not answer', costing one render of the run. Narrowing it needs a load generation from the surface (a document counter on AppSurface) or the version in the ready matched against the draft's published version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"08d96c676d85502e5c5457946caed112156a65c3fa079d646c82a94bc3a248c5"},"summary":"An inspection takes the first ready for the draft's artifact after load() is called; a ready the previous document of the same draft posts in that gap would be taken, and the Inspect call then goes to a document without a nonce and is dropped","tags":["inspector","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/read_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.860066Z","id":"e2b8fca37b254e5b338cf987c8080dfe30d96084ea511421a6c068a82df882a0","body":{"detail":"DialogReadConsent pushes a DialogRoute on the root navigator. data_tools.dart _askOwner pauses the run's budget clock while it waits, so the run does not time out, but the background notification (BackgroundRuns in apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart) keeps showing the run's last step, not that an answer is needed. A notification step such as 'Waiting for you to allow reading <app>' while the dialog is up would tell the person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"bfb6da1079bc5dc4f25a9bcc24ba5945bbff1f7824d786fffecee946feb404c0"},"summary":"The agent-read consent dialog shows only over the app in front: a change running while Clax is in the background waits on it unseen, with its wall clock stopped, until the person comes back","tags":["consent","background","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.860268Z","id":"9ffa45afc77bd72d4b1923e3716df7f2a6d2cecfcecaa9e1dd6918d45045ea07","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9221bb779242ab1d90f622b38202c2f1268c75ef0f2e285d990efb7820a20f97","summary":"onOpenTarget is wired since f1c07f346b12: AppRoot._openTarget opens the app and, once its page is up, sends LoadVersion(n) for a version item or OpenThread(tid) for a reply once the shell lists the thread (test/app_test.dart 'an inbox reply opens its app at the thread once the shell lists it; a version item at that version'). onOpenQuestion is still not passed: a question item opens its app (or nothing, for a question about no app) until the question sheet lands (plan Task N2).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.484863Z","id":"82f204305d00ad70c2603de3415819a0d2bc2367747f12eb82061427d7915954","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot passes commentButtonDy from AppSettings.commentButtonDy and keeps onCommentButtonMoved in settings.json (comment_button_dy). test/app_test.dart \"the comment button's place is kept for later app screens and launches\" and test/ui/settings_test.dart \"the comment button's place round trips\" pass.","supersedes":"f2abe3a554c4bf0a080e2eec785dc86a3e389a68782de9f054f46a12b38a93e5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.485812Z","id":"6252942c4cc82bcc172762d0c754ceb9f0b046e699f771743a883ac007e24902","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot holds one SharedClaxStream on gallery, inbox and questions from the first Up (f1c07f346b12); Launcher follows gallery and inbox on it instead of /api/events and its own stream, and hands it to InboxScreen, which leaves it open (f1c07f346b12). Tests: test/clax/shared_stream_test.dart (5), test/ui/launcher_test.dart 'a shared stream is used for the launcher and its inbox, and left open', test/app_test.dart 'once the daemon is up the app holds one stream on gallery, inbox and questions' pass.","supersedes":"e43c349dd88f0c9de7b00218b7172982b9a575c0b53037699439e54df0363680","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.486930Z","id":"8b4c00c405299ab71e2426eb81184481f708792c3d921df620856c0936e035fc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot._make reports MakeProgress for each event, and MakingScreen gets timings from AppRoot._offerLostMake and from Launcher (its timings parameter). test/app_background_test.dart 'a make streams to the making screen, which hands over to the new app in its place' (narration shown on the making screen), test/app_test.dart (say-first-output started beside say-usable) and test/ui/launcher_test.dart 'with handOver ... the making screen records on the timings' pass.","supersedes":"a648cc7ed637989e9154f5d35c6f5ee48d6402285dcb762ce90b006f633918ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.488139Z","id":"37cc967d04c846d812f6c5b24094ba5510aea7316e16d9c77758456b47fc481c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: MakingScreen.onMade hands the new app over; AppRoot._handOver pushReplacement's the app route in the making route's place (result Made), and _AppPage keeps the last render's PNG as an opaque cover (made-cover) until the shell's first ready for the app, or a load fault. test/app_background_test.dart 'a make streams to the making screen, which hands over to the new app in its place, covered by the last render until ready' and test/ui/making_screen_test.dart 'with onMade the made app goes to it' pass. A single-call make (no render) has no PNG and shows the app screen's own cover.","supersedes":"3bdc33348d0e37f079ec8435b6d05059a76e5e275959c9149981277dd2dd721d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:26:47.046414Z","id":"c042ce08d148f9c94bc16e8ae073beb9e0f9931f7feb3dac8104a14217df9c35","body":{"detail":"Failure: any new app made on macOS with the tool loop (MessagesRunner streaming PartialFile for index.html). MakingScreen._makeView (lib/ui/making_screen.dart:338-343) always passes background: colorScheme.surface; webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0 WebKitWebViewController.setBackgroundColor (lib/src/webkit_webview_controller.dart:568-571) calls PlatformWebView.setOpaque, which on NSViewWKWebView does `throw UnimplementedError('opaque is not implemented on macOS')` before any Future exists (lib/src/common/platform_webview.dart:380-386). The `.catchError` here only sees an asynchronous error, so the constructor throws. The throw runs _load -> PreviewThrottle._fire -> offer -> MakingScreen's report -> app.dart progress -> MessagesRunner._emit (lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart:99-103, no guard) -> the turn's stream handler (lib/agent/runner/turn.dart sink calls), so the run fails with a non-AgentError, or, if swallowed, _view stays null and every later load throws again. Observed with a macOS debug probe built from this file with the same wkwebview version: `Unhandled Exception: UnimplementedError: opaque is not implemented on macOS` at `new WebViewPreview (making_preview.dart:65)`. making_screen_test.dart never builds a WebViewPreview, so no test catches it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"c9c4d2c44cc4d52340716f0993dec702720c5199b09a43ef7948aa291a419a9b"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the call so a synchronous throw is caught too (try { c.setBackgroundColor(b).catchError(...) } catch (_) {}), or skip it on macOS; and make MakingScreen._load tolerate a throwing _makeView (no preview, run continues). Add a test that a PreviewView factory that throws leaves the run going and the placeholder shown.","summary":"On macOS, WebViewPreview(background: …) throws UnimplementedError synchronously, so the making screen's first streamed index.html chunk throws out of the progress sink","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:26:47.046519Z","id":"058f5f5993b3825032ff4269681217e701dd08d14c913425da70c4b32cd0882c","body":{"detail":"The preview's own documents never need a data: navigation: loadHtmlString arrives as about:blank on WKWebView (probe log: `NAV ALLOW main=true about:blank` for every load), and Android's loadDataWithBaseURL is not routed through shouldOverrideUrlLoading. A meta refresh to data:text/html is a renderer-initiated top-level navigation to a fresh document without the previewDocument meta; whether it keeps the initiator's CSP depends on the engine. On macOS WKWebView the probe saw `NAV ALLOW main=true data:text/html,…<img src=http://127.0.0.1:<port>/data-escape>` followed by `ERROR 102 Frame load interrupted` and no request reached the server, so WebKit stops it. Android WebView is unchecked (Chrome's block on top-level data: navigations does not cover WebView). The test at test/ui/making_screen_test.dart:85 asserts data: is allowed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"4b62b074f42f359d2e788e16f90a15ff9b9bb8a7415cf934e9a79efa02cdf852"},"suggested_fix":"Allow only about:blank (and about:srcdoc for subframes), refuse data:, and flip the test's data: expectation.","summary":"previewAllows lets the preview navigate to any data: URL, which a streamed <meta http-equiv=refresh content=\"0;url=data:text/html,…\"> uses to leave the CSP-carrying document","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:26:47.046627Z","id":"c131b7f1c986d69d0692b9279914c1e0d14f122c0db45bad65df789967706ac7","body":{"detail":"Cases loaded through WebViewPreview.loadHtml with a NavigationDelegate logging previewAllows' decisions: img, picture srcset, CSS background url(), @import, @font-face url(), link stylesheet/prefetch/preload/icon, iframe http and data:, iframe srcdoc, object, embed, video poster/src, audio, svg image, input type=image, a form with autofocus, <base href> with a relative img: 0 requests logged. Meta refresh to http and to a <base>-relative URL: `NAV PREVENT`. Meta refresh to data: allowed by previewAllows, then `ERROR 102 Frame load interrupted`, 0 requests. Pages finished loading (onPageFinished about:blank, no resource error). Still unchecked: pixels on screen (no display was available to capture), Android WebView, and flashing between loads. Constructing WebViewPreview with a background throws on macOS: see the blocker on lines 63-66.","kind":"comment","references":"c92f75e6d32cb353ff4fa5f3b5d0e8689da2043da6bc98eb8799b18b9e309970","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"276a79963a171f155c4b209818537d93b5eae334a471bd789d2dd03cd6846682"},"summary":"macOS WKWebView (webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0) probe of WebViewPreview with JavaScript off: every loadHtmlString arrives as about:blank and passes previewAllows; later loads are not refused; no subresource reached a logging server on 127.0.0.1","tags":["review","verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:26:47.046695Z","id":"2eb9fca33e8af010a9be716c3015b8c0a2c746f5f987196bdba1641a309521da","body":{"detail":"Rendered with MakingScreen at physical 720x1280, devicePixelRatio 2, textScaleFactor 2.0, light and dark, failure reason 'Exception: The model refused: check Settings': `A RenderFlex overflowed` on Column-[<'failed'>] (constraints h<=592); the buttons sit under the overflow stripe. The layout is unchanged from before f1c07f346b12, so this is not a regression, but a large-text user cannot reach Retry or Edit (back still leaves). The making view itself fits at the same size, with the step line wrapping beside 'waiting for you'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":620},"end":{"line":682},"content_hash":"d6c35161140dfb68d9e7ec41a5da71378335d4db48b3f3da9bd93f23c0c1f785"},"suggested_fix":"Put the failure Column in a SingleChildScrollView (or LayoutBuilder + scroll) and add a widget test at textScaler 2.0 on 360x640 that finds Retry hit-testable.","summary":"At text scale 2.0 on a 360x640 dp phone the failure view overflows its Column and pushes Retry, Edit and Cancel off the screen","tags":["review","a11y","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:29:23.036746Z","id":"1e90d5cefc1766806145ddfc1d0d0787e015b356436fb339cd7ba244787048fc","body":{"detail":"webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 (pubspec.lock) builds WebViewWidget with displayWithHybridComposition false (lib/src/android_webview_controller.dart:1121, 1211), so _initAndroidView takes initSurfaceAndroidView: texture-layer hybrid composition, falling back to a virtual display. In both, the android.webkit.WebView stays attached to the activity's window with View.VISIBLE and the size InspectorHost lays out (inspectorSize: the screen on a phone); the framework paints the TextureLayer under the ColoredBox and neither framework nor engine hides or detaches an occluded texture-layer view (hiding views missing from a frame is the Hybrid Composition path only). Chromium's page visibility follows the view and window, not whether Flutter composites the texture, so the document is visible, timers run unthrottled and requestAnimationFrame ticks. The screenshot is taken inside the page (web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts: modern-screenshot domToPng at scale 1, no requestAnimationFrame in web/node_modules/modern-screenshot/dist/index.mjs), not from the composited texture, so a fully covered view loses nothing. The pixel-uncovering fallback 6a02da4e names is therefore not needed for the app in front; the background case is record below on _surfaceFor.","kind":"comment","references":"6a02da4e63a17498f0541bd288ab47e88df003de761051c7859f8321e99b605c","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"73111d21a466cae114ae761f5db1895021be33d642102aab24361a3a1f231fa0"},"summary":"Source reading: with the app in front, an Android WebView under InspectorHost's opaque cover keeps loading, running script and answering inspect; record 6a02da4e still wants one device run","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:29:32.197954Z","id":"a703715845acf150bbb1394c44472518d26510c24d39a0d3d57756e32e0e7ccd","body":{"detail":"_surfaceFor (lines 159-166) makes the WebViewAppSurface when the first inspection asks for it; InspectorHost only attaches its platform view on the next frame. On Android a run goes on in the background under the dataSync service (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/background_work.dart), but a paused Flutter app draws no frames, so a first render after the person switched away loads the inspect view into a WebView that was never attached to a window (no layout size, no visible document): the inspection fails or screenshots nothing, and RenderTool (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart:146-152, 165-170) tells the model its page 'did not answer ... fix it and render again', which finish then refuses. In front, the first render also pays Chromium's start, the shell's first load and its lazy host chunk inside inspectLimit (8 s, render_tool.dart:22) together with the 3 s settle; the macOS run in 6a02da4e does not measure a phone. Unverified on a device; a later render in the background reuses an attached WebView whose document Chromium marks hidden (timers throttled), also unchecked.","kind":"concern","references":"1e90d5cefc1766806145ddfc1d0d0787e015b356436fb339cd7ba244787048fc","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"507b264fc29675dcf074235c18a6d907c7f7be629dbe9545808e2e580a5c9dab"},"suggested_fix":"Make and attach the inspector surface as soon as the daemon is Up (AppRoot._onState's Up case), loading the shell's inspect view once so Chromium and the shell's chunks are warm before the first render, and make it again on a new endpoint there rather than in _surfaceFor. Then run CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT once on a phone, in front and switched away, and record the render's settled_ms from agent-timings.jsonl.","summary":"The inspector's WebView is made at the first render, so a first render while the app is in the background, or a cold WebView on a phone, can miss the 8 s inspection limit and fail a working page","tags":["review","android","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:30:33.411335Z","id":"20670f1b3e4344e2e0d65c6d3d7df87eb37ceb4625bf97709b2e42f024b61da3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"WebViewPreview skips setBackgroundColor on macOS (previewSetsBackground) and catches a synchronous throw; MakingScreen._load catches a throwing preview factory and keeps the placeholder; MessagesApiRunner._emit ignores a throwing listener. Tests 'a preview that cannot be made leaves the placeholder and the run going', the previewSetsBackground expectations in 'the preview document shuts the network…' (test/ui/making_screen_test.dart) and 'a progress listener that throws never fails the run' (test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart, failed with 'Bad state: listener broke' before the fix) pass: flutter test test/ui/making_screen_test.dart test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart, all passed.","supersedes":"c042ce08d148f9c94bc16e8ae073beb9e0f9931f7feb3dac8104a14217df9c35","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_preview.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:30:33.412293Z","id":"2b5741d4ecd3509244c16bd3ccc074dd33be8931aa9168c76bee739974840ad4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"previewAllows accepts only about:blank and about:srcdoc; data:text/html and about:config are refused in the test at apps/clax_app/test/ui/making_screen_test.dart (the preview document test), which passes: flutter test test/ui/making_screen_test.dart, +22 all passed.","supersedes":"058f5f5993b3825032ff4269681217e701dd08d14c913425da70c4b32cd0882c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:30:33.413136Z","id":"be066afd98a6569d881d87d602e288b060a66e2ae13e2b41b0e8321be0162bfc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The failure view is a SingleChildScrollView, and with scaled text the making view scrolls with the card at half the height. Test 'at text scale 2 on a small phone the failure view scrolls to Retry, Edit and Cancel' (360x640, TextScaler 2.0) finds each button hit-testable, taps Retry, and sees no overflow: flutter test test/ui/making_screen_test.dart, +22 all passed.","supersedes":"2eb9fca33e8af010a9be716c3015b8c0a2c746f5f987196bdba1641a309521da","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:30:50.803323Z","id":"732ae91cb65295c8fc3bc4b857630001d0f536fa7b184070075dec0957e27400","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot._onState's Up calls WebViewInspector.warm(endpoint.base), which makes the surface (mounted by InspectorHost at once, while the app is in front) and loads the shell's inspect view once, hidden, queued behind any inspection; a new endpoint warms a new surface. Tests pass: test/ui/inspector_surface_test.dart 'warm makes the surface and loads the inspect view once, hidden; the first inspection reuses it' and 'warm waits for an inspection in progress; a new address warms a new surface'; test/app_test.dart 'a WebViewInspector is kept in the root, under the app, and warmed once the daemon is up' (13 + 20 + 18 passed). The phone timing (front and switched away) is still unmeasured, with 6a02da4e.","supersedes":"a703715845acf150bbb1394c44472518d26510c24d39a0d3d57756e32e0e7ccd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:23.183138Z","id":"2521833ce54c328d42580dca6a4a3fd2a56ac2af72f370c86e4dc1a8235e254c","body":{"detail":"Notification permission is asked for only by _make in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart (background.requestPermission, once per install; see record da2ee5a9 on BackgroundWorkChannel.kt). _showNotice only asks AppNotice.allowed, so on Android 13 and later an install whose first act is opening an existing app (an inbox link, a restored gallery) shows the right-edge handle and the hint's notifications-off text until a Make asks. The first-run hint says to allow notifications but offers no button for it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":331},"content_hash":"ea004b35607bfb15510925a581364d9a8a41878b891a722108fd12caff183847"},"suggested_fix":"Ask once from the first app screen too (before or with the first-run hint), or give the hint's notifications-off text an Allow button that calls requestPermission and then opens the app's settings (dev.empathic.clax/native openAppSettings) when the request was already used.","summary":"An app screen never asks for POST_NOTIFICATIONS: someone who opens an app before their first Make gets the edge handle, not the notice","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:36.760279Z","id":"11bf555c4d1fcbf848425fab3fdd423a39cf83cfb0a9fe378bca885dccb6fd9b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a QuestionsMsg whose open count rises while the app screen is in front shows the toast 'Clax has a question', whose View calls OpenQuestions (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart, case QuestionsMsg). flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart --plain-name 'a question that lands shows a toast' passes (+1: All tests passed).","supersedes":"cfd9e233e857857f8678d1298c6047ebe831b08ae8d46aaacfb864439c6ce8a5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:17:24.445196Z","id":"47f926e615726ac70e672dbb101e69e356632a941417d5ee7a3209b315101d77","body":{"detail":"AppInspector takes a plan builder, but Launcher (lib/ui/launcher.dart _menu) pushes AppInspector without one, because PlanStore (lib/agent/plan.dart) was not on the branch when the inspector landed. Wiring it means a read-only view over PlanStore.watch(aid) passed from lib/app.dart through Launcher.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"baa264bfdef13d6f8fad303f258a2624a936ec3dba6586400a4774ac75d3ad4b"},"summary":"The Plan tab always shows 'No plan': nothing passes AppInspector.plan yet","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector_permissions.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:17:24.445296Z","id":"bc4cd6cc9b68bb19cb5fcac34d23e09fce02d4ad9266c79f14c2b1a14041627d","body":{"detail":"The daemon has no route listing the readers granted a source, so DbGrantPermissions.load asks every other app's grants (GET /api/artifacts/<reader>/db-grants) and filters by source. Fine for tens of apps; a GET /api/artifacts/<source>/db-readers route would make it one request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"c30e2486d6f667596afd64a4c0beb3aa4eee74a3bfd5985e5fca2df66fc30ac2"},"summary":"'Who may read this app' makes one GET db-grants per app on the device","tags":["performance","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector_code.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:17:24.445341Z","id":"d126063d9ab194cc971d75df132772db0e7bdf4a5bff36bb8f44a7ac40bcd5ce","body":{"detail":"Only block comments and JavaScript template strings carry across lines; a regex literal, a '//' inside a one-line string the pattern misreads, or script and style inside HTML are coloured plainly or wrongly. Highlighting stops after 5000 lines (_CodeViewState._highlightLines).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":62},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"d96a5860590be79bd30dc22b280ced5a552ca7c367c817d04e24bb776a8ced45"},"summary":"Highlighting is per-line regular expressions, not a parser","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:19:37.163932Z","id":"6eb839c54fb9e264a2b0e6898422dca6c0cfb373408fbe0e0a645e578c38e44d","body":{"detail":"_AppInspectorState._load awaits api.readFiles (lib/clax/http_api.dart readFiles: one GET per text file, all in parallel) before any tab renders, so Overview, Data and Permissions show a spinner until the largest file arrives, and a single file request that fails replaces all five tabs with the 'Try again' state. Fine for the generated apps of today (tens of KB); an app with many or large files pays it on every open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"c65a622aa47efe8766098aa12e462e66622592e525ea8472821a20f432846704"},"suggested_fix":"Render Overview, Data and Permissions from getArtifact and collections, and load a file's text when it is opened (or load the file map in the Files tab only).","summary":"The whole inspector waits on every text file of the live version, and one failed file fails every tab","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:19:37.235936Z","id":"3a2ddc377336ea6fa97ea5fd8d9fdbf8d489b0fb0559df8cbbdcf52de411e5e6","body":{"detail":"test/ui/app_inspector_test.dart exercises only success paths. The code handles failure (_Failed with retry at lines 208-240, 'Couldn’t read these' per permission source, the 'Couldn’t revoke it' snackbar in _PermissionsState._revoke, 'Couldn’t load. Try again' in CollectionPage), but a regression in any of them would pass. FakeClaxApi can throw ClaxError for one call to cover them.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"f8ed032c24ac24eaebfc48c23c5377ce753eb0e6dd7a30cc62e47a9d0e2f0f0b"},"summary":"No test covers the failed load: daemon down, 'Try again', or a revoke that fails","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:06.897970Z","id":"104ee7477a5c12d0365908c7f6a31a4c37775bf5094f42a7ba7d7d1154db8225","body":{"detail":"The harness imports tests/*.test.js with a dynamic import() from the page's frame. In sandbox mode the frame's origin is opaque, so the import is a cross-origin module load; Chromium accepts it with the daemon's headers (the e2e passes), but WKWebView and Android WebView were not run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"8a053c3c33444fc2338f4261303e0c7fa985aaad004053565fc51934f6bf0ef8"},"summary":"Tests in render are verified in Chromium (web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts, both frame modes) and against the fake surface, not in the app's WKWebView or an Android WebView","tags":["app","tests","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:43.842735Z","id":"65ad8422a14cecd977387d6dae1ed57ff6b64a4948aaa25e5b94da482c018d8d","body":{"detail":"git show f1c07f346b12 -- apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart adds DeviceResult and OpenRoute beside RunTests; DeviceResult's doc names [DeviceRequest], which f1c07f346b12 does not define (it is in the uncommitted working copy). The file compiles at f1c07f346b12 (dart:convert is imported), but the device task's history now starts in another task's commit, and its own commit of this file will show no such hunk.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":528},"end":{"line":559},"content_hash":"c9a2a1524240256375fc3132fdab4bada09b8e3bffb5f2d5f352d2f862ad36ca"},"summary":"DeviceResult and OpenRoute (the device capabilities' host calls) were committed in f1c07f346b12, a tests-in-render commit","tags":["review","review:T1","process","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:53.201152Z","id":"c0156d60d54d5a362b71432cd5db54f51e5f93c688d570d3373e36ddd7aed272","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: Launcher passes AppInspector.plan, a read-only BuildPlanPanel over PlanStore.watch(aid) (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart _menu). Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'a tile shows its going build, and Inspect shows the plan'. flutter test test/ui/build_view_test.dart: +8, all passed; flutter test test/ui test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +419, all passed.","supersedes":"47f926e615726ac70e672dbb101e69e356632a941417d5ee7a3209b315101d77","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:53.203120Z","id":"34d387dba686d623453ba74a2f87eae31e6e6205e903942ecafc2a9cbd25517b","body":{"detail":"MakingScreen._follow feeds each continue run's BuildState.progress into MakingLog, which loads PartialFile('index.html') text into the preview. A continue run that edits (PartialEdit) or writes other files (app.js) changes nothing on screen until a render's Inspected screenshot. Showing the published app's latest version in the preview, or applying the edit to the shown text, would keep the preview live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":525},"content_hash":"4ff79646038ec2ac0b6edcdd9705ff4a187453e453219428d11476dc00ef2ec1"},"summary":"After the first version, the build view's live preview follows only whole-file writes of index.html, not edits","tags":["build","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:53.203188Z","id":"aafdfe33a6efe2dcaf7d3acc2a1a65200f185baf35a0c3b1e38eaee468db61f3","body":{"detail":"AppScreen shows the build chip only while the build is queued or running; once it stops the chip goes and the Resume/Undo action lives on a 4 s toast. The inspector's Plan tab (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart _menu) is read-only with no Resume. After the toast fades, Add to plan (BuildLink.addToPlan resumes) is the only way back from the app. A Resume in the launcher tile's menu or the inspector's Plan tab would cover it; a toast while the build sheet is open is also not shown (the route is not current), the sheet itself showing Resume.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":607},"end":{"line":640},"content_hash":"f0df04e9af76aeb754cd5548c63e71e98f8240219f1ab7f27e348e0163c7d2ca"},"summary":"A stopped or failed build can be resumed only from its toast, Add to plan, or the build view","tags":["build","ux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.963254Z","id":"2634bc3a6f71c6a81f399dca34b891617db6b1fe1c4fa617ac5696e61429c0a5","body":{"detail":"Failure: open any app whose build goes (queued or running), e.g. the Focus timer with 6 features. BuildChip ('Building · Weekly focus chart · 2/6', ~650 px wide at 1080 px) is drawn at top: 8 for every queued and running phase, across every continue run, so it covers the app's header and anything tappable under it until the build ends; target/flutter-app/x1/build-4-chip-light.png and -dark.png (CLAX_X1_SHOTS=1 flutter test --update-goldens test/ui/build_view_shots_test.dart) show 'Focus timer' hidden. The rule for app screens is transient notices only (no permanent Clax UI over apps). The change chip is acceptable because a change lasts seconds; a build lasts minutes.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1005},"end":{"line":1022},"content_hash":"b9fedc768659068bbf3bffc64fc4a59799d9767f7a3a51a63df71d98fc10dcc1"},"suggested_fix":"Show the chip expanded for ~4 s when the build starts, a feature starts or finishes, or the phase changes; then collapse it to a small pill (a progress ring with '2/6', ~36 px) in the top-right of the status-bar/safe-area band, clear of the app's content; a tap on the pill expands it, and a tap on the expanded chip opens showBuildSheet. Inject the clock so the collapse is tested without sleeps.","summary":"The build chip sits over the app's own title for the whole build (minutes), which amounts to permanent Clax UI over the app","tags":["review","review:X1","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.963711Z","id":"4ea28a1d9fc6ef509ff626fe04078b6beceba3623a53690718af8f51fa1b129a","body":{"detail":"Decision on aafdfe33 (coordinator's call, owner may overrule): a stopped or failed build is resumed from the launcher tile's menu, shown only when the plan is stopped or the last BuildState is stopped/failed and the plan has todo features, and from the inspector's Plan tab (launcher.dart _menu passes BuildPlanPanel with no onResume today). Both call BuildControl.resumeBuild(aid).","kind":"concern","references":"aafdfe33a6efe2dcaf7d3acc2a1a65200f185baf35a0c3b1e38eaee468db61f3","span":{"start":{"line":336},"end":{"line":347},"content_hash":"a5bf511209ab29e3051ffe6aa9158e6f43bc3b85626917fa29862a960b9dcd3a"},"summary":"Add 'Resume build' to a tile's long-press menu (next to Open and Inspect) and a Resume to the inspector's Plan tab for an app whose build is stopped or failed","tags":["review","review:X1","ux","build","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.964351Z","id":"6920a0dab4e78b19fa730f575be9d5cc7ec5afcae8140714a570c296697d39a8","body":{"detail":"_addToPlan sends CancelDraft before awaiting BuildLink.addToPlan; if PlanStore.addFeature throws, the snackbar says 'Couldn’t add it to the plan' but the text is gone. If addFeature succeeds and resumeBuild throws, the feature is added but the person is told it failed. The add button is also an icon-only IconButton.outlined (playlist_add, tooltip 'Add to plan') beside Send in threads_panel.dart, so its meaning is found only by long-press; a text label or a first-use hint would make it discoverable. build_plan.dart _PlanChecklistState._submit has the same pattern: it clears the field before addFeature and does not catch its failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":657},"end":{"line":668},"content_hash":"6c2c8f61d749dfc09dad9dbde5bdcb146ca4b7bdbc0993754cfbdcb38872c90f"},"suggested_fix":"Await the add first and close the composer only on success; on failure keep the draft open. Treat a resumeBuild failure separately from the add.","summary":"Add to plan closes the composer before the add, so a failed add loses the person's comment","tags":["review","review:X1","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.964692Z","id":"eafe8e74a8d6398297e3b60c15500b4749f00a7c0f32a00477e6a4080c3e34b2","body":{"detail":"On a failed first run the screen keeps the request and offers Retry (good). Retry clears _planKey and the next run makes a fresh pendingPlanPrefix key, so features the person added or dropped during the failed run are not carried over, and the old 'new:<micros>' plan stays in the store forever (_recoverBuilds skips pending keys; nothing removes them).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":422},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"a9dacd2ceda5d61153f7883d636d7910ea19eacdc9ddcd2dfcb625e3c14f44d5"},"suggested_fix":"Reuse the failed run's plan key on Retry, or remove the pending plan when the run fails or is cancelled.","summary":"Retry after a failed first run drops the person's plan edits and leaves the old pending plan in PlanStore","tags":["review","review:X1","build","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:05.965893Z","id":"b0bad776b9f20cab78a6ae9c1386db53d6a288206e2042003c6849c5fb68c37d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 as decided in 4ea28a1d: the launcher tile's menu offers 'Resume build' when the build is stopped, capped or failed with features to build, and the inspector's Plan tab has Resume. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'a tile shows its going build, and Inspect shows the plan'. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"aafdfe33a6efe2dcaf7d3acc2a1a65200f185baf35a0c3b1e38eaee468db61f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:15.900059Z","id":"fa7c7cf0e6527404144fc85eb1b1405bb63a5eafb7b7b80e093ee2d793289c92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 and f1c07f346b12: AppScreen._addToPlan sends CancelDraft only after the feature is added, keeping the text with a message on failure; BuildLink.addToPlan no longer fails an add whose resume fails; the peek labels the button 'Add to plan' at 380 dp and wider (icon with tooltip below); the checklist's add field clears only after the add. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'a failed Add to plan keeps the composer and its text'. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"6920a0dab4e78b19fa730f575be9d5cc7ec5afcae8140714a570c296697d39a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:15.901189Z","id":"a039df31bc389c226ff49b070727a7f489877ce1b0d404f76ba638c40f00329d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 and f1c07f346b12: the build chip shows whole for 4 s (AppScreen.clock) when the build starts, a feature starts or ends, or the phase changes, then folds into a pill (ring and '2/6') in the status bar's band at the top right; a tap opens it, a tap on the whole chip opens the sheet. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'the chip shows the build while it goes; its sheet stops it and a toast says so'; target/flutter-app/x1/build-4b-pill-{light,dark}.png show the title clear. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"2634bc3a6f71c6a81f399dca34b891617db6b1fe1c4fa617ac5696e61429c0a5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:15.902182Z","id":"837dadfe9fb6e88147c7a3b55e2e191c414d448adb386b17f0994ecbebfc993b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: a Retry writes the plan the failed run left (edits included) under the new run's key before it plans, so its first plan_set is shown that plan; the failed run's provisional plan is already removed by AgentLoop.newApp (loop.dart, the finally of newApp). Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'Retry after a failed first run starts from its plan, the person's edits included'. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"eafe8e74a8d6398297e3b60c15500b4749f00a7c0f32a00477e6a4080c3e34b2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082605Z","id":"32f8f89d4048214e8c13b6cfbbb6fc2be52efdcb4e41f63b02f868bed02e9fbc","body":{"detail":"It runs Navigator.maybePop, so from a thread page over an app it goes back to the app. Cmd-[ is only the native menu's key equivalent (no Flutter shortcut, to avoid handling it twice); test/ui/app_menu_test.dart checks the item's shortcut and onSelected, not the menu delivering the key while the WebView has focus. Esc is a Flutter shortcut and does not reach Flutter while the WebView has focus (record 098fa267 on lib/ui/app_screen.dart).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"ba6cf415e641ec5913daf9dc0f170b4f7b0987615331a318d9f4597f066a91d2"},"summary":"App > Back to Apps (Cmd-[) goes back one screen, not to the launcher, and its key equivalent is unverified on a real Mac","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082654Z","id":"d5bd79bed5e33776caafa9ab60bdeed7986be4bd1eacc97171dcc56ff3fa86ff","body":{"detail":"MakeService runs each new app's first run beside FeedbackWorker (concurrency FeedbackWorker.maxConcurrent), with no limit of its own, each under the first run's own per-run caps. Spend and API rate limits grow with the number of makes the person starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"f8ced030698341d8d1e3fbc333423706f9914d4be240420056bb38bd986fc611"},"summary":"Makes are not counted in the worker's cap of three: several makes plus three worker jobs can run model calls at once","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:10:51.019647Z","id":"5d07bed9192e4e6fe97a65c9b0e48c79e8d676763806bd333c825e3393102fe4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d5bd79bed5e33776caafa9ab60bdeed7986be4bd1eacc97171dcc56ff3fa86ff","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"cde4ef05b5267fbfb811c7f7e959af7af69d1285de8fc8c9063b4a2c3f763244"},"summary":"Recommend a cap of three running makes (the worker's maxConcurrent): MakeService.start keeps a fourth as a queued tile (MakeSession.started false, already supported by add) and starts it when one ends. A few lines in _changed; bounds spend and rate-limit errors.","tags":["review","review:X2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:10:51.019800Z","id":"d15f67e2d3403c76b4aac3eb51e488e0383e88c214ffd80de3fe392136d97f8b","body":{"detail":"The CallbackShortcuts wraps the whole MaterialApp, so it runs after WidgetsApp's DismissIntent (dialogs, popups close first, as test/ui/app_menu_test.dart checks), but EditableText does not consume Esc: a sheet or page with a half-typed request or comment is popped and its text lost. Consider skipping back when primaryFocus is an EditableText with text, or confirming a non-empty sheet.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"a6f7dd5159e0f03990e21d024ed7f89915fbe3e63b60409eea7cbd2d6f33913e"},"summary":"Esc on macOS pops the top route even with a focused text field, so Esc in the New sheet discards the typed request","tags":["review","review:X2","macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:16.754354Z","id":"94945846c41ffef8dacb578d43714b5a64c6fb11c13294fe2b460dd79c0ee712","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"b101339287270f594990da2324f3ff8e52686adc7bd04e14df8afe7bc7c8e804"},"summary":"Fixed: MakeService.maxRunning (3) caps running makes; later ones wait as queued tiles and start oldest first. test/ui/make_service_test.dart 'at most three makes run; the next waits and starts, oldest first, as one ends' passes (flutter test: +1333, all passed).","supersedes":"d5bd79bed5e33776caafa9ab60bdeed7986be4bd1eacc97171dcc56ff3fa86ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:16.757044Z","id":"53508af52e9df449a09cefb5925099107d82dc96b56ed7c8dc3b8aa0f517e343","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":143},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"83e28b42a88ed68f5246ec8bd2ede3a8039ed05ed1a922847d5ad2ffa378cd1a"},"summary":"Fixed: Esc on macOS is EscapeIntent (escapeShortcuts/escapeActions on the MaterialApp); escapeOrBack unfocuses a focused field instead of going back, and in a field Esc is the platform's cancel (a sheet closes, its text kept as the launcher's draft). test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'Esc in a text field never goes back and keeps its text' and test/ui/launcher_test.dart 'on macOS Esc in the New sheet keeps the typed request for the next New' pass.","supersedes":"d15f67e2d3403c76b4aac3eb51e488e0383e88c214ffd80de3fe392136d97f8b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_icon.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:35:23.452212Z","id":"cd770a15ff0b3d5fa1d7745f8ab5f9bcc6b06c5a8b4aec784ffb0ba6ce463239","body":{"detail":"The launcher drops a deleted app's tile on artifact_deleted (lib/ui/launcher.dart _onGallery) but AppIcons has no forget, so the JSON file (at most 32 KB of SVG plus a few bytes) stays. Harmless at today's app counts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"03f11d9ba20eabb09db4dc79c8ad64e0490d6561014c76ce47f0aef6a55c74e8"},"suggested_fix":"Add AppIcons.forget(aid) and IconStore.remove, called from the launcher's artifact_deleted branch.","summary":"FileIconStore keeps an entry per app forever: a deleted app's icon file under <support>/app-icons is never removed","tags":["x4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_icon.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:35:23.452252Z","id":"d4c7ee8f836dcf77c005e64bca2864fa3636e24a3c50edf18cf844d296f55e4f","body":{"detail":"Not done: flutter_local_notifications takes a bitmap, so it needs rendering the SVG to PNG (vector_graphics picture to image) and a file per app and version, and the reminder scheduling code (lib/platform/device/reminders.dart) has no access to AppIcons. Notifications show the Clax launcher icon meanwhile.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"b3b5bc6ba1c4aa119f232636ac684bfbfb6135b90d2293654061db8c26048b43"},"summary":"Android reminder notifications could use the app's icon.svg, rasterised, as their large icon","tags":["x4","revisit:reminders become a main use of apps, or the owner asks for per-app notification icons","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:13.491923Z","id":"a97a7e81396ea4d5188c254ad00ba75040c26dd7a47c0816fe2d2366dab3d6ea","body":{"detail":"Failure: any app with an icon.svg, on a 412 dp phone (target/flutter-app/x4/launcher-phone-light.png): each tile is a ~120x140 dp card with the icon in its top-left corner, the title left-aligned at the bottom and most of the card empty, so the launcher reads as a card list rather than a home screen of the apps' own icons. _AppTile lays out padding 16, badge 52, Spacer, title (lines 626-700); the grid is SliverGridDelegateWithMaxCrossAxisExtent(maxCrossAxisExtent: 176) at line 569, which gives 3 columns at 412 dp.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":616},"end":{"line":698},"content_hash":"849d8df4628ea2266fa15c86aa5479d02817904d55a8518d30d3c68454e2c8f2"},"suggested_fix":"Lay the launcher out as a phone home screen: the badge at 56-64 dp, centred; the title below it, centred, at most two lines; no card background (or a very subtle one); 4 columns on a phone and more on desktop (a maxCrossAxisExtent near 96-112 dp). Keep the build ring on the badge's corner, and give MakingTile (lines 700-) the same shape: its ring or Waiting/Interrupted/Couldn't-make-it state in the badge's place and the request as the centred label. Update _AppTile.extent to badge + gap + two label lines.","summary":"The launcher tile buries the agent-designed icon: a 52 dp badge pinned top-left in a large surfaceContainerLow card, three columns on a phone","tags":["ui","launcher","x4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_icon.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:13.492139Z","id":"80c7a40ccc7a9ff4c2bbd15ac7fb60e4016c216b34831a87a6e57f3451ade0c0","body":{"detail":"Entries are cleaned before save, so only a file changed on disk is affected, and flutter_svg fetches nothing; re-running cleanIcon on load would keep the one rule that every drawn icon has passed it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"bc2102ab9ccef7ed7c7eb1ad35c264aee41c354510e493ccb8aeab8dac1866e8"},"summary":"FileIconStore.loadAll hands the svg it reads from disk to SvgPicture without cleanIcon","tags":["security","x4","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:45:00.575814Z","id":"2013c34475181be88dad2a78b4309edb3e790374b0fede1d6929a8329337259c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed by removal: the chip no longer expands inline; a tap opens the change sheet (lib/ui/change_sheet.dart), which scrolls within a bottom sheet capped at 86% of the height or a full-height side panel (f1c07f346b12, f1c07f346b12). flutter test test/ui/working_chip_test.dart passes, including the renders at text scale 2.0.","supersedes":"708cf82e8842748a383d4e906cc888e0b959721e84b69f817397b4031a9d8357","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:45:38.872273Z","id":"1caf42d1bd8a594847e9cf82e7ac24a8038c221f9b453d6827c60363dc47ec98","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Launcher is a home-screen grid: 60 dp centred icons, centred 2-line labels, no card, maxCrossAxisExtent 112 (4 columns at 412 dp, 11 at 1280 dp); MakingTile states take the icon's place. flutter test: +1363 ~79 all passed (launcher_test making-tile tests included); shots target/flutter-app/x4/launcher-{phone,desktop}-{light,dark}.png","supersedes":"a97a7e81396ea4d5188c254ad00ba75040c26dd7a47c0816fe2d2366dab3d6ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_icon.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:45:39.345129Z","id":"eeb26e47942a00754ca30c58469a40cbca8be539de398aa19c0124267b4d646d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppIcons._load passes every kept svg through cleanIcon; test/ui/launcher_test.dart 'a kept icon is cleaned again before it is drawn' passes","supersedes":"80c7a40ccc7a9ff4c2bbd15ac7fb60e4016c216b34831a87a6e57f3451ade0c0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:31.353653Z","id":"50103d76c34a5cfc6a498b41d702d4f7552e8afc56cdcd94055766de7610999a","body":{"detail":"Failure: any change on a phone. target/flutter-app/x3/change-phone-dark.png shows 'Checking how it looks 47s' covering the 'Focus timer' heading; the chip stays expanded from the first step to the outcome (lib/ui/working_chip.dart _workingView). The build chip already follows the no-permanent-UI-over-apps rule (2634bc3a: expanded ~4 s, then a small pill in the status-bar band).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1234},"end":{"line":1257},"content_hash":"6a08ceb54f9b817da28044128b679163ab4f30d0ae98b0b4531090c11b0da3f5"},"suggested_fix":"Give WorkingChip the build chip's pattern: expanded on start, on each new step and on the outcome for ~4 s (injected clock), then the small pill in the status-bar band; a tap on the pill expands it, a tap on the expanded chip opens the change sheet. Test with the injected clock, and re-render the x3 shots.","summary":"The Working chip sits over the app's title for the whole change (a minute or more), unlike the build chip, which collapses to a pill","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:31.353716Z","id":"6c5639186165866531722031ec044fecf9b44f7b40714009b2ace2ea54707482","body":{"detail":"_show sets _landed on the first ThreadView; _target returns null when focusComment is absent (an inbox item or notification racing the thread read, or a stale cache), and later loads from the event stream never land again. With focusLatestReply, if the reply is not yet listed, the previous agent reply is lit as if it were the new one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"ba6a9298526eaf21be5e2afddcaee74ccaa92184fcf2627fe702305f96e6dba0"},"suggested_fix":"Keep landing pending until the target is present (or a bounded number of loads), and for focusLatestReply prefer an agent comment newer than the page's opening.","summary":"The thread page lands only on its first load: a focus comment not in that load is never lit, and focusLatestReply lights an older Clax reply","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:31.353774Z","id":"68caa5283482ae1e3d8661b3c4d997e22af676f21478142da66f1da6c9164ac5","body":{"detail":"WorkerReplied's toast opens _openThread(threads.first, reply: true, run: threads) (app_screen.dart:661-664) but the chip's onReplied opens the panel. The replied chip is visible only while or right after the change sheet was open, so it is rarely reached; it should land the same way.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1244},"end":{"line":1250},"content_hash":"26d5ea28d2e46ec824450ccf99ca4a3c8f24e2e51e45d9b8718918ecebd25eab"},"summary":"Tapping the 'Answered in the thread' chip opens the panel's Threads tab, not the thread at the reply as the toast's View does","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:14:26.260099Z","id":"aa67dfb8754372fefe5ebabab85f503de7634709ee375f0a6912c4b1abf5f030","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the Working chip shows whole for buildChipFor (on AppScreen.clock) when work begins, at each new step, the new version loading and the outcome, then folds into WorkingPill in the status bar's band; a tap on the pill opens it, a tap on the chip opens the change sheet (f1c07f346b12). Test passes: test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'the chip shows whole at each step and outcome, then folds into the pill; a tap on the pill opens it again' (pill within the 24 px band). Re-rendered target/flutter-app/x3/change-2-pill-{phone,desktop}-{light,dark}.png: the app's title is clear.","supersedes":"50103d76c34a5cfc6a498b41d702d4f7552e8afc56cdcd94055766de7610999a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:14:26.261843Z","id":"ab2607c6bfb0e93da12d74a29160a63bfe3be3a9efb97b9f6a3ea45f7aaee9cd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: landing stays pending until a read holds the focused comment, and focusLatestReply lights only an agent comment that is the thread's newest (after the person's last comment) (f1c07f346b12). Tests pass: test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart 'a focused comment missing from the first read is lit once a later read holds it', 'focusLatestReply waits for the reply to the last comment, and lights it when it arrives'.","supersedes":"6c5639186165866531722031ec044fecf9b44f7b40714009b2ace2ea54707482","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:14:26.264287Z","id":"c637bb45b4e469000a5abc4475036960d959be3d68c07fe08376051744e0983f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the replied chip and the toast's View both call _openReplied, which opens the last replied threads at the reply (f1c07f346b12); flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart passes, including 'View on a reply to several threads opens the first at the reply, stepping through the others'.","supersedes":"68caa5283482ae1e3d8661b3c4d997e22af676f21478142da66f1da6c9164ac5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.922713Z","id":"e6aad054d0aa41f6bc9d7737c9ac14504019d3aafceb99fc8b1398b958f9e6c9","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§10.2 asks for a question badge on the comment button and for the sheet to open by itself. The comment button no longer exists, and the app screen draws nothing of Clax's over an app but the Working chip, brief toasts and the first-run hint (app_screen.dart class doc, 'No Clax control over the app'); an unprompted sheet over the app would break that. The open count still shows where Clax surfaces things: the change sheet's 'Clax has N questions for you' with Answer (change_sheet.dart _question). The agent waits at most 45 s on a change's question (AskTool maxWaitChange), so a missed toast leaves the question in the inbox and its late answer re-runs the change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":653},"end":{"line":666},"content_hash":"6b926ef5ead0ba63da3e17bbf2315319b9d67a1e5dc9e185159971c618582fe0"},"summary":"The app screen does not open the shell's questions sheet by itself when a new question about the app lands in front, and shows no question badge; it shows the toast 'Clax has a question' (View: openQuestions) and a light haptic","tags":["revisit:the owner wants the questions sheet to open over the app by itself, or a count on the open app's notice","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.923299Z","id":"6a28a0de6ae07209a5522f3e2011683537545899b98749a4388523d993975740","body":{"detail":"Checked against a scratch daemon with Playwright at 400x640: the card is focused and scrolled into view, the inbox header partly above it. A card-only route in the shell (or an app=1 flag on /inbox hiding the chrome) would make the sheet just the question. The WebView also relies on the shell's own /api/token cookie flow to act as the owner, the same as the app view; a change to how the app hands the token to its WebViews must reach WebViewQuestionPage too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"b9cfbbf676d26787cd8bf984ec8686576cc6a21ab7718586f89e52d4a59ea98a"},"summary":"The question sheet shows the whole shell inbox page at /inbox?q=<qid>: its header, 'Notifications are blocked for this site', search and other items sit above and around the focused card","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:50.306253Z","id":"96a87a0df92ed42f0080783a2d0f47adeec76c6eb33c5772f45e94ac7d6e5892","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: OpenQuestions takes an optional question ID, CloseQuestions exists, QuestionsMsg carries showing (host_protocol.dart). flutter test test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart --plain-name question: +13 All tests passed.","supersedes":"797ee449689a740f1edf422aaec6aca843ec63b106b34984ef78d2eb50767b46","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:50.307879Z","id":"63c04ab8491405a7f9ece474052b9f7e11ada5eb9b345823b170cc1b2164bec6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot passes onOpenQuestion: _openQuestion, which shows the question sheet on /inbox?q=<qid>. flutter test test/app_test.dart --plain-name 'a question in the inbox opens the sheet' passes.","supersedes":"9221bb779242ab1d90f622b38202c2f1268c75ef0f2e285d990efb7820a20f97","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:50.309080Z","id":"04d4ea59be97fd5fa81008ad7e9dd524deb4bcb03bc1148b57f43c94708a6450","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a new open question about no artifact, with no app screen on top (the making screen included), opens the question sheet over it (AppRoot._presentQuestion). flutter test test/app_test.dart --plain-name 'a question about no app opens the question sheet' passes.","supersedes":"99f09dc6ecca581b95fc45c9672d68c5155405b88eda3c2de19f3aebeae94bac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:50.476793Z","id":"fcfe275bb6829fb392f2cc2d3b3df9497cac4149b00e2596fa70d050cd46a124","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6a28a0de6ae07209a5522f3e2011683537545899b98749a4388523d993975740","summary":"Confirmed in WebKit at 412x730 against a scratch daemon (clax serve --foreground, POST /api/sessions/<sid>/questions, then /inbox?q=<qid>): the focused card renders with its options, Other and Answer/Skip, below the shell's top bar (Clax logo, Inbox), Notify me, Mark all read and the search. In the sheet, the top bar's links are top-level navigations off /inbox, which WebViewQuestionPage's delegate (question_sheet.dart:50-56) prevents silently, so they look live and do nothing; Notify me asks for web notification permission inside the WebView. The card-only route proposed here would remove both.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:52.464903Z","id":"ecb9517d5e52219ba2744dfa6cfe119f22270688314e58b1d5537c9ed92d3159","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6a28a0de6ae07209a5522f3e2011683537545899b98749a4388523d993975740","summary":"The app's daemon now starts with --require-credential: /inbox and /api/token answer 401 without a credential. This WebView reaches them with the key cookie (clax_key_<port>) that apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:95-103 puts in the shared WebView cookie store on every Up; WebViewQuestionPage sets none itself. See the concern on apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:89:103 for the timing gap; the question page is unverified against the locked daemon.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:20.578759Z","id":"18cb7cff96af19d765c9dd603aadfc03fe8e61475ef0203d4f4471deeccf805c","body":{"detail":"webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 calls CookieManager.setCookie(cookie.domain, ...) with domain 127.0.0.1 from keyCookie (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart:80), a URL without a scheme. Whether android.webkit.CookieManager fixes that up to http://127.0.0.1 and then sends clax_key_<port> to http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ (any port: cookies ignore ports) is unverified; if it does not, every shell load on Android answers 401 and the app shows no app. Only macOS is covered (apps/clax_app/integration_test/locked_daemon_test.dart). Also unverified on Android: the shell's /api/token request then receiving the owner and events cookies, the room WebSocket and event streams under the gate, and the content frame on <id>.localhost loading /v/, /_clax/ and /_blob/ with no cookie (the server side of each passes on a scratch daemon with --require-credential). A device or emulator run of the shell, a page using db and net, a comment and the inbox closes this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"dc2a847a7f558dfa2e0980066269d69eb6caed11a20e0ac996f28848ba97becf"},"summary":"Android: the key cookie is set for the scheme-less URL 127.0.0.1, unverified on a device","tags":["review","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.960881Z","id":"b3eae590ce2181f3f6dec88df0a4849ad55352e799e47c25de457cc07408312d","body":{"detail":"Since git:f1c07f346b12 the key cookie is made in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart (DaemonKeyCookie.cookieFor): on Android its WebViewCookie.domain is the daemon's full URL, which webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 passes unchanged as the url argument of android.webkit.CookieManager.setCookie (android/src/main/java/io/flutter/plugins/webviewflutter/CookieManagerProxyApi.java setCookie); with no Domain attribute in the value it is a host-only cookie for 127.0.0.1, sent to every port. On WKWebView the domain stays the host, as HTTPCookie's domain property takes it. From the code, the other paths need no app cookie: the shell's GET /api/token is same-origin (web/shell/src/api.ts getToken, owner.ts) and its Set-Cookie for clax_owner_<port> and clax_events_<port> lands in the same CookieManager store; the stream (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts, credentials same-origin) and the room WebSocket (web/shell/src/caps/room.ts, same host) send those cookies as first-party requests; the <id>.localhost frame's /v/, /_clax/ and /_blob/ need none (crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs open_without_credential). Still unverified on a device or emulator: that CookieManager stores and sends the cookie, the shell loads, a page using db and net works, a comment and the inbox (WebViewQuestionPage) load, and a daemon restart recovers the open shell and question page.","kind":"comment","references":"18cb7cff96af19d765c9dd603aadfc03fe8e61475ef0203d4f4471deeccf805c","summary":"The cookie is now set for http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ on Android (DaemonKeyCookie.cookieFor in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart); a device run is still needed","tags":["android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:33:36.124699Z","id":"6a0b64642df23dd3e62d04ff4b5dbc2406199fb1582a2b19d96172422d2a5589","body":{"detail":"CookieLoads.load sets _loaded = true after the cookie is ready but before _load (WebViewController.loadRequest) commits a page. A restarts event in that window calls controller.reload(), which reloads the committed document (about:blank on a fresh question page) rather than the URL being loaded; the pending load may also be cancelled by it, leaving the question page blank or on the old token's 401. The window is one daemon restart landing during a question page's first load. Fix: remember the last URL passed to load and on a restart call _load(lastUrl) instead of _reload.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"f0e76ad04dac6bd60325e513f5467eac31ac93864a65261292a5c42c34f22cc2"},"summary":"CookieLoads marks a page loaded before its load commits, so a restart then reloads nothing","tags":["webview","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:19.175338Z","id":"1cd5e41a36f3f7147e56148abd29040b900fd17b43b6dec4f43ea4c701d5d339","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: CookieLoads keeps the last loaded URL and loads it again after a restart's cookie, instead of controller.reload(). daemon_cookie_test 'a loaded page following restarts loads again with the new cookie' now expects 'load <url>' (it logged 'reload' before); flutter test test/ui/daemon_cookie_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/question_sheet_test.dart: +17, All tests passed.","supersedes":"6a0b64642df23dd3e62d04ff4b5dbc2406199fb1582a2b19d96172422d2a5589","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:55:21.754435Z","id":"7c4650a4a178f758101985e63ebc10d6680c1acd5728b43d00554d388aae1a10","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts runs claxHost.runMigration against a real daemon draft and checks the document migrate.js wrote; test/ui/inspector_surface_test.dart drives WebViewInspector.runMigration over FakeAppSurface. Whether a WKWebView or Android WebView imports migrate.js from the artifact origin under the daemon's CSP is unchecked until integration_test/bundle_test.dart runs on macOS.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"901630266a5adf211db7771c20e3e67b0e5d87369d62599b04f57f113c7b5719"},"summary":"runMigration is verified in Chromium (web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts, both frame modes) and against the fake surface, not in the app's WKWebView or an Android WebView","tags":["bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:58:52.040229Z","id":"9c782cf3ae1f53b16331d0d7492c7df78322d23051c623b9675d5dfa57a64c48","body":{"detail":"Failure: an update whose migrate.js takes longer than 30 s on the live app (the draft's copy is capped at 2,000 documents and 8 MiB, so a run that passed on the draft can run past its limit on the full data), or one cancelled part way. runMigration returns InspectorError or MigrationRun.failed('it took longer than …') while the page stays loaded: _ask's finally (inspector_surface.dart:216-222) only calls setVisible(false), and a hidden WebView still runs timers and promises; harness.ts runMigration's `within` (web/bridge/src/harness.ts:300-325) stops waiting but cannot stop the migrate function. The updater then restores the snapshot (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §8.2 step 7, §8.4) while migrate.js is still issuing db sets and deletes, so the restored documents end partly migrated, or a restore's pinned write meets a moving version, and the sheet says the data is back as it was. The Inspector contract (lib/agent/inspector.dart:40-56) gives the updater no way to stop the page itself.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"a943763423d1e1d232e614bd51178569dd9a9bfe1ef73351b76c3e32072ac17e"},"suggested_fix":"End the document before runMigration returns on every path except ok (or on every path): load about:blank, or a fresh inspect view of the warm ID, into the surface in a finally, and await that load; state in Inspector.runMigration's doc that no code of the run is running once it returns. A test over FakeAppSurface: hang the migration, let the limit pass, and check the surface was loaded away before the error returns.","summary":"A migration that times out, is cancelled or fails keeps running in the inspect view's page after runMigration returns, so it can write over the live run's snapshot restore","tags":["bundles","security","review:BW","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:09:18.013993Z","id":"af1a8f77708f2a4aafd3b79c34c85e5109aceb79d6c047a72f404a581dc73a43","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: WebViewInspector.runMigration loads the migration view again and waits for its ready (at most readyLimit) in a finally, on every outcome, before it returns. Evidence: test/ui/inspector_surface_test.dart 'a migration run that never answers, or is cancelled, is an InspectorError only once its document is replaced' and the ok/failed case (flutter test: 17 passed); web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts 'a migration over its time is reported, and stops writing once its view is loaded again' passes in both frame modes.","supersedes":"9c782cf3ae1f53b16331d0d7492c7df78322d23051c623b9675d5dfa57a64c48","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:29.103860Z","id":"128c1f7ff7c8037153cc9b6229882f36d77e497b62cff806d90e666e82cb8628","body":{"detail":"Bundles spec §12.1 asks for File › Import App… in the macOS menu bar as well. The menu bar is ClaxMenuBar in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart, which takes no import callback; app.dart would pass _bundles.importPicked with the navigator's context.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":575},"content_hash":"d4be78dcfc00cf7573008085310a4ed4f19a6a14c48803113327e35464ad26ca"},"summary":"The Mac has no File › Import App… menu bar item yet; Import app… is only in the launcher's overflow","tags":["bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:14:29.179166Z","id":"a22c402ec84c847fb362cb526842b88384f4b3b075b916aa7ea0d82215e71819","body":{"detail":"Unchecked: share_plus with XFile.fromData and the application/vnd.empathic.clax+zip type on Android (Files/Downloads targets), FilePicker.saveFile writing the bytes in the macOS sandbox, and FilePicker.pickFile with FileType.any on Android returning bytes. Widget tests drive the flows through test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart's FakeBundleFiles.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":918},"end":{"line":963},"content_hash":"16f3dbc641f6134a4d32593dd4f39224a2006232eba9f6f95753b41378d8b37e"},"summary":"PluginBundleFiles (share sheet, save panel, picker) has run only behind FakeBundleFiles; nothing has shared, saved or picked a .clax file on a device","tags":["bundles","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:17:45.428117Z","id":"665a24a0d5e81c869158915de5ad8e4afc2ebdaa9aadda6d02c539f1194ff2f6","body":{"detail":"BundleFlows._update shows BundleProgressSheet with dismissible: false (line 1201), then awaits u.update with no try. Updater.update (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart 175) turns ClaxApiError into outcomes, but anything else thrown (a FileSystemException from LineageStore.update or keepBundle after the publish, an inspector error not mapped to a step, a StateError) propagates to app.dart _bundleSheet's catch, which only logs it. The sheet stays on 'Checking vN against your data…' with a spinner, the barrier and back are disabled, and the person has to quit Clax. _working (line 1243) handles this for build and install by catching Object and showing BundleFailed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1199},"end":{"line":1237},"content_hash":"5831d0385eb349bd147bef2d67a31b1489211077f4ed9b74fed649b95cda3d91"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the u.update call in try/on Object and set progress.value to BundleFailed('Something went wrong.', details: ['$e']), as _working does; a widget test with an Updater stub that throws.","summary":"An exception out of Updater.update leaves the update's progress sheet up for good: it is not dismissible and nothing pops it","tags":["bundles","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:17:45.428223Z","id":"c1dc9d72cce22b4afc31ca857d047a0007a7aae307e7b2f57f703538d415c5e3","body":{"detail":"ExportSheet's fork layout (target/flutter-app/bu/export-modified-phone-light.png) shows the switch, then 'Share Alex's v2' and 'Share my version as a new app'. _done drops includeData for ExportMode.reshare (line 331), which is right, but a person who turns the switch on and taps Share Alex's v2 is not told their data stayed out. The subtitle is null in this layout, so the 'v1' the fork carries (spec §3.5) is never shown.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":420},"content_hash":"10b18d37f6e7898cfb2e6f26cbd8bf32ecc38b083eed30a56ed80404fbe9d6c8"},"suggested_fix":"Label the switch for the new app ('Include my data in my version'), or disable it with a line under it while the original is the focus; show 'Yours goes as v1' in the paragraph.","summary":"On a modified copy the Include my data switch sits above both buttons but only the fork uses it, and the fork's version is not shown","tags":["bundles","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.137753Z","id":"51fd61570f66113fdc2030c6db1128c0a5136c5c9392b7f22aaf30db119d8aa9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"BundleFlows catches any error from Updater.update into UpdateRefused, so the progress sheet ends on BundleFailed. Test bundle_flows_test.dart \"an updater that throws ends the progress sheet with a failure\". flutter test test/bundle/ test/agent/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart test/ui/bundle_sheets_test.dart test/ui/bundle_entry_points_test.dart test/app_test.dart: +868 ~4, all passed.","supersedes":"665a24a0d5e81c869158915de5ad8e4afc2ebdaa9aadda6d02c539f1194ff2f6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:48:17.584454Z","id":"664cefd459207408cfed6d1f68658e94c0b8b47bf009c6b7a196bc9c7142aa23","body":{"detail":"_tellVisible stops every running watch when the screen is not visible, and visible is false whenever the screen's route is not on top: a second device consent dialog (say camera.take while watching), the thread page, the inspector or the questions sheet's route all end the watch with stopped. The consent dialog that a watch's own start shows is spared only because watches still asking are skipped (DeviceHost.stopWatches, asking: false). If pages find this disruptive, stop only on lifecycle hide, the screen's dispose and a new document, and treat Clax's own routes over the app as still on screen.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":483},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"f6b46048bee5c44b6423cd91e70e9b59bc9fdf025a4ad9ca0cd4f49a99ecdeee"},"summary":"A location watch stops whenever anything covers the app screen, a dialog of the same app included","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:35:39.246662Z","id":"a55ecb23c818ff0ff151026fa676564e5c8c9f8a5817047b74c0ca2fa39b6355","body":{"detail":"Comment mode showed two Send buttons: the shell composer's (web/shell/src/ui/Composer.svelte) and the peek's. The peek's was removed, keeping Send next to the textarea the keyboard types into, with its screenshot wait, its shortcut and Cancel. The other way, the peek's Send sits right above the keyboard on Android whatever the WebView does, beside the mic, but the composer would need a Cancel in the peek and a way to hide its own buttons only when the app hosts it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"5d800927e2609786a3f056770c72a319371bda3e1e68df8dca9549c5e584b1ad"},"summary":"Keep the peek's Send and hide the shell composer's Cancel and Send in app mode","tags":["revisit:the composer's Send is found under the keyboard or out of reach on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:39:50.184114Z","id":"7b0c40315e453f0e051e408693a06516854f004ed5bc0361bc11be633548328d","body":{"detail":"AppPanel lays out a wide panel as _peek then the threads list (lines 131-140) while a draft is open. Each open thread not yet sent to the agent has a TextButton 'Send' (resend) at line 351. A comment without @agent is unsent, so a desktop person composing with the panel open sees the composer's Send in the page and one 'Send' per such thread beside it. The phone layout shows only the peek, so the narrow case holds one Send.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":351},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"c5bce7ba1525dae174bedb6e4bc2ad4a8c2e969d1be949f60c85c8f8a12e2df0"},"suggested_fix":"Label the row action 'Send to agent' (or an icon with that tooltip), or hide the list's resend buttons while a draft is open.","summary":"On a wide screen a composer's peek sits above the threads list, whose unsent threads each show a 'Send' button, so the page's composer is not the only Send","tags":["ux","comments","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:48:29.519132Z","id":"bc06b658b27ac8b568b1e7ca1c6a758528eceb5c486e974a29c336798b00917b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The thread row's action reads 'Send to Clax' (the row's status says 'sent to Clax'), so the composer's Send is the only plain Send. Evidence: test/ui/threads_panel_test.dart 'a wide panel composing beside an unsent thread offers Send to Clax, not a second Send' passes; flutter test test/ui: 491 passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"7b0c40315e453f0e051e408693a06516854f004ed5bc0361bc11be633548328d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.950198Z","id":"bc0ed8550ffb44c43e041318a5726a37b300b91573fc335ffa1c53a803b6768b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a55ecb23c818ff0ff151026fa676564e5c8c9f8a5817047b74c0ca2fa39b6355","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-15): \"I preferred the Flutter UI send box. We should also do a better job of rendering the 'snippet' being sent\". The app's composer is the send box; the shell's is hidden in app mode.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.950298Z","id":"508dcbb2ad7210221b4f73b2aeb0c7c70da3509f305a7c40065ac50529b55922","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Taken as the owner decided: apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_composer.dart is the one Send (mic, field, Cancel, Add to plan, Send, snippet preview); web/shell/src/app/app.css hides the shell composer in app mode; submitDraft({text}) sends. flutter test test/ui: 511 passed; playwright app-mode, hold-drag, inspect, drag-release, app-questions: 45 passed.","supersedes":"a55ecb23c818ff0ff151026fa676564e5c8c9f8a5817047b74c0ca2fa39b6355","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.960609Z","id":"e2d39b88dc7e26e0524037958ead89b91bcf6a6dac71b6c7ffda9fa1b724eb7d","body":{"detail":"While a draft is open the Scaffold does not resize for the keyboard (resizeToAvoidBottomInset: !composing) and the composer is positioned at viewInsets.bottom. Widget tests at 320x568, 390x844 and 1100x720 with a 260 dp inset and text scale 1.3 hold Send, Cancel and the field above the keyboard with the page rect unchanged. Not checked: that the Android platform-view WebView keeps its size (no relayout of the app's page) when the Flutter TextField raises the IME, and that focus moves cleanly from a page input to the composer field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1378},"end":{"line":1430},"content_hash":"ff7b8429e4d575ee5c714eb8cb092e82aeacf16482c3963ede9fa3d0faf9be80"},"summary":"The keyboard-over-the-page layout while composing is verified in widget tests and renders only, not on a phone","tags":["android","unverified-on-device","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:52:34.960713Z","id":"ca36e7684571b03c837cb3c451e2f3a47de9b4884a593bbfbc3cbd40c9609e3d","body":{"detail":"Rendered in target/flutter-app/c2/10-wide-1100-scale1.3.png: a 960x150 clip shows about 56x9 dp in the threads list. Crop to the card's left part, or show wide clips on their own line under the summary.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"d9a4c6afbcb20eb65ac8e65f7cadd4961a2be042ba5818dcbdd9a76783f87cbd"},"summary":"A wide screenshot (a row of the page) is tiny as a 56 x 44 list thumbnail","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_composer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:56:00.881098Z","id":"dceb3f2e808b62898d627b83a5558c21d4ab441a4fba48ef947754c8a53e5c62","body":{"detail":"Image.memory has no cacheWidth/cacheHeight, so the composer's preview and every visible row of the threads list (threads_panel.dart _ThreadClip) hold a full-resolution RGBA decode: a 1600 x 2400 area clip is about 15 MB of image memory per thumbnail, and AppScreen._clips keeps every thread's PNG bytes for the screen's life. Together with the base64 hop recorded in web/shell/src/app/.qual 42c815ab, this is the phone memory cost of the preview.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":74},"content_hash":"deaf564e2e900b62f17fd2542d37e5155d8635ddbcd158fa3f835fa431a16438"},"suggested_fix":"Pass cacheWidth (maxWidth x devicePixelRatio, rounded) to Image.memory, or wrap in ResizeImage; and/or have the shell downscale the draftClip preview to about 512 px before posting it.","summary":"ClipThumb decodes each screenshot at full size (up to 1600 px a side, web/bridge/src/clip.ts MAX_SIDE) to show it at 96 x 72 dp or a 56 x 44 list thumbnail","tags":["perf","unverified-on-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T23:56:00.881233Z","id":"ef0b80e7034146c80753661bdebaf4c27f4c0e37b7482e4778d12fe5bc7a6625","body":{"detail":"_sending clears only on the composer closing, a busy-to-idle state, or any Notice. web/shell/src/ui/Composer.svelte:69 cancels a post queued behind a pending screenshot when the anchor changes (a page's composer moved to another area keeps its key), with no notice and no busy, so the app's composer reads Sending… until Cancel. Rare (page-opened area composers only); Cancel still works.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":661},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"10f4898ac7c7f96330b70014802be5558eb1a0bf166708dadcefa0efb3dc59cf"},"suggested_fix":"Also clear _sending when a state arrives with the same key and a changed kind/label/quote, or have the host post a notice when a queued post is dropped.","summary":"Sending… can stay on, with the field and Send disabled, when the shell drops a queued post without going busy or posting a notice","tags":["ux","comments","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:05:45.974728Z","id":"d3171b4f5fc4468550887261a07d872c846914cd75289b1f8d49893545414c1e","body":{"detail":"onCancel is the app screen's Stop (FeedbackWorker.cancelChange, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:371-409), which cancels the running change and drops the app's queued comments. After it, the thread is stopped but unanswered, which threadStatus reads as working (concern 14d2ae32), so the card says 'Clax is working on it' until the page is reopened from a fresh change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":812},"end":{"line":820},"content_hash":"436b1a059f6809e1890d94e04ad185002793a7ded1ab5c6d3b7be2f4963255e1"},"summary":"Cancel on a waiting thread stops the app's whole change, every thread it carries, and the page then reads 'Clax is working on it'","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:05:45.974798Z","id":"7b568e1991b8276db425c9edd375d5c8a03a2a19fdb3569d8b48629c0f3447de","body":{"detail":"The tile's status line is one line wide (two lines overflow the cell by 18 px, seen in a render of test/ui/offline_shots_test.dart), and 'Waiting for connection' is cut to 'Waiting for …'. The tile shows a cloud-off icon and 'Offline'; its build view and its screen reader label say 'Waiting for connection'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":828},"end":{"line":837},"content_hash":"148e754526db31380a7f45312b8b811093adcf160922dbcb399a11f8f139bd2b"},"summary":"A make waiting for the connection reads 'Offline' under its tile, not 'Waiting for connection'","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:09:09.471204Z","id":"14821d2e73ff1b7f4052bc11c169bb6a16c4a4027a38c7521d3ee9f93ee11288","body":{"detail":"Failure: comment on an app with the Claude API unreachable, open the thread (card 'Waiting for connection'), tap Cancel. AppScreen's onCancel (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart, ThreadDetail onCancel) calls widget.onStop = FeedbackWorker.cancelChange (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:371-409), which cancels the change, drops the app's queued comments and keeps each of its threads as stopped (no recovery runs it, after a restart too). _waitingThreads is cleared, so the card falls back to threadStatus (thread_detail.dart:36-46): sent and unanswered with feedback acknowledged reads ThreadStatus.working, 'Clax is working on it / The app stays as it is until the change lands', and the working status has no action (no Send, no Retry). The person is told work is going on that was just cancelled, and has no way on this page to send it again except writing a new comment. It also cancels every other thread the same change carries, without saying so. Builds on d3171b4f and 14d2ae32.","kind":"blocker","references":"d3171b4f5fc4468550887261a07d872c846914cd75289b1f8d49893545414c1e","span":{"start":{"line":812},"end":{"line":820},"content_hash":"436b1a059f6809e1890d94e04ad185002793a7ded1ab5c6d3b7be2f4963255e1"},"suggested_fix":"After a cancel, show the thread as stopped ('Cancelled — not sent', with Send again calling the worker's retry), from the worker's stopped threads (StoppedThreads) or a local flag set by onCancel; and say on the Cancel (or a confirm) when the change carries other threads.","summary":"Cancel on a thread waiting for the connection leaves the page saying 'Clax is working on it' with no action, while nothing runs","tags":["ux","offline","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:08.803402Z","id":"052c0b40d73610e37e44d1148ee31e0ad955f5e23a2502d4821cc04743145316","body":{"detail":"_topPill places them at MediaQuery.paddingOf(context).top + 6, inside the side insets, off the status bar's icons and any cutout (test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'the pills at the top', app_screen_device_test.dart location pill tests). The page fills the area under the inset, so a kit app's top-right action (target/flutter-app/nav/pill-*.png, rendered by test/ui/app_screen_nav_shots_test.dart) can sit under the 24 px pill until it is tapped open or the change ends. Not checked on a phone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"27bdded228e78f7d55ed0e1b62fc58c6ae9f3a891e225c09a9b647d1876b2997"},"suggested_fix":"If it gets in the way: reserve a 32 px strip above the page while a pill shows, or tell the page the occupied corner (a CSS env-like variable through the bridge) so the kit pads its app bar.","summary":"The folded chips and the location pill now sit 6 px under the top inset, so they cover the top corners of the app's own header","tags":["ux","needs-verification","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:08.803644Z","id":"93b32b9ec250e49d0041f492440b872ff36cebb9fe20486097687ea65246114a","body":{"detail":"_restore calls ReloadLatest after the restore publishes; the shell's newer for the restored version may arrive first and _offerNewer shows the toast until the Ready of that version ends the offer (_endOffer).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1383},"end":{"line":1400},"content_hash":"53929e528e3a06344c719d0c10492b7725243879f75d9d81259d071547c7c9ce"},"summary":"Restore or Undo can flash the New version toast before its own reloadLatest frame lands","tags":["ux","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:13.259595Z","id":"10b0994e9aafb850cdc3240a8a32251312e40010c3c4351db3f6594041a63fff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Cancel now stops the thread alone (FeedbackWorker.cancelThread, f1c07f346b12) and the page reads Cancelled with Send again from the worker's stopped threads (f1c07f346b12, f1c07f346b12). Evidence: flutter test test/agent/worker_offline_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart pass ('cancelling one thread of a waiting change stops only that thread…', 'Cancel on a waiting thread leaves it reading Cancelled, with Send again, never working', 'a change waiting for the connection … which then reads Cancelled'); full flutter test +1766 passed.","supersedes":"14821d2e73ff1b7f4052bc11c169bb6a16c4a4027a38c7521d3ee9f93ee11288","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T02:24:13.265419Z","id":"ac7632d46d8a471995ca052fdd0f11d9614908a7c70da68167a44ebd7b1ac1fe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Cancel stops only its thread; the change's other threads run again without it, and the thread reads Cancelled (same evidence as the resolve of 14821d2e).","supersedes":"d3171b4f5fc4468550887261a07d872c846914cd75289b1f8d49893545414c1e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_composer.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:31:38.144718Z","id":"34c5d538994a46839077da40d37044abdeb008edd1521ce0be2d4942c35d33fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"ClipThumb now resolves its PNG through ResizeImage(policy: fit, allowUpscaling: false) bounded by its laid-out box times devicePixelRatio, covering the composer preview and the threads_panel.dart list thumbnail. Evidence: flutter test test/ui/comment_composer_test.dart passes 'a full-size screenshot is decoded at its thumbnail size, in device pixels' (1600 x 800 PNG at dpr 3 in a 96 x 72 box decodes to 288 x 144, shown at 96 x 48).","supersedes":"dceb3f2e808b62898d627b83a5558c21d4ab441a4fba48ef947754c8a53e5c62","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:48:15.019825Z","id":"1642cd027f92ad61648d05528148862d933631a2463139ce0b9df55444080a98","body":{"detail":"Failure: on the Android phone where a change landed but the open app was not replaced (the unexplained fault in web/shell/src/app/host.ts record 7e88cd61), make a change from the app; the worker reports WorkerLanded(version) to AppScreen, but the toast only shows on the shell's `newer`, which comes from the same version event (web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts:157) that went missing, so no toast shows, the change chip stays landing, and the person has no way to load the version. The WorkerLanded case here knows the version and ignores it unless the view is pinned.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":931},"end":{"line":943},"content_hash":"eda49148156c0729535a2a46758148e44bb2588f6469ca7f02ec78aa10cbdcef"},"suggested_fix":"In the WorkerLanded case, when not pinned and version > _ready.version, set _newer = version and call _offerNewer() (the same path NewerMsg takes). Reload's reloadLatest fetches the artifact over HTTP (host.ts follow(), getArtifact) and needs no stream event. Widget test: WorkerLanded(2) with the shell showing v1 and no NewerMsg shows 'New version ready', and Reload calls ReloadLatest.","summary":"The New version toast depends on the same shell stream event whose loss (7e88cd61) stopped landed changes replacing the app on the Android phone","tags":["review","android","live-update","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:48:15.019984Z","id":"fc63101e255cb2b2ffe6981bd7516d55a20c895938a74b69b187bff372ea2578","body":{"detail":"The toast is shown on the app-wide ScaffoldMessenger (8 s, or queued behind another toast). Leaving the app with back, or opening a thread page, does not hide it: the setVisible handler (line 570) clears only widget.notice, and dispose does not hide it. On the launcher the toast still offers Reload, whose onPressed calls _call on a disposed surface. A queued toast can first appear after the person has left.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1273},"end":{"line":1313},"content_hash":"a066331263f90eac80ed88e793a5973021df9cdf9d11fd8f9d2d68e10b2ac8ec"},"suggested_fix":"When the screen stops being in front (the !visible branch near line 570) and in dispose, set _newerShown = null and hide the toast if it is the current one (keep the ScaffoldFeatureController and call close()); _offerNewer already shows it again when the screen comes back.","summary":"The New version toast outlives the app screen: it stays over the launcher or a pushed route, and Reload there does nothing","tags":["review","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:48:15.020054Z","id":"7c30ebc09b4df4aa5e51359b6a182efcd4f7145c4168405e3da172aa126db33b","body":{"detail":"_back closes what is over the page only when _wantComment (_open || _bar) or _questionsShowing. The composer can be open with both false: _page shows the panel while _draft != null (line 1638) and _setOpen(false) keeps the draft. Then canPop is !_canGoBack: back moves the page under the open composer via GoBack, or pops the screen and drops the draft, although _closeTop would cancel it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":668},"end":{"line":676},"content_hash":"00e4178c4a94fca68e09fad05749eb04d415c439e096604df7c25de09f83d411"},"suggested_fix":"Treat _draft != null like _wantComment in _back and in the PopScope's canPop; test that back with a draft and the panel closed sends CancelDraft and no GoBack.","summary":"Back with the composer open and the panel closed goes back in the page (or leaves the app) instead of cancelling the composer first","tags":["review","navigation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:51:52.369574Z","id":"39271245d56db2a096db12210ac52e58e393c2f594ab7a20700059bf2caf2ea9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: WorkerLanded for an unpinned view newer than the shown version sets _newer and offers the toast; a later NewerMsg for that version is not offered again. test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'the worker landing a version offers it with no newer from the shell, and Reload loads it; ...' passes (toast without NewerMsg, Reload sends ReloadLatest, late NewerMsg(4) shows nothing); flutter test in apps/clax_app: 1770 passed.","supersedes":"1642cd027f92ad61648d05528148862d933631a2463139ce0b9df55444080a98","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:51:52.375220Z","id":"b7077291a4975ef7198e88434e10ac80e102e3719c450b4c6ca4220f2c3a3c88","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: _putAwayNewer removes the New version toast after the frame when the screen is hidden (left, covered, app in background) or disposed. test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'leaving the app screen takes the toast with it' passes (back over the launcher, no newer-toast); flutter test: 1770 passed.","supersedes":"fc63101e255cb2b2ffe6981bd7516d55a20c895938a74b69b187bff372ea2578","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:51:52.380699Z","id":"f3883d2244515e7dc3daf8a0347599a4b890531a85dc591f8c9939adae23c92c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: PopScope cannot pop while a draft is open and _back closes it (CancelDraft) before GoBack or leaving. test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'back with a composer open and the panel closed cancels the draft, ...' passes (one CancelDraft, no GoBack, screen kept); flutter test: 1770 passed.","supersedes":"7c30ebc09b4df4aa5e51359b6a182efcd4f7145c4168405e3da172aa126db33b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:56:43.004556Z","id":"33f7f69555c764303c9b797402dd24faa7244d843a765902ef74f7330e79d938","body":{"detail":"_putAwayNewer calls removeCurrentSnackBar() and clearSnackBars() on the root ScaffoldMessenger. When the New version toast is queued behind another snack bar (_offerNewer with queued: true, or a 'Version N is ready' / error snack shown after it), leaving or covering the screen removes that other snack bar and any the launcher queued in the same frame (for example AppRoot's _madeAway/_failedAway notices in lib/app.dart), not only the toast.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1351},"end":{"line":1362},"content_hash":"272be6c9f9c3f2b489a3dd0c966e5707f66cf17f1e19d4a69c9693bc12a41422"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the ScaffoldFeatureController returned by showSnackBar in _offerNewer and close only that one (controller.close()), or remove the current snack bar only when it is the toast (compare its key 'newer-toast').","summary":"Putting the New version toast away removes whatever snack bar is current on the app-wide messenger, and every queued one","tags":["review","nav","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T04:58:48.609720Z","id":"ad147ab7a5cac161d16f5f040ad84d2979c04812408190625e695be6fe4c96a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the pills sit in a 32 px strip (AppScreen.pillStrip) above the page while work goes. flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_device_test.dart: +111 ~2, all passed, including 'the pills at the top' (page.top >= pill.bottom for status bar 24/48, cutout 56, landscape cutout; the page takes the strip back when nothing runs). Renders: target/flutter-app/fix2/after/pill-*.png show the header's actions uncovered.","supersedes":"052c0b40d73610e37e44d1148ee31e0ad955f5e23a2502d4821cc04743145316","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:08:18.608918Z","id":"46216f7a4acc8ca4c85e5f4b5b91104231560db3137cd53fdf619ee05da9b9cc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: dictation results after Send no longer rewrite the field (the edit that dropped the queued post), and a post the shell's composer drops now raises a 'Not sent: …' notice in app mode, which clears Sending…. Evidence: flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart, 'a dictation result after Send leaves the sent text alone' failed before (setDraftText(\"make it blue\") after Send) and passes after, file +103 all passed; npx vitest run shell/src/comments.test.ts shell/src/app/host.test.ts: 111 passed, including onDropped in the two 'drops a queued shortcut' tests and 'a post the composer queued and then dropped reaches the app as a notice, each time'.","supersedes":"ef0b80e7034146c80753661bdebaf4c27f4c0e37b7482e4778d12fe5bc7a6625","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:11:33.856383Z","id":"6ae873820452d79d264309358e0f4e4edf145d204f3a6c73e44e5bed405ceea6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the screen keeps a handle on its own New version toast and removes only it (up), or makes it go as it comes up (queued); other toasts stay. Evidence: flutter test test/ui/app_screen_test.dart +105 all passed, including 'leaving the app screen puts away only the toast, not one queued behind it' and 'leaving the app screen leaves a toast that took the toast's place, and the toast queued behind it never shows', both failing on the code before (no 'Saved elsewhere' after leaving); the second fails again with the queued path disabled.","supersedes":"33f7f69555c764303c9b797402dd24faa7244d843a765902ef74f7330e79d938","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:03:24.715168Z","id":"0971df5fe367cc6ccfcd1d3fe53606e133fd5714b7508cbbab8e9ff9f8d368eb","body":{"detail":"_home answers available and every call by widget.aid (fixed by the route in app.dart), and the event push at apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:530-537 checks the same. But WebViewSurface.decide (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart:96-111) and ShellSession.isShellUrl (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart) let the top level navigate to any /a/<id>?app=1, and documentLoaded hands that document a fresh nonce. In subdomain frame mode the content frame has no sandbox (record a3ca2a5d on web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts), so the home app's page, or a cross-origin frame it embeds, can navigate the top window with a tap (a target=_top link to /a/<other>?app=1 is enough). That other artifact's shell then asks home.available inside the home AppScreen and gets true, reads apps(), receives every HomeDeviceEvent and can open apps. Sandbox-mode frames (FRAME_SANDBOX, no allow-top-navigation) and nested frames posting clax:call (web/shell/src/bridge-link.ts:8 checks e.source) are not affected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":894},"end":{"line":914},"content_hash":"9fd6bfe2d839bd21fafd4368e37cc336180482388486e2a516f05740f945e928"},"suggested_fix":"Answer home (available, calls and the event push) only while the WebView's current shell document is /a/<widget.aid>: expose the loaded document's artifact ID from ShellSession (or take Ready.artifact) and compare it with widget.aid; or let an AppScreen's top level navigate only to its own artifact's shell URL.","summary":"The home gate trusts the screen's artifact ID, not the document's: another artifact loaded at the top of the home app's WebView is served home","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:08:28.729952Z","id":"84b155374b47bc6ed81e5f025a8b261265ea602b25516a7e84d223c9ae2cb29a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppScreen._homeServed (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart) requires AppSurface.document, the artifact of the WebView's committed shell URL (ShellSession.document in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart), to equal the screen's artifact for available, every call and every pushed event; WebViewAppSurface.decide refuses a top-level navigation to another artifact's app view and reports it on AppSurface.elsewhere, which AppScreen.openApp opens as its own route (app.dart passes _open). flutter test test/home/app_screen_home_test.dart test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart: +44 All tests passed, including 'another artifact loaded at the top of the home screen gets no home, and a navigation to one opens it as its own screen' (available false, apps/open refused, no HomeDeviceEvent, openApp called with the other ID) and 'the top level stays on its own artifact'.","supersedes":"0971df5fe367cc6ccfcd1d3fe53606e133fd5714b7508cbbab8e9ff9f8d368eb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084314Z","id":"fc574c9a4955ff885c0f6ecf2eea8d6a72eff367cf34ab7c46306013885a427f","body":{"detail":"decide() hands any other artifact's app view to openArtifact, and app.dart passes _open, so an app whose page navigates its top to /a/<homeAppId>/?app=1 pushes an AppMode.app AppScreen for the home app over itself. That screen is served home (aid and document both equal homeAppId), which is correct security-wise, but a second home screen sits on the stack. _open could pop to the root when the target is settings.homeAppId.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"329def452636b86aeb62cc4c8132981fdc17b927b184e895e1cef4cb2985d43a"},"summary":"Another app's top-level navigation to the home app's app view opens a second home-served screen","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:54.625186Z","id":"204f67f5366b9a3195d5d34ca68f62df8640a4d7d16597e39e71ef1a87a1e4e7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fc574c9a4955ff885c0f6ecf2eea8d6a72eff367cf34ab7c46306013885a427f","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"329def452636b86aeb62cc4c8132981fdc17b927b184e895e1cef4cb2985d43a"},"summary":"Settings › Home screen › Open (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart, HomeScreenControls.open) takes this path too: it calls _open(homeAppId, action: AppAction.comment), pushing an AppMode.app screen of the home app over Settings. Popping to the home route and sending AppAction.comment on _homeActions would need the thread and version cases kept on the pushed path, and an app-level test.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:45:28.687206Z","id":"e7c636250bc238d88cfdc66dd1bf09c080bbf1b28561745b8711da0484422bff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppRoot._open (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) pops to the home route and sends the action on _homeActions when the home app is shown as home and no thread, version or comment is asked for; Settings › Home screen › Open takes the same path with AppAction.comment. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/home/app_home_test.dart -> '+3: All tests passed!' ('another app taking its top level to the home app goes back to the home screen instead of opening it again', \"Settings › Open takes the home screen's own page into comment mode\"); both fail with _homeShowsApp forced false.","supersedes":"fc574c9a4955ff885c0f6ecf2eea8d6a72eff367cf34ab7c46306013885a427f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:27:59.172051Z","id":"adb2f031b857160dd899c3591d363b82b0786a17a1c92f899fbf9b0f66bed62c","body":{"detail":"FinishTool.capStop's planned branch (lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:282-292) ends ChangeFailed(plannedStopReason(cap)), so the worker sends WorkerFailed and the Working chip shows 'Couldn't make that change: This change was too big for one go ... so what is left of it is planned and being built in steps' with the red Retry button (lib/ui/working_chip.dart:249-283). Tapping it calls FeedbackWorker.retry, which refuses (the thread's last comment is neither a failure reply nor a Keep going reply), and the chip then says 'Nothing to run again: reply in the thread.' while the build runs. The thread page shows 'Clax replied' for the same change. A distinct outcome (or ChangeAnswered) for a planned stop would show the build instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"0c2f4ce06351966ff574bdb23a76b41200797dc5af00e779e31360444995af7b"},"summary":"A planned stop that published nothing shows as a red 'Couldn't make that change' with a Retry that does nothing","tags":["review","keep-going","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:36:51.593653Z","id":"04e34043ad1e4e1aa73d9e8d1549153e7742765ca36e5ca3f0762a0d4f25334d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"A planned limit stop that published nothing ends RunGaveUp(planned: true), which AgentLoop maps to ChangeAnswered, so the worker sends WorkerReplied (no red failure, no Retry) and the build's chip takes over. Evidence: test/agent/loop_limits_test.dart 'a run that plans the rest and then stops at a cap says the rest is being built, offers no Keep going and keeps nothing' expects ChangeAnswered and failed with ChangeFailed before f1c07f346b12.","supersedes":"adb2f031b857160dd899c3591d363b82b0786a17a1c92f899fbf9b0f66bed62c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:19:37.760726Z","id":"dee09e0f4304e7e401db6a4c82fcda157dbaaf9987cae6433a5b49ffc28037ca","body":{"detail":"Flutter applies FilledButtonTheme to both FilledButton and FilledButton.tonal and gives the theme no way to tell them apart. The ink fill set here (fg, primaryHover on hover) therefore also paints the tonal buttons in lib/ui/version_page.dart, settings_screen.dart, build_plan.dart, comment_bar.dart and change_sheet.dart (grep FilledButton.tonal), which §2 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md wants on accent-tint.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"cb651f12b7100d9569c2d7135d03fe923f69667a2f17ae76183d77712e301f8b"},"suggested_fix":"Give tonal buttons an explicit style (ClaxButton with ClaxButtonKind.tonal sets backgroundColor accentTint, foregroundColor agentInk) and replace each FilledButton.tonal with it.","summary":"FilledButton.tonal reads filledButtonTheme too, so every tonal button draws as ink until it moves to a component with its own tonal style","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:19:37.802490Z","id":"d8b4dc06325b9799a75954a613dc72b08856b8c04e8d2196b5f699d40e75396a","body":{"detail":"§1.3 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md routes every mono use through ClaxType.mono (SF Mono then Menlo on Apple). lib/ui/version_page.dart does; these still name 'monospace': lib/ui/app_inspector.dart:557,799,995,1015, lib/ui/app_inspector_code.dart:205, lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart:807, lib/ui/error_screen.dart:60.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":557},"end":{"line":557},"content_hash":"01ae4fb7237c558f54ea46a81fa1de1912a27697d90fc45f5f9c67e1e0074d69"},"suggested_fix":"Take fontFamily and fontFamilyFallback from ClaxType.mono(Theme.of(context).platform) at each site.","summary":"Bare fontFamily: 'monospace' remains in the inspector, the bundle sheet and the error screen; on the Mac it falls back rather than taking SF Mono","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:33:36.354339Z","id":"347e1edb78a676a73de83c8a654cd1175e42b030c23251cde849b51b8d4ef519","body":{"detail":"Remaining sites (grep -rn FilledButton.tonal apps/clax_app/lib): version_page.dart:339, comment_bar.dart:110,117, settings_screen.dart:355, build_plan.dart:278, change_sheet.dart:737. Each file belongs to a later task of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-18-professional-ui.md (Tasks 14, 19, 22, 23, 24), which is where each switches to ClaxButton; the record closes when the last one has.","kind":"comment","references":"dee09e0f4304e7e401db6a4c82fcda157dbaaf9987cae6433a5b49ffc28037ca","summary":"ClaxButton(kind: ClaxButtonKind.tonal) now sets accent-tint and agent-ink itself (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/button.dart, test 'tonal is Clax's tint, not the ink of the filled theme' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/kit/controls_test.dart); the FilledButton.tonal call sites still draw ink until each moves to it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.980303Z","id":"4daaa2762828ca8f74bb750af6f2e7ffb95c77e3582c7960820eaa10c781e855","body":{"detail":"Flutter 3.47.7's floating SnackBar with a width drops the horizontal margin and wraps the bar in SizedBox(width: width) (packages/flutter/lib/src/material/snack_bar.dart:815-823). On a 412 dp phone the 560 is clamped to the screen width, so the bar touches both edges with its 8 dp corners. ClaxToast.show computes min(560, width - 32) itself (lib/ui/kit/toast.dart:56-59), but the ~38 existing ScaffoldMessenger.showSnackBar call sites in lib/ (app.dart:1479,1566,1758, settings_screen.dart:138, app_inspector_code.dart:335, ...) take the theme value. No phone render shows a SnackBar, so the renders do not catch it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":253},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"42288bf60e918238b753097d9cfa3e6cb8906b5690b98e64d13dfacdcdb0d693"},"suggested_fix":"Leave width unset in the theme (margins 16) and cap the width per call, or route the call sites through ClaxToast.","summary":"snackBarTheme.width 560 makes every plain SnackBar on a phone full-bleed, with no 16 dp side margins","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:43:35.167236Z","id":"2b5ef62ea47d3b57b64af7b281c267a18fc350ea9acef71371b8cb5fdd226761","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: sendFirstStep now lives in lib/agent/timings.dart and timingLabel reads 'Send → first step'; developer_test 'shows Recent timings only once Developer tools is on, every name labelled' and 'every timing name has its own label' pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_developer_test)","supersedes":"15fafe1f351244c19bda835ec7d6bcb3a9233d21b4cb9ee87b575e911510eafe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/user_message.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:44:20.267870Z","id":"c83850ea9921223bdfd5983b0e01c4a00e13e1ce849e36c2c2cbc9061016cc3b","body":{"detail":"userMessage returns AgentError.message for any AgentError past the busy and key checks. MessagesApiBackend builds messages such as 'Claude API error (HTTP 400): <API message>' and 'Claude API error mid-answer (<type>): <message>' (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart _httpError and _parseStream), so a 400 or 500 shows a code and raw API text on screen, against spec section 7.1 (no codes, type names or stack text). Spec section 7.3 lists 'an AgentError -> its own message, which is already plain', which these messages are not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"24e296f0d7247b6fd813fd1ced77f04e633f1b77ca7b6dcca574d5ef6d8ef7ed"},"suggested_fix":"Map an AgentError whose message starts 'Claude API error' to a plain line (for example 'Claude couldn’t answer just now. Try again.') and keep the raw message for Developer tools, or make MessagesApiBackend's messages plain at the source.","summary":"An AgentError that is neither busy nor a refused key reads as its own message, which can carry an HTTP status and the API's text","tags":["copy","errors","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:44:20.303817Z","id":"10c2822441047d7eee9b610c5996c9eb6826c2eb3f74119af7dec3dc13b13a1b","body":{"detail":"lib/ui/making_screen.dart shows MakeSession.failure (userMessage's line); failureDetail (rawError) is only logged. Spec section 5.6 and 7.3: the raw text belongs under Details with Developer tools on (DeveloperScope.of, lib/ui/developer.dart).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"76d1226fc46b02f95827f783e0052f744a885f8d51217a73a6cd833ef63b4159"},"summary":"MakeSession.failureDetail keeps a failed make's raw text, but the build view does not show it under Details with Developer tools on yet","tags":["errors","developer","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:00:26.963011Z","id":"7dd01921672ed730d4f9ca7ee53adf4a3e7bb1d0c6861dac3da03d06a17a545f","body":{"detail":"lib/agent/failure.dart stores the Keep going line in touch's words (keepGoingHint) and the thread page shows it in the reader's words with keepGoingIn(text, ClaxVerbs.of(context)) (lib/ui/thread_detail.dart _comment). This chip's failure text (c.outcomeText) and the change sheet's outcome text (lib/ui/change_sheet.dart, the Text of _c.outcomeText near its Keep going button) are shown unchanged, so with a mouse they still say Tap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"9aea0fc8cebcc467457728066abe6e6f848f3ac360bce9942d5f65d19a1e70fc"},"suggested_fix":"Show keepGoingIn(outcomeText, ClaxVerbs.of(context)) in both places.","summary":"The Working chip and the change sheet show a limit stop's outcomeText as stored, so a Mac reads 'Tap Keep going to pick up where it stopped.'","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:51.764820Z","id":"b3dad43c27873a6538a167868dceff46460208dc00711ca6127bf5bf9fef6abe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The theme gives insetPadding 16 and no width. 'a plain snack bar on a phone keeps 16 from the sides' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/kit/surfaces_test.dart failed before (rect.left 0.0) and passes: `bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_kit_surfaces_test` PASSED; theme_test's expectation updated in f1c07f346b12.","supersedes":"4daaa2762828ca8f74bb750af6f2e7ffb95c77e3582c7960820eaa10c781e855","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/threads_panel.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:53.843725Z","id":"3955c22038dde74ddfeb83b21d8a04700ded7baa7c31200143a7f230a48def1e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a clip wider than 16:9 gets its own line at the panel's width, cropped to 16:9 from its left; threads_panel_test 'a wide clip gets its own line at the panel width, cropped to 16:9' passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_threads_panel_test), seen in target/flutter-app/shots/threads-panel-{phone,mac}-{light,dark}.png","supersedes":"ca36e7684571b03c837cb3c451e2f3a47de9b4884a593bbfbc3cbd40c9609e3d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:14:46.536787Z","id":"1d205f7730ae982b39984f3e5079ff76083ad6948b8179c63c90243c6efa3b7c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dee09e0f4304e7e401db6a4c82fcda157dbaaf9987cae6433a5b49ffc28037ca","summary":"comment_bar.dart's general comment is now ClaxButton(kind: ClaxButtonKind.tonal) (git:f1c07f346b12, test 'the hint says Click once a mouse is in use, and the general comment is a tonal button' in test/ui/comment_bar_test.dart). Left: settings_screen.dart, version_page.dart, build_plan.dart, change_sheet.dart (grep -rn FilledButton.tonal apps/clax_app/lib).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:18:44.517385Z","id":"211547bcd19d238ab0eeff72797f36aecc04f7f29e65b5097fd66b4411a8643c","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.5 says 'Saving warns that changes in progress will stop' and lists Versions under Home screen. Saving a key (_writeKey) stops nothing today: each make reads its backend when it starts (lib/app.dart _make, _s.backend(settings, _s.key)), so the warning would be untrue until saving does stop runs. HomeScreenControls has no versions action, so a Versions row needs one wired in lib/app.dart to the home app's version page. Notifications (Task 29) and Licences (showLicensePage) are added by other work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":393},"end":{"line":606},"content_hash":"7e06315f8f9095926cc2a5618eacb6cb6baf3aec21db5a9d4233414b0668bd0c"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether saving a key should stop changes in progress; add the warning only with that behaviour. Give HomeScreenControls a versions callback and show the row when it is set.","summary":"Settings lacks two rows §5.5 lists: the warning that saving a key stops changes in progress, and Home screen › Versions","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/theme.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:18:44.629567Z","id":"dfe4894e6d59dd74cb6c2fcbcb3965bae9e9d42b3a3c6422f961be01c40300d9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"347e1edb78a676a73de83c8a654cd1175e42b030c23251cde849b51b8d4ef519","summary":"settings_screen.dart's FilledButton.tonal (Save key) is now ClaxButton(kind: ClaxButtonKind.tonal), checked by 'the key field is a ClaxTextField' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/settings_test.dart (git:f1c07f346b12). Remaining sites: grep -rn FilledButton.tonal apps/clax_app/lib","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:30:38.112135Z","id":"937bb135d3c49eeb3bc22a50f2e0abe197cea40cb0aabedf1b5bcffb43af746f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: each tab reads what it shows (texts only when Files or Code first shows, collections on their own, icon.svg alone) and a failed read shows Try again in its tab alone; test/ui/app_inspector_test.dart 'the plain tabs read no file texts', 'a failed read of the files shows Try again in Files and Code alone, while Overview renders' and 'a failed read of the data shows Try again in Data alone' pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_inspector_test)","supersedes":"6eb839c54fb9e264a2b0e6898422dca6c0cfb373408fbe0e0a645e578c38e44d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
