{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:47:23.390172Z","id":"d28bd4d26152b608c97e6505b3a4a9597fbbc047a80f8138b0769c8e7559b13e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d8b4dc06325b9799a75954a613dc72b08856b8c04e8d2196b5f699d40e75396a","summary":"The start error's log (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/log_details.dart, used by error_screen.dart) now takes ClaxType.mono (git:f1c07f346b12). Left: bundle_sheets.dart and thread_detail.dart (grep -rn \"'monospace'\" apps/clax_app/lib/ui).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:47:23.390271Z","id":"d30c24e9e68f2020e277f5c0aa013e33edfb2e5600b6512bc4da488ad0a5cee5","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.6 names the actions Make it again and Cancel without saying what Cancel does. Closing the question (Escape, a tap outside, Back) keeps the make, so Cancel forgetting it keeps the only way to drop an interrupted make's tile.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1092},"end":{"line":1112},"content_hash":"3aa1ea2ec8a1776fc9b8bc45762bac73458975ab638c513458659f079eda6c83"},"summary":"Cancel on \"This wasn’t finished.\" forgets the interrupted make (as Discard did); it could instead only close the question","tags":["revisit:the tile gains its own Remove, or people lose makes by pressing Cancel","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:31.628878Z","id":"0f885bfcc3edbab8a0c477d4acdf0d4a4b8f7f3a74c9c30acf63fa93d0a4dfe7","body":{"detail":"BundleFlows.share (lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart) falls back to the screen's centre when its caller gives no origin. The inspector passes its Share button's rect (lib/ui/app_inspector.dart, shareAnchorOf); the home menu's Share app does not, since the tile's rect is not at hand in _act. On iPad its share popover points at the middle of the screen.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1243},"end":{"line":1244},"content_hash":"c15ff983fa0f07d472ced4e7fc7835e491d27c4660882076a58b025911d1477e"},"summary":"The home menu's Share app anchored at the tile rather than the screen's centre","tags":["ios","revisit:the home menu becomes a context menu anchored to its tile on iPad","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.125823Z","id":"2276971d4953ee03fa8c33562732e839fe08fa4c9d744a9e2af2a9af8094cb2e","body":{"detail":"Failure: send a comment, let the change fail (a limit stop from limitFailureReason('10 turns', leftUsd: 6), or any WorkerFailed), then tap the failed Working chip. The sheet's _sync (change_sheet.dart:203-208) copies ChangeTracker.threads, which after _endRunning (change_tracker.dart:383-389) is empty: threads returns running or _changes.keys (change_tracker.dart:156-157) and both were cleared, while the threads survive only in failedThreads. So _threads stays empty: 'What you asked' reads “Waiting for the comment…” (change_sheet.dart:325) and _actions builds no Open thread (change_sheet.dart:731-744), leaving Keep going/Retry as the only way on and no way to the reply with its Details. The committed render target/flutter-app/shots/change-sheet-limit-phone-light.png (from test/ui/shots/change_sheet_shots_test.dart:75-82) shows exactly this. test/ui/change_sheet_test.dart checks Open thread only while running (:105-110).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"1f9a1e4b5ea21d19572c251b7d03a9abcdf233d9b52215adbfff64ddcf5fc26f"},"suggested_fix":"Read _c.failedThreads when threads is empty and the outcome is failed or stopped (or have ChangeTracker.threads return _failed after a failure), and add a change_sheet_test case: failed change, sheet opened afterwards, finds change-open-thread and the person's comment.","summary":"A change sheet opened after a failure shows “Waiting for the comment…” for good and no Open thread: the tracker has already dropped the failed change's threads","tags":["review","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.125922Z","id":"2cf6dc70375199f70cc599dd366520a0db5eca093c808a02fb58ac759d942ebc","body":{"detail":"ChangeTracker.workerFailed stores 'Couldn’t make that change: $reason' as outcomeText (change_tracker.dart:313-316), and the sheet's failed header uses the literal title 'Couldn’t make that change' with that outcomeText as its line. The render change-sheet-limit-phone-light.png reads 'Couldn’t make that change' / 'Couldn’t make that change: it was too big for one go …'. The Working chip shows the same prefixed text (working_chip.dart:292-296).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"c9094ebe0217b704c74a0e3e88993e17685c5c0afc07091279415251748a02b3"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the bare reason in the tracker (or strip failurePrefix/its curly twin in the sheet's line) and capitalise it, as parseFailureReply does for the thread page.","summary":"The failed change sheet says “Couldn’t make that change” twice: the title, then the line under it opens with the same words","tags":["review","copy","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.125968Z","id":"adc086542cdbd079dfd35b54d0b4317e688c441302816dbb79723b20614c0d6c","body":{"detail":"A spent limit stop's text is keepGoingLine's 'It has used the $6 a change may cost, so it can’t keep going: reply with a smaller step.' (failure.dart:119-123), which offersKeepGoing does not match, so the sheet's button reads 'Retry' (change_sheet.dart:771-776) and the chip's too (working_chip.dart:274-280). The worker refuses it (worker.dart:1276: changeCapUsd - spentUsd < minKeepGoingUsd) and the tracker then reads 'Nothing to run again: reply in the thread.' (change_tracker.dart:286). The thread page hides Retry for the same reply through FailureReply.spentLimit (thread_detail.dart:1015). A primary, default Retry that cannot run anything is the opposite of what the thread page says.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":762},"end":{"line":777},"content_hash":"b5337d668faf37df262ad4ed73bfe6a47c607ba176a0549446aaddd81e1d8339"},"suggested_fix":"Give the sheet and chip the same test as the thread page (parseFailureReply(outcomeText).spentLimit, or a shared helper in failure.dart) and offer Open thread / Done instead.","summary":"The change sheet and the Working chip offer Retry on a limit stop that has spent the change's $6, where the thread page hides it; pressing it only says “Nothing to run again”","tags":["review","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126405Z","id":"bedc91e78d5b54373f5eaa19bbdfb8a18e0846f7be1c41887117619703c89c5e","body":{"detail":"Cancel in a dialog reads as 'do nothing'; §5.8 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md also says destructive actions are ClaxButton.destructive. Either label it 'Discard' as a destructive button (closing the dialog by Escape, a tap outside or Back leaving the make as it is), or keep 'Cancel' and make it only close the question. The spec's line '**Make it again** and Cancel' (§5.6) needs the owner's reading either way.","kind":"comment","references":"d30c24e9e68f2020e277f5c0aa013e33edfb2e5600b6512bc4da488ad0a5cee5","summary":"Judged a defect, not an alternative: at f1c07f346b12 the dialog's plain, non-destructive 'Cancel' calls host.makes.dismiss(s), so a person who presses Cancel to back out loses their request with no undo","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126489Z","id":"8e1d5f84af8a6fc98f174092f9b2f28464c72bef0085278ea906194dacb26951","body":{"detail":"f1c07f346b12 records name at pick time (web/bridge, Anchor.name) and the shell's anchorLabel uses it (web/shell/src/app/label.ts:105-119). The Dart fallback anchorWords reads only label/quote, then 'this area'/'this spot'. It is used by the thread page whenever ThreadDetail gets no label (thread_detail.dart:642-644) and by the change sheet's thread card (change_sheet.dart:494-498), so a thread on <button aria-label=\"Save\"> reads 'This spot' there and '“Save”' in the threads panel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":69},"content_hash":"9cdb583fb3688867038e207d443b8daa70328bba9730419fae70cf864d6ce572"},"suggested_fix":"Read anchor['name'] after the quote (with the 'Kind under ‘heading’' form the shell parses), and fall back to 'A spot on the page' to match the shell's wording.","summary":"anchorWords ignores Anchor.name, so where the shell gives no label the app titles a named pick “this spot”","tags":["review","copy","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/read_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126626Z","id":"ecedaf2a1aaf893847952790145108ce1a38a5a840cf554581d2ccb4636159a2","body":{"detail":"ClaxDialog.ask's suppression checkbox turns the 'Allow once' answer into ConsentAnswer.always and memory.allow (:165-168). The person presses a button labelled 'once' and gets a standing grant; nothing on the dialog says the label changed meaning. The Mac's NSAlert suppression box usually reads 'Don’t ask again' for this reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"0acb1519ad5ed1f59af3988a26537b3d6d1329205758bc996eda50fd2b33c442"},"suggested_fix":"Relabel the primary 'Allow' while the box is ticked, or word the box so the pair reads true ('Don’t ask again for this app').","summary":"With “Always for this app” ticked, the button still says “Allow once” but grants always","tags":["review","copy","consent","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126702Z","id":"11880fb4160a6ba28d63f99c9af4ff1579347e89537a2cea6d0bbe25e74a07ec","body":{"detail":"For an installed app the person changed, the buttons read 'Share mine with my data' (four words; §5.8 caps labels at three) and 'Share Alex’s v2', the subtitle 'Yours goes as v1 · 5 files, 20 KB', and the body '… since Alex’s v2. “Share Alex’s v2” sends theirs …' (render bundle-export-modified-phone-light.png). §7.2's glossary says 'version 4' in prose, 'v4' only in tight badges; 'Yours goes as v1' also reads as a downgrade.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":390},"content_hash":"d5050696f5beb8a8c4f82d222ce2014d446e914ea6869849bb563f7b54507a20"},"suggested_fix":"E.g. 'Share mine', 'With my data', 'Share theirs', and a body 'You changed Plant log since Alex’s version 2 …'; subtitle 'Shared as a new app · 5 files'.","summary":"The modified export sheet breaks §5.8 and §7.2: a four-word label and v-numbers in prose","tags":["review","copy","phase-3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:41:37.318674Z","id":"1985a6a3b10057b958b41d1f92905231badc681ce76fb0777df7533d821e19e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: anchorWords reads the quote, a custom name, Anchor.name (quoted when it is the page's words, plain as 'Chart under “p95”' when a kind word), the element's tag kind word, then 'A spot on the page' / 'Area on the page', as web/shell/src/app/label.ts anchorLabel does. Test 'anchorWords reads the quote, then the name, then a kind word' in test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_thread_detail_test).","supersedes":"8e1d5f84af8a6fc98f174092f9b2f28464c72bef0085278ea906194dacb26951","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:41:37.367794Z","id":"ba6b7b9cd281c35bd6bed9668d4b4ba86034a099484e3283c88e3269e2df954a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d8b4dc06325b9799a75954a613dc72b08856b8c04e8d2196b5f699d40e75396a","summary":"thread_detail.dart's failure details now take ClaxType.mono (git:f1c07f346b12). Left: bundle_sheets.dart:840 (grep -rn \"'monospace'\" apps/clax_app/lib/ui).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:41:37.367952Z","id":"165804ecc39e4f48a881cff9ef35150bba9b69e13b1ee2097d032d3b46eb46d9","body":{"detail":"ClaxScaffold (lib/ui/kit/scaffold.dart) draws the subtitle with maxLines: 1. Seen in target/flutter-app/shots/inbox-thread-waiting-phone-light-130.png from test/ui/shots/inbox_shots_test.dart: 'On the chart under “p95 by four-hour wi…' with no version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"7a022c4448b48c731a0b0d626cc6410c9ec71b4d8fc1bf57c468bcb5aa884e25"},"suggested_fix":"Let ClaxScaffold's subtitle take two lines on compact widths, or draw the anchor and the version as two ellipsized parts so the version is always kept.","summary":"The thread subtitle is one line, so at 130% and 200% text on a 412 dp phone a long anchor still pushes 'Version N' past the ellipsis, even after the 48-character cut","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:41:37.368025Z","id":"118d52b32c3268b673c69f9b20e421160086e0847cacafdcd85ae1e2e464e0c6","body":{"detail":"anchorWords and threadSubtitle tell the app's kind words from page names by this set. Nothing checks the two lists agree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":73},"content_hash":"230d28f8366cdfe112fe1890079ce3ac3be4c88f7f81ca5f78460ecf558dd546"},"suggested_fix":"Add a check (like //design:tokens_sync) that the Dart map equals protocol.ts's KIND_WORDS, or generate it.","summary":"_kindOf copies KIND_WORDS from web/bridge/src/protocol.ts by hand; a word added there reads as the page's own words (quoted) in the app's fallback titles","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:41:37.368086Z","id":"fe65f11c0e6ea980dda177e8e987669cb9e73be081b0200eceadfabe1fc50a13","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"eaea79d27241df1c3d9b77e2066b89eecf6be204a29534d50fdc8aca563bb255"},"summary":"Changes is read as the kinds version, published and finished; replies show only under All and Unread. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.4 names the chips but not what Changes holds.","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:42:16.409822Z","id":"4e42a129e6755f969e971b63d74d4dbf7996486071f38daa0276bc6cc7bd6222","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","references":"1985a6a3b10057b958b41d1f92905231badc681ce76fb0777df7533d821e19e9","summary":"The fix this close cites is git:f1c07f346b12, not git:f1c07f346b12: that commit was replaced on the branch (by f1c07f346b12, without these files) before the fix landed again as f1c07f346b12. The test 'anchorWords reads the quote, then the name, then a kind word' passes there (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_thread_detail_test).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:42:37.711090Z","id":"6d394e8120bb9058ad65cdf165e465440212e1eb8761bf33a10fe9b8c3e323de","body":{"detail":"lib/ui/kit/banner.dart draws the Apple family as a full-width inline bar with a hairline under it, meant for the top of a pane. The launcher wraps each banner in EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(16, 0, 16, 8) for the Material card, which the Mac form keeps (render: target/flutter-app/shots/launcher-banners-mac-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_screens_shots_test). The split layout (plan Task 46) is where the Mac banner's place gets settled.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":813},"end":{"line":815},"content_hash":"66d7206fab7750b0285d55fde5a68cff1848311e91bc005cfbddad1903e29361"},"summary":"On the Mac the key and recovery banners draw ClaxBanner's Apple bar inside the launcher's 16 dp side padding, so the bar is inset rather than the pane's full width under the toolbar","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.315420Z","id":"c33d0e5a1743f4ca563cab7776478214d5d41ef9ee1fe37ff4350da5d8328235","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: ChangeTracker.ended keeps a failed or stopped change's threads and the sheet reads them. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_change_sheet_test passes 'after the change ends a failed / limit-stopped / spent / stopped change shows what was asked and Open thread' (failing before the fix with “Waiting for the comment…” found); change-sheet-limit-phone-light.png now shows the comment and Open thread.","supersedes":"2276971d4953ee03fa8c33562732e839fe08fa4c9d744a9e2af2a9af8094cb2e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.384406Z","id":"f58f4173835ed3c2c3c603e4b187f73a50ab7a46a00e3740d0b5361838d7947a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the failed sheet's line is parseFailureReply(outcomeText).line. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_change_sheet_test passes 'a failure says “Couldn’t make that change” once' (line starts 'It was too big for one go'); it failed before with 2 matches. The Working chip keeps the prefixed text: it has no title to repeat.","supersedes":"2cf6dc70375199f70cc599dd366520a0db5eca093c808a02fb58ac759d942ebc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.449555Z","id":"665b459741deeba8a3d1ddfdb2efb46c277579d3efbe7f8a09c03cac44a41fa1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the sheet and the Working chip offer no Retry when parseFailureReply(outcomeText).spentLimit. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_change_sheet_test ('a limit stop that spent the change’s limit offers Done, not Retry') and //apps/clax_app:ui_working_chip_test ('a limit stop that spent the change’s limit offers no Retry') pass; both failed before the fix.","supersedes":"adc086542cdbd079dfd35b54d0b4317e688c441302816dbb79723b20614c0d6c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/read_consent_dialog.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.511785Z","id":"0e75fef35103b26d9977f56354cc71dc327d11ab7973388ac4b1e2a5d5c5f2e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: ClaxDialogAction.suppressedLabel; the consent's primary reads 'Always allow' while 'Always for this app' is ticked (layout restored in f1c07f346b12). bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_read_consent_dialog_test passes 'Always is remembered for the pair' and 'unticking Always puts Allow once back', which failed before; consent-read-always-{phone,wide,mac}-{light,dark}.png show it.","supersedes":"ecedaf2a1aaf893847952790145108ce1a38a5a840cf554581d2ccb4636159a2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.574584Z","id":"7b46a14d43f3385305b43111111a39f3ecc1e458a325988d6e2e50e88ea3a156","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a changed copy's export sheet reads Share theirs / With my data / Share mine (Export on the Mac), subtitle 'Shared as a new app · 5 files, 20 KB', body 'since Alex’s version 2'. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_sheets_test passes 'a modified copy … in labels of three words at most' (checks every label ≤ 3 words and no v<N> in text); failed before. bundle-export-modified-*.png rendered.","supersedes":"11880fb4160a6ba28d63f99c9af4ff1579347e89537a2cea6d0bbe25e74a07ec","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:02:15.528264Z","id":"27be3f5ce19ead7cfc4d807615cb533c5a4b3591aa47b39bc8235f69fe1a556d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d30c24e9e68f2020e277f5c0aa013e33edfb2e5600b6512bc4da488ad0a5cee5","summary":"Changed in f1c07f346b12: the dialog's buttons are Make it again (primary) and Discard (destructive, which forgets the make), so no button reads Cancel; Escape, a tap outside and Back keep the make. test/app_background_test.dart 'Discard forgets the lost make; closing the question keeps it' covers a tap outside, Escape and Discard.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:02:15.528523Z","id":"a00b26c51b65be813034e197a1ef58beddbc9c9de8defa85205e21a6abc36129","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: Cancel is now Discard (destructive), and closing the question keeps the make. Evidence: `flutter test test/app_background_test.dart --plain-name 'lost make'` at f1c07f346b12 -> 'Discard forgets the lost make; closing the question keeps it' +1: All tests passed!","supersedes":"d30c24e9e68f2020e277f5c0aa013e33edfb2e5600b6512bc4da488ad0a5cee5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/user_message.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:02:15.575641Z","id":"3ce95e7a8f505394a46fbd92fe506bac86c71b5e240aceeadf502ad2ca7438b0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: userMessage maps an AgentError carrying a raw report (Claude API error (HTTP …), mid-answer errors, claude's own reports, unreadable answers, other exceptions' text) to 'Claude couldn’t answer just now. Try again.', an unreachable or network-kind one to a connection line, a timeout to 'That took too long'; rawError keeps the raw text. Evidence: `bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_user_message_test` at f1c07f346b12 -> PASSED, including 'an AgentError carrying a raw backend report reads as Claude not answering, and the raw text stays for the log'.","supersedes":"c83850ea9921223bdfd5983b0e01c4a00e13e1ce849e36c2c2cbc9061016cc3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:26:08.477540Z","id":"3dcf2d95f2df29f944d41589aeaba9679d44848ed330c3b2e490f714bc9dc4e0","body":{"detail":"Seen in the simulator screenshot open-bundle.png that //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_open_bundle writes (bazel-testlogs/apps/clax_app/integration_ios_open_bundle/test.outputs/, Clax iPhone, iPhone 17 at iOS 26.5): the action bar's buttons are cut by the bottom of the screen. _Frame's column ends with ClaxActionBar and adds no bottom safe-area inset; whether the sheet route adds one on iOS was not checked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"5bfc06b749920e96216b927d67a5beeffef255fdd959793e77210e5ee1944be9"},"suggested_fix":"Pad the sheet's content by MediaQuery.viewPaddingOf(context).bottom (or wrap it in SafeArea(top: false)) and look at the screenshot again.","summary":"On iPhone the install sheet's Cancel and Install buttons sit at the screen's bottom edge, partly under the home indicator","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:36:42.744700Z","id":"aaa66402d6ff6400b4a998cba800373864708bac0ef5da33d1e7913fcb1a55d4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b1224ce3f13c186dcd9c4661a06ebc3","summary":"The cut-off buttons were a shot taken mid-slide: //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_open_bundle took open-bundle.png the frame the sheet's route was pushed. Settled, the sheet already clears the bottom inset (ClaxSheet's _SheetBody pads by max(viewInsets, viewPadding).bottom, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart:159-170). The test now waits for the route (IosRig.routeIn) and asserts Cancel and Install end above the bottom view padding; it passed on Clax iPhone (iPhone 17, iOS 26.5) and its open-bundle.png shows both buttons clear of the home indicator. //apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_sheets_test 'on iOS/Android at 100%/200% Cancel and Install clear the bottom inset' passes (34 pt home indicator, 48 dp bar).","supersedes":"3dcf2d95f2df29f944d41589aeaba9679d44848ed330c3b2e490f714bc9dc4e0","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/system_bands.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:15.037201Z","id":"256d6b4cf3fa574921548283f738133ddd6f92926b05c3fe7a26533199c35f2b","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/ui/system_bands_test.dart and app_screen_test.dart 'edge to edge' check the bands' rectangles and colours and SystemChrome.latestStyle; target/flutter-app/shots/app-phone-*.png and app-dark-page-phone-*.png (test/ui/shots/app_shots_test.dart) show them with stand-in bars. Not checked: drawEdgeToEdge (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:69) on API 29-34, where the system may still draw a scrim under three-button navigation; the icons' brightness following the AnnotatedRegions as the page's colours change; a display cutout in landscape; and the real WebView's elementFromPoint at y 0 under the band.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"438c57a2463f2330b8f2199a5843a9e84472e2abaf30b658b45c7166041f84b3"},"suggested_fix":"On a phone, gesture and three-button navigation, light and dark: open an app with a dark header and a white tab bar, scroll it, and confirm the bands and icons follow.","summary":"Edge to edge and the page-coloured bands are checked by widget tests and renders only, not on an Android phone","tags":["device","unverified","phase:8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:52:58.151665Z","id":"8631eba30d7c9e67489aa5e167703563d7dd3c8de0d9dcc049428dae7589b958","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: HomeFlows._act passes the menu's anchor, the long-pressed tile's global rect, to BundleFlows.share as its origin (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart, case 'share-app'); //apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_entry_points_test and :home_home_menu_test pass (bazelisk test)","supersedes":"0f885bfcc3edbab8a0c477d4acdf0d4a4b8f7f3a74c9c30acf63fa93d0a4dfe7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/ai_consent_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:55:47.316758Z","id":"0b394a782a214a8a3beb9a1bf2b502ed4059e81a7284c095e1e82d83100d014b","body":{"detail":"showAiConsentSheet goes through ClaxSheet.show, which at compact width is showModalBottomSheet sized to its content, with Not now and Allow as push buttons at the end of one row (target/flutter-app/shots/consent-ai-iphone-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_consent_shots_test). The iOS spec §7.1 gives ClaxSheet detents and a grabber, and ClaxButton a 50 pt primary at the bottom of a sheet; once ClaxSheet and ClaxButton have that idiom this sheet takes it with no change of its own, and its renders should be looked at again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"8d81cba635dff4321154814105c3f32b9caafc7889cdbd2ad674f02ed4c32e5f"},"summary":"On iPhone the AI consent sheet is the kit's compact bottom sheet, not a medium-detent sheet with a 50 pt full-width Allow","tags":["ios","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:34:40.433870Z","id":"0866747170b89edfe143c4e327e37c349a97b1b5ff642cb0ad8dbbc396540a89","body":{"detail":"_pillState gives ClaxPillState.working for any change in flight (ChangeTracker.working), and ClaxPill.label for working is 'Working' (lib/ui/working_chip.dart). Before the pill, the Working chip's step line read 'Waiting for connection' (ChangeTracker adds that step on WaitingForConnection). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 lists only Working, Building, New version and Location, so a person offline sees Working until they open the sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"16434150ad58fd6e11057f1bfa47ac79f3f050dff721c5951285ed319a14416c"},"suggested_fix":"A fifth pill state (or the working state's label) for ChangeTracker.waitingForConnection, if the owner wants it on the pill.","summary":"The pill says Working while a change waits for the connection; only the change sheet and the thread page say Waiting for connection","tags":["ux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:34:40.434021Z","id":"242f96cc2cc22a10fb0a52a636c318aa69cece03a5fe7f4268e88d9850c9af1e","body":{"detail":"_pillState orders working, building, newVersion, then location, one state at a time, and a toast of the screen hides the pill. Android 12 and later still show their own location indicator in the status bar; before Android 12 nothing of Clax's says so while the pill says something else.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"16434150ad58fd6e11057f1bfa47ac79f3f050dff721c5951285ed319a14416c"},"summary":"Location in use is the pill's last state: while a change, a build or a new version shows, the pill does not say location is in use","tags":["privacy","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:34:40.434102Z","id":"b613e3968e2814988d5b35579224b0adf98924c3df87f9ab664f3c2deec686e9","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 gives the hint's two lines for notifications off ('Turn on notifications to comment from the shade.' with Turn on) and refused ('Use the Comment tab on the right to comment.'). With notifications already on, _hintCard says 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.' with only the dismiss button. Until Task 29 adds the Comment tab, the refused line points at the edge handle's place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2157},"end":{"line":2175},"content_hash":"84de059562f7b0880d7b880b5c1366f99a106ade4242a46dcad75e6d0617d247"},"summary":"The first-run hint's line with notifications on, 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.', is not in the spec","tags":["copy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:34:40.434215Z","id":"08d98af838521a0a053a9c20d007c31a481eeaffd153bccf839de2489aafd937","body":{"detail":"The pill is fg (#1C1B19 light) at level 2, as §5.2 asks; over a dark header such as #102A4C (target/flutter-app/shots/app-working-phone-light.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_app_shots_test) the circle folded to the mark has little edge against the page. The dark theme's level 2 outline (borderHover) gives it an edge there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":520},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"4e39546c8558b1c881048b345b1b047d43c2de4b82a1f2d1647027d2136a657f"},"suggested_fix":"A hairline ring in bg at low opacity, or the dark theme's outline, around the pill in the light theme.","summary":"In the light theme the pill's fg fill sits close to a dark page header, so it stands out from it by its shadow and words only","tags":["ux","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:35:19.698113Z","id":"5e63db723d3ef576089c027f5326286a1c0add1457141493abac74c44751a478","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the first-run hint offers Turn on with notifications off (AppNoticeSlot.turnOn: Android's POST_NOTIFICATIONS request while it may still ask, else Clax's notification settings), and after a refusal points at the Comment tab. 'with notifications off the hint offers Turn on…', 'a refused Turn on points at the Comment tab' and both settings tests in apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test); the Kotlin compiles (bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:apk). Device check: record 09ce55aa.","supersedes":"2521833ce54c328d42580dca6a4a3fd2a56ac2af72f370c86e4dc1a8235e254c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:35:19.766924Z","id":"7db0ff06f74c27a5140f34244c874205c83a9732d4eab7b78a9a1fce695838de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: _restore holds New version offers (_reloading) until its reload's Ready or Landed, and a failed restore offers what the shell offered once its toast goes. 'Undo and Restore wait for their own reload' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test).","supersedes":"93b32b9ec250e49d0041f492440b872ff36cebb9fe20486097687ea65246114a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:35:19.833880Z","id":"cb587e4755fe9dfdd6351e3247976c4b0923216b96f654c45fa57ec8012a1216","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the Working chip shows keepGoingIn(outcomeText, ClaxVerbs.of(context)). 'a limit stop says Keep going in the pointer’s words' in apps/clax_app/test/ui/working_chip_test.dart passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_working_chip_test).","supersedes":"7dd01921672ed730d4f9ca7ee53adf4a3e7bb1d0c6861dac3da03d06a17a545f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/ask_prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:37:01.453501Z","id":"aff42bbc057135fb5ccd53f509c3dd93a7fcd3b7834a293a79f15babe4ca9c36","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:ui_ask_prompt_test and //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_ask_test drive AskPrompt and AppScreen with a fake surface; //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_ask_prompt_shots_test renders it on phone, wide and iPhone. Not yet seen: the shell posting ask over the real WebView channel after init names it native, the answer reaching native.ts, askCancel on a version change, and the WebView giving up keyboard focus so Return and Space reach the Flutter route. On the Mac ClaxDialog.ask shows an NSAlert sheet instead (f1c07f346b12).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"51fc2662fd1417ac65badf62b19f1795dd8cec4efe41fafd9843316d9e017b16"},"summary":"The native permission prompt is verified in widget tests and renders only, not in a running app on Android or iOS","tags":["unverified","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_tab.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T09:44:24.381758Z","id":"7b66779e017ba04675b711e140449ea9b22d09f7ba74f0d2aa11a4e3e04f6405","body":{"detail":"comment_tab_test sets systemGestureInsets.right to 32 dp and app_shots_test to 24 dp; no phone has shown that MediaQuery.systemGestureInsetsOf reports the zone at each gesture-sensitivity setting, nor that a back swipe beside the tab no longer opens it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"7af560aec7a66412250974410655f23373cff6ec44b9f1e49b8148fe21df2065"},"summary":"The Comment tab's place outside the back-gesture zone is checked only with FakeViewPadding in widget tests and renders","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:01:41.329112Z","id":"1292065b484d200f66cde0c2c567e3d05dbecf1f53b3d0ad5d9c015308699cf9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the WebView /inbox page (question_sheet.dart) is gone; QuestionsSheet (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/questions/questions_sheet.dart) draws the questions natively, read and answered through the daemon, with no shell chrome or links. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_questions_sheet_test //apps/clax_app:app_test //apps/clax_app:app_background_test: PASSED.","supersedes":"6a28a0de6ae07209a5522f3e2011683537545899b98749a4388523d993975740","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:15:30.896777Z","id":"b74e83e276c3ba87bd6adbbfc004287722a0bd74648ea457a232e70ff362578f","body":{"detail":"_withBanners puts the 48 dp ClaxBanner in a bg strip above the page, which shrinks by the strip's height (about 64 dp on a phone) while an agent drafts or its draft shows. Laid over the page it would cover the page's heading for as long as the draft lasts, the defect record 8cded220 describes for the web banner (web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte), so it moved to the foot of the stage there. The cost of pushing is a WebView resize when the banner comes and goes. Renders: target/flutter-app/shots from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_native_overlays_shots_test (app-drafting-*, app-draft-showing-*).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2227},"end":{"line":2259},"content_hash":"068ba2dbc9394339e9f09289d1334f954baff4ec83f03c2394a9c3418341765a"},"summary":"The native draft banner laid over the page's top, as the Clax pill and top toasts are, instead of pushing the page down","tags":["revisit:the draft banner's resize of the page shows as a jump or reflow on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:15:30.943270Z","id":"41d2fe3677a25800dcb2597ba9beb7f2d96b7cb27db58ffead23d0ea96527975","body":{"detail":"_notice shows each notice through _showToast (toastFor, 4 s on the screen's clock); only with a screen reader on does a toast with an action stay. The shell's one notice with an action, a failed follow of the latest version with Try again (web/shell/src/app/native.ts:96-99), is then gone after 4 s and the person cannot retry from it; the shell posts the same notice text again only after it changes (lastNotice). Also, a notice that comes while the screen is not in front (_toldVisible not true) is dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1077},"end":{"line":1090},"content_hash":"545fe3321664079f13733b70be00ac6ddac045b2186439d7873872d027c52881"},"summary":"A native shell notice goes after 4 s like any toast, while the web notice banner stayed until the shell cleared it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/comment_bar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:16:29.037539Z","id":"35381b3d63c1e4bc467d4c67c0ee37961cc2674bd0ce6ba77f8bd6567bbc2222","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.3 names only 'Tap anything to comment on it'. With 48 dp controls in one row, below about 340 dp at 130% text (or at 200%) the full sentence cannot keep whole words in the bar's height, so CommentBar shows '${verbs.tap} to comment' (comment_bar_test 'fits at 320 dp and text scale 1.3'). Renders: target/flutter-app/shots/app-comment-bar-phone-*-200.png.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"c70b71745e9386786d62e1f5e7cb88c693471e196319b4540d8c5e3d627459c7"},"summary":"The bar's last fallback, 'Tap to comment', is copy the spec does not name","tags":["copy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:22:16.105227Z","id":"f18418ba85516f2866fa844b615b80b53cb97840d3d97ef1695e940950595d46","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppScreen holds the latest shell notice (_heldNotice); one with an action or error tone shows with ClaxToast.show(stays: true), which has no timeout and a close button, and stays until its action, its close, or the next notice; it comes back after another of the screen's toasts over it goes and when the screen returns to front, and a notice that came while the screen was not in front shows then. Info notices still go after toastFor. Tests: apps/clax_app/test/ui/native_overlays_test.dart group 'notices' (12 passed via flutter test); bazelisk test //apps/clax_app/... and the web/design/copy lanes: 193 tests pass.","supersedes":"41d2fe3677a25800dcb2597ba9beb7f2d96b7cb27db58ffead23d0ea96527975","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:22:16.140305Z","id":"9485e93d0e980d25902ba680090055a3cca84e7e6ceae32bb86615d53caf5985","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":534},"end":{"line":535},"content_hash":"aff59d5de2775e59560d1a2bb69cbe30239e5a3cbfb5155d07f581a1053bb892"},"summary":"The Clax pill is hidden the whole time a shell notice that stays is up","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:22:24.520543Z","id":"2287426edba0be84298efa97ee897eddd008c2733240c4211b41ea4a95159c0f","body":{"detail":"_pillState returns null while _toastUp is set. A shell notice with an action or error tone (AppScreen._stays) now shows with ClaxToast.show(stays: true) and stays until Try again, its close button or the next notice, so while a failed follow's notice waits the pill does not say Working, Building or New version. A New version toast that the notice replaced is offered again only once the notice goes (_offerNewer waits on ClaxToast.current.closed).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":534},"end":{"line":535},"content_hash":"aff59d5de2775e59560d1a2bb69cbe30239e5a3cbfb5155d07f581a1053bb892"},"suggested_fix":"Let the pill show beside a notice that stays (place it clear of the notice card), or show the notice's state in the pill.","summary":"The Clax pill is hidden the whole time a shell notice that stays is up","supersedes":"9485e93d0e980d25902ba680090055a3cca84e7e6ceae32bb86615d53caf5985","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.740107Z","id":"f07a03db68776f736f6cce9f780a0ff5593eb9689cb15b79817e047326881115","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: Back to Apps is gone; App › Back (⌘[) steps the page's history (the app screen's PopScope sends GoBack) before leaving the screen, and App › Home (⇧⌘H) pops to the grid. Both are MainMenu.xib key equivalents, which work while the WebView has the focus. test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'App › Back steps the page’s history (GoBack) before leaving the screen' and 'App › Home goes to the grid from two screens deep' pass, and macos_app_test checks the compiled items (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_menu_test //apps/clax_app:macos_app_test: PASSED). That the keys reach the menu in a running app is the open record on apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/EditBridge.swift.","supersedes":"32f8f89d4048214e8c13b6cfbbb6fc2be52efdcb4e41f63b02f868bed02e9fbc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.787375Z","id":"b2268398581fac3a8dc77b4fa81b883b6eb099febeaef56a59660bf20a10b7d4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: File › Import App… (⌘O) is in MainMenu.xib (tag 2) and runs the home screen's HomeActions.importApp through ClaxMenuBar. test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'File › New App…, Import App… and Window › Inbox run the home screen’s flows' passes; macos_app_test checks 'File › Import App… | ⌘O | claxMenuAction: 2' in the compiled nib (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_menu_test //apps/clax_app:macos_app_test: PASSED).","supersedes":"128c1f7ff7c8037153cc9b6229882f36d77e497b62cff806d90e666e82cb8628","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:12:10.832795Z","id":"6b9a1d036613d848981ca5aba209260dbff608ebf341e13709946d7d1e0b68bd","body":{"detail":"_handler maps only Settings, New App, Import App, Inbox, Comment, Show Threads, Back and Home; every other menu command answers null, so ClaxMenuBar sends setEnabled false. ClaxMenuBar.titles and MacMenu.setTitle exist, but AppRoot passes no titles: View › Show Threads reads 'Show Threads' while the panel is open, because CommentsCommand (lib/ui/app_menu.dart) does not know whether it is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"d568b197b30d15a37e7d1c2df0b0790960ac66bad6563ef568deb8a6b2f05592"},"suggested_fix":"Wire each command where its surface lands (the split layout's sidebar and selection, the toolbar, the app screen's reload and zoom), and give CommentsCommand the panel's open state for the title.","summary":"Share App…, Show Sidebar, Reload App, Actual Size, Zoom In, Zoom Out, Forward, Inspect, Versions…, Star and Resume Build stay disabled, and no item's title flips (Show/Hide Sidebar, Show/Hide Threads, Star/Unstar)","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:37:08.808644Z","id":"dde41e41a02dd37024a1a08bbb0a8cf3575559b9a1711d8903ccfe00f9d8e4b4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"098fa2674ee5a04b2ce6ddf57ff7b631804febce9c41fb4a03c79151f1c3e1bc","summary":"On macOS the window now takes Escape from a page's WKWebView while the app screen has the comment bar, the panel, the composer or the questions sheet up (_escapeCloses, reported by _reportEscape through MacWindow.setEscapeWanted) and the screen closes the top one (WindowBridge.escape in apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift). Checked by test/ui/app_screen_test.dart ('an Escape it catches from the page closes them') and macos/RunnerTests/WindowBridgeTests.swift; unverified with a real key press in the built app.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:32:45.961334Z","id":"3c020e348256b96d2916041c9d099dabe171b77b827722283df9276243c6dbe8","body":{"detail":"The launcher is not a ClaxScaffold: its SliverAppBar takes the window's top padding (the row's height, from ClaxViews) like a status bar, so it starts below the row. Nothing overlaps the window buttons (test/ui/mac/traffic_lights_test.dart checks it; target/flutter-app/mac/launcher.png shows it), but the window has 52 points of empty chrome above the launcher's own bar. version_page.dart, app_inspector.dart and app_inspector_code.dart's AppBars are the same.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"e3a569af4d9261102960ebb7d3d90a8239b62e2f31fc0679d92effb153020146"},"suggested_fix":"Move these screens onto ClaxScaffold, or give their bars the row on the Mac as ClaxScaffold's _MacHeader does.","summary":"On the Mac the launcher's SliverAppBar sits below the toolbar row, which stays empty beside the window buttons, unlike ClaxScaffold screens whose bar is that row","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:37:28.651561Z","id":"ea3fb7b376d40bc561c1df0e6dfe5a75b03d351ed7646a7e09f1c42fa423a0bd","body":{"detail":"A change asks for a Keep going press after its second stop before the planning run (lib/agent/worker.dart retry); a make starts that planning run itself (MakeSession catch of MakeStopped, when MakeStopped.plansNext and not planned and the $6 budget allows), so the person presses Keep going once and the plan and build take over. It spends up to RunCaps.first.costUsd without a press. A planning run that itself stops without a clean render waits for a press again, so it never loops.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"36c8074a1e220434f2939f75888c271d54e0171e9e6de3ba078930471134dbeb"},"summary":"After a new app's second stop at a limit the make goes on by itself, once, with the run told to plan the rest","tags":["status:needs-decision","keep-going","make","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:37:28.651684Z","id":"5920b083d568e03c1086eaa465211799be5a7f51c818d7b7dd4964cd905c7569","body":{"detail":"Retry next to Keep going reads as the same thing, so the stop state names it Start over (it runs the request from the start and forgets the kept draft; MakeSession.start). A failed make keeps its Retry label (_failed). With the $6 spent, Start over becomes the primary action.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1370},"end":{"line":1380},"content_hash":"426cb687aac85d91705927656ec237ded11718d3cb94ea2f5dd163e0219a95a1"},"summary":"A stopped make's Retry is labelled Start over, and is a plain button beside Keep going","tags":["status:needs-decision","copy","make","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:24.066233Z","id":"cc194284c155d0e8c1f119e7c32be9128cc71409019468dc24a011b5725dfef2","body":{"detail":"HistoryMsg (lib/ui/host_protocol.dart) carries `back` only and there is no GoForward call, so docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.4's Forward (page history, then the app selection) has nothing to act on. Giving it one is a contract change (docs/contract.md, web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, the kit's fake host, the prompt copies).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":958},"end":{"line":1000},"content_hash":"96bb29e729ed8ff4504ce22c170013ee94b1ca82ed8c8ff43775d8be0e2fd1a9"},"summary":"The toolbar's Forward is always disabled: the shell's history message reports only whether the page can go back","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:24.066318Z","id":"e6f6fb7b0c71ab8e4ebb454897a9dab4c755ade2d06029eb5912e3b545bd874a","body":{"detail":"The sidebar and its search arrive with the split layout (plan Tasks 46 and 47); Working opens the change popover and New Version replaces the pill's state, so the pill keeps both until those items exist. ToolbarItemSpec and Toolbar.swift take any SF Symbol item; NSSearchToolbarItem and a custom working item are not built.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":958},"end":{"line":1000},"content_hash":"96bb29e729ed8ff4504ce22c170013ee94b1ca82ed8c8ff43775d8be0e2fd1a9"},"summary":"The toolbar carries Back/Forward, the title, Comment, Threads and Share; §4.4's Toggle sidebar, Working, New Version and Search items are not declared yet, and the Clax pill stays over the page on the Mac","tags":["macos","revisit:the split layout's sidebar lands (plan Task 46)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/version_page.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:24.066372Z","id":"db3a0c6b89ba86dfcb72aac3d653d0288dec7860c7f83ecde106c1f97049702e","body":{"detail":"lib/ui/version_page.dart:329 and :712, lib/ui/app_inspector.dart:223, :1268 and :1358, and lib/ui/app_inspector_code.dart:317 are AppBars under the window's top padding. The launcher's bar now sits in the row (lib/ui/launcher.dart, test/ui/mac/traffic_lights_test.dart); these screens do not. The row still moves the window (WindowRowDrag).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":329},"end":{"line":329},"content_hash":"8950ec2baebb97276cf8758db1f8e1851dbc21d78bc192e1570b42984ffb7c3e"},"suggested_fix":"Move them onto ClaxScaffold, or give their AppBars the row as the launcher's SliverAppBar does (primary: false, toolbarHeight and titleSpacing from WindowTitlebar).","summary":"On the Mac the version page, the inspector and its code and data pages keep a Material AppBar below the toolbar row, which stays empty beside the window buttons","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:39:35.502998Z","id":"929f2098eef6d9bca5aee221a8a55609edf25bd019569335a62eed1f2ca2a79f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed for the launcher: its SliverAppBar is the toolbar row on the Mac, the title after the window buttons and its actions centred with them; 'the launcher keeps out of the window buttons corner, its bar in the row' (light and dark) in test/ui/mac/traffic_lights_test.dart failed before (title at 80, not 26) and passes: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_mac_traffic_lights_test PASSED. The version page and inspector AppBars it also named are record 443fd67b.","supersedes":"3c020e348256b96d2916041c9d099dabe171b77b827722283df9276243c6dbe8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.231361Z","id":"07a9143420d2da6759be9672d729051daf777bd17a24085b818a45746bba8ff5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e6f6fb7b0c71ab8e4ebb454897a9dab4c755ade2d06029eb5912e3b545bd874a","summary":"The split window's sidebar toggle is now declared: SplitShell leads the window's toolbar with it (MacToolbar.setLeading, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart). Working, New Version and Search are still not declared, so the Clax pill keeps both states over the page on the Mac.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.231579Z","id":"f5975aa4902b931d162e5040bb2f6a4b139a0b0f3ade163e183d7dc74b355ae9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6b9a1d036613d848981ca5aba209260dbff608ebf341e13709946d7d1e0b68bd","summary":"View › Show Sidebar is enabled while a split window shows, and its title flips to Hide Sidebar and back (ClaxMenuBar.toggleSidebar and titles, set from apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart; test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'View › Show Sidebar runs the split window's toggle'). The other items this record lists stay as it says.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:40:45.918423Z","id":"4fd19903d2f20588e3536816caf815a45db1c6c4ca3d28815b536e0fd23bde32","body":{"detail":"The toolbar item shows whatever the pill says (the pill puts Working, Building and New version before Location and folds after 3 s), so a watch is always visible on the Mac; the pill's Location state is kept so the platforms share one pill rule and its tap still opens the same details toast. Hiding the pill's Location state on the Mac would remove the duplicate.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":992},"end":{"line":999},"content_hash":"9afe5ccf80a1ef0c39d5e7de37c68142a947b54b9857eed1f54371133b466c4e"},"summary":"On the Mac the Clax pill keeps saying Location beside the toolbar's Location item, rather than leaving location to the toolbar","tags":["revisit:the Mac's toolbar carries the pill's other states (Working, New version)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:36:01.867797Z","id":"0422186cd44b5e62c022292ab1efe1d554679c6f59d58d0cc9684649098b0ea5","body":{"detail":"Draft.at is where the pick was when it was made (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts pickElement/pickRange/pickArea pass the box at pick time); the popover stays there if the page scrolls or relayouts under it. CSS pixels are taken as logical pixels, which holds at page zoom 1 and no pinch (macOS has neither).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2744},"end":{"line":2770},"content_hash":"0c02e8fc777e66807c81f2aa22e44f07452e5bdf6691469fb7a50efe9e0f5d91"},"summary":"The composer popover is checked only in widget tests: over the page's WKWebView in a running Mac app (drawn above the platform view, the keyboard in its field, Return through the macOS text input), and its place after the page scrolls are unverified","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:36:01.868405Z","id":"1499112145529d353902195cfc30aa7f63b40bfd405de73ac4a0866838a376cd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6b9a1d036613d848981ca5aba209260dbff608ebf341e13709946d7d1e0b68bd","summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 View › Reload App is enabled, titled Refresh, while Home is selected in a split window (ClaxMenuBar.reload, set from apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart; test/ui/app_menu_test.dart 'View › Reload App runs what it is given…'). With an app selected it is still disabled and titled Reload App.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/new_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:38.694846Z","id":"097956ba04f662ca5b9d05e970a9cab53742017c52497ddb87db2d87f23f0b56","body":{"detail":"showNewSheet uses showModalBottomSheet in every family and width, so New app (⌘N) on a wide Mac window slides a bottom sheet up over the split window, unlike every other ClaxSheet (lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"31d33f8ce4554b807a21d61c3a8cac0d9b70c023e0bbe6f84a67c611105adfb9"},"summary":"The New sheet is a Material bottom sheet on the Mac, not a ClaxSheet hanging from under the toolbar","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.976546Z","id":"3577e5296471599e23b312e4c5bacc806bcfa0663192295f1350d9fd1bbf2de3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0422186cd44b5e62c022292ab1efe1d554679c6f59d58d0cc9684649098b0ea5","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f1c07f346b12 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): comment-light/dark.png show the popover drawn over the page's WKWebView beside the pick. Still unverified: the keyboard in its field and Return through the macOS text input, and its place after the page scrolls.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.977412Z","id":"33540355f243fa29f5def23c6b2107ace145e1bf98f1e6921ab044d0e9f36640","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"098fa2674ee5a04b2ce6ddf57ff7b631804febce9c41fb4a03c79151f1c3e1bc","summary":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/mac_chrome_test.dart presses Escape with the composer up after a click in the page and expects it closed when the app is active. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f1c07f346b12 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): skipped (no key window).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:23:15.188135Z","id":"6cb5b1b7a4617e9f2b4355399d0fc2417fd16d3d9bff5e84aee5ef303dfc7929","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 puts the build and change chips' content in a side sheet on Android wide. Working and Building are the bar's BarStatus, whose tap opens the change (showChangeSheet) or the plan (showBuildSheet side: true) in a side sheet; the outcome keeps WorkingChip's Retry, Retry send, the reply link and dismiss in a strip so none of them is behind a tap. The strip moves the page down while it shows and back up when dismissed.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2576},"end":{"line":2588},"content_hash":"31e66de89ad39c7e6c065bfbae6ae1829443dd80e6c4053ae29087adb0078eaf"},"summary":"In a pane, how a change ended (WorkingChip's outcome) is a strip between the top app bar and the page, pushing the page down, rather than shown only in a side sheet","tags":["revisit:the owner wants the outcome in the side sheet only, or the page must never move","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:23:15.188319Z","id":"bceec8301949596f09d7618f977d44a3d9139b655eb955039d86461a963d8ca2","body":{"detail":"The sheet and its scrim are inside the AppScreen body, so the app bar's Threads button stays usable to close it and the rail stays reachable. Material's modal side sheet normally covers the whole window with its scrim. The Mac's pane keeps its 280 to 420 resize edge.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2416},"end":{"line":2455},"content_hash":"a8788353b1515565b2260d3698a4cd30054e50e84ee1cc402b044ef6b86bc7b3"},"summary":"Below large width the threads modal side sheet lies over the page under the pane's top app bar, not over the whole window, and is a fixed 360 dp on Android (no resize edge; AppSettings.threadsWidth is the Mac's only)","tags":["revisit:a Chromebook or tablet session shows the sheet should cover the bar, or people want to resize it","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:23:15.188420Z","id":"51dd3a1a7fe0a79b8f745b7b9e85050fa938d3a1c7e6fb578672a50b6661d9d1","body":{"detail":"split_shots_test.dart's split-app scene draws a stand-in detail, not AppScreen. Share from the bar uses PluginBundleFiles(toFile: false) with the share sheet anchored at the screen's centre. Phase 8 (device verification) should look at the bar beside the rail, the side sheets' scrims and the inline toasts' width in the split's detail.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2874},"end":{"line":2900},"content_hash":"c1b25106405a802e428bb421abae64e9a82aa08ca607c88b374e852366077321"},"summary":"The app in a pane is rendered only as AppScreen alone in the window (test/ui/shots/app_shots_test.dart app-pane-*), not inside SplitShell beside the rail and list pane, and is unverified on a tablet, foldable or Chromebook","tags":["phase:8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:23:15.188508Z","id":"789dd940fbccb12596daae0233671ac7331f4bc28bb4108cdaf92b0df1cb08ac","body":{"detail":"test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'More offers Inspect, Versions and Star…' runs without a HomeHost, so Star is not offered there. A test needs test/support/split_fixture.dart's HomeHost with a readable layout/main.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3008},"end":{"line":3050},"content_hash":"cb9773dc42fa3731f97deb1a74bd4f3f0ab3309372bd55f95f3f791463154f3f"},"summary":"The pane's More › Star and Unstar (HomeLayout.star/unstar through widget.home.layout) has no widget test; only Inspect and Versions are tested","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:23:15.188815Z","id":"744a869b00a7287d543c913771fc37f627e1c296be184a44c4fbad898b3e2a35","body":{"detail":"The change sheet is shared with the Mac and was left as it is; moving it onto ClaxSideSheet (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/kit/sheet.dart) for the Material family would make the two sheets on wide Android match.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"7ac174f79ab7d979147087ac9706a59583018a8a8eb0e1166f02db56fd3a091d"},"summary":"The change's side sheet (showChangeSheet from medium) is 400 dp with its own 20 dp corner and black26 scrim, while the plan's (showBuildSheet side: true) is the kit's ClaxSideSheet, 360 dp with radius-lg and the palette's scrim","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:36:00.075529Z","id":"df4af55c174a6419efafce3f1b597dc4f7e54175d06df4f3c225377e1ba991f8","body":{"detail":"SplitShellState._report sets HomeHost.setQuery from the list pane's search while it holds the toolbar; Launcher reads no HomeHost.query, so typing in the list pane's search narrows the list pane only. The launcher's Import app… lived in its bar's overflow (lib/ui/launcher.dart PopupMenuButton 'launcher-more'), which is not drawn while railed; neither the rail nor ClaxListPane offers import (the home app's own page drops its bar the same way, home/home.js ownBar).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":267},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"892b215ece3fc89bd3dc1097d5fcd4fbc2652deaa16187041f58b23ab64d037c"},"summary":"Beside the Android rail at expanded the built-in launcher drops its bar, but its grid does not follow the list pane's search, and Import app… is reachable nowhere","tags":["android-wide","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:36:00.075633Z","id":"227863f5dc10b1aba932326d4945a68a304b14965571c111ad8e57bccef6da26","body":{"detail":"Seen in target renders split-inbox-wide-*.png and split-inbox-expanded-*.png (apps/clax_app/test/ui/shots/split_shots_test.dart). The chips keep the 24 dp wide gutter; a 16 dp gutter in a pane, or a filter menu, would fit them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":640},"end":{"line":660},"content_hash":"36b5043ca95f83811dc42cd694a601612585be9f6ce52a8ecbeaaf025c681d4d"},"summary":"In the 360 dp inbox list pane the four filter chips (All, Unread, Questions, Changes) are wider than the pane and scroll sideways, Changes cut at the pane's edge","tags":["android-wide","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.326015Z","id":"2e8f40c811c6261a004b5a26e19fd41b6ab954b96beb38e2325bff13b6e70509","body":{"detail":"Escape is a CallbackShortcuts binding in the Flutter focus tree. After a tap in the page the platform WebView takes the keyboard focus on macOS and Flutter sees no key events, so Escape does nothing; Cmd-K still works there because it is the native menu item's key equivalent (app_screen.dart _menus). Unverified on the built macOS app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2513},"end":{"line":2517},"content_hash":"7331e446b7a2a1deeb35e3316b69cd118d0b19febdcb0ecc906cab18233b0c4f"},"summary":"Escape closes the panel only while Flutter has keyboard focus, not while the WebView does","supersedes":"098fa2674ee5a04b2ce6ddf57ff7b631804febce9c41fb4a03c79151f1c3e1bc","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.380510Z","id":"c105b39c1fd1f69626fdeea26581a0ea08e1d6c801ca5c6df4f3c6731bd209c2","body":{"detail":"_retryChange calls onRetry once per failed thread, awaiting each. FeedbackWorker.retry (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:577) queues a job and calls _kick, and _drain dequeues it synchronously (_next, worker.dart:332), so the second thread's job cannot be merged into the first: a change that was one run for threads [a, b] becomes two runs. When the first starts while the second retry is still awaiting the threads list, WorkerWorking([a]) clears the Retry (ChangeTracker._newWork), retried() then does nothing, and b is not tracked until its own WorkerWorking, so after a lands the chip goes idle and comes back. The usual failed change has one thread; a FeedbackWorker.retryAll(aid, tids) that queues every thread before kicking would keep the change whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1764},"end":{"line":1779},"content_hash":"6dacb3084c3543cb0eb1a282bffc229cdbf67940ae6ecafd27feaf4ba64aedfc"},"summary":"Retry of a failed change that answered several threads runs them as separate changes, and the chip can go idle between them","supersedes":"287cd716ee56ce6aff649efb229d3ca554610d5ca8b31c6782e63234a68e4c11","tags":["review","u2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.445825Z","id":"f18590c11a44a6899165c2015ccb3e625b97bd2e9288d51ba2b82806111bb698","body":{"detail":"_tellVisible stops every running watch when the screen is not visible, and visible is false whenever the screen's route is not on top: a second device consent dialog (say camera.take while watching), the thread page, the inspector or the questions sheet's route all end the watch with stopped. The consent dialog that a watch's own start shows is spared only because watches still asking are skipped (DeviceHost.stopWatches, asking: false). If pages find this disruptive, stop only on lifecycle hide, the screen's dispose and a new document, and treat Clax's own routes over the app as still on screen.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":814},"end":{"line":819},"content_hash":"f27a7e41deb050a4940214d50996e15724ec2056ed1f8cfbc88e129ebab1b129"},"summary":"A location watch stops whenever anything covers the app screen, a dialog of the same app included","supersedes":"664cefd459207408cfed6d1f68658e94c0b8b47bf009c6b7a196bc9c7142aa23","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.500654Z","id":"7aba6247bbb20a4d7fc4b6fc3640f5ba614b12d85dc8b5fbae3e035d9feb86a5","body":{"detail":"While a draft is open the Scaffold does not resize for the keyboard (resizeToAvoidBottomInset: !composing) and the composer is positioned at viewInsets.bottom. Widget tests at 320x568, 390x844 and 1100x720 with a 260 dp inset and text scale 1.3 hold Send, Cancel and the field above the keyboard with the page rect unchanged. Not checked: that the Android platform-view WebView keeps its size (no relayout of the app's page) when the Flutter TextField raises the IME, and that focus moves cleanly from a page input to the composer field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2372},"end":{"line":2424},"content_hash":"87ca5a9043c738c9f404f6ad06f233b34d2e68ababf29420f8a5101376fa4a2b"},"summary":"The keyboard-over-the-page layout while composing is verified in widget tests and renders only, not on a phone","supersedes":"e2d39b88dc7e26e0524037958ead89b91bcf6a6dac71b6c7ffda9fa1b724eb7d","tags":["android","unverified-on-device","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.554656Z","id":"2713e7df182f3d8382826fc742c047a5598f3f4a4eb6cdb1bc8e1b728cf31172","body":{"detail":"_pillState gives ClaxPillState.working for any change in flight (ChangeTracker.working), and ClaxPill.label for working is 'Working' (lib/ui/working_chip.dart). Before the pill, the Working chip's step line read 'Waiting for connection' (ChangeTracker adds that step on WaitingForConnection). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 lists only Working, Building, New version and Location, so a person offline sees Working until they open the sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"16434150ad58fd6e11057f1bfa47ac79f3f050dff721c5951285ed319a14416c"},"suggested_fix":"A fifth pill state (or the working state's label) for ChangeTracker.waitingForConnection, if the owner wants it on the pill.","summary":"The pill says Working while a change waits for the connection; only the change sheet and the thread page say Waiting for connection","supersedes":"0866747170b89edfe143c4e327e37c349a97b1b5ff642cb0ad8dbbc396540a89","tags":["ux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.625647Z","id":"9f1a09e80e37083874a4b76aad8b3da84c2c0e6473953ee3f7be340a6a41c16c","body":{"detail":"_pillState orders working, building, newVersion, then location, one state at a time, and a toast of the screen hides the pill. Android 12 and later still show their own location indicator in the status bar; before Android 12 nothing of Clax's says so while the pill says something else.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"16434150ad58fd6e11057f1bfa47ac79f3f050dff721c5951285ed319a14416c"},"summary":"Location in use is the pill's last state: while a change, a build or a new version shows, the pill does not say location is in use","supersedes":"242f96cc2cc22a10fb0a52a636c318aa69cece03a5fe7f4268e88d9850c9af1e","tags":["privacy","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.680709Z","id":"0105696682eaa7231bdfba53c5a2913deeae2811b127fd9d04ca23cdbbabaeb4","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 gives the hint's two lines for notifications off ('Turn on notifications to comment from the shade.' with Turn on) and refused ('Use the Comment tab on the right to comment.'). With notifications already on, _hintCard says 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.' with only the dismiss button. Until Task 29 adds the Comment tab, the refused line points at the edge handle's place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3082},"end":{"line":3100},"content_hash":"84de059562f7b0880d7b880b5c1366f99a106ade4242a46dcad75e6d0617d247"},"summary":"The first-run hint's line with notifications on, 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.', is not in the spec","supersedes":"b613e3968e2814988d5b35579224b0adf98924c3df87f9ab664f3c2deec686e9","tags":["copy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.735806Z","id":"8ebf96ab07bb7a93b823729c1a71b366c05e3d3bfb9fff509bf77357e879fbf0","body":{"detail":"_withBanners puts the 48 dp ClaxBanner in a bg strip above the page, which shrinks by the strip's height (about 64 dp on a phone) while an agent drafts or its draft shows. Laid over the page it would cover the page's heading for as long as the draft lasts, the defect record 8cded220 describes for the web banner (web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte), so it moved to the foot of the stage there. The cost of pushing is a WebView resize when the banner comes and goes. Renders: target/flutter-app/shots from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_native_overlays_shots_test (app-drafting-*, app-draft-showing-*).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2670},"end":{"line":2702},"content_hash":"c50bb698913b605a72555959eef2b939d35bd4a5a08633af4ef391b6c46c01aa"},"summary":"The native draft banner laid over the page's top, as the Clax pill and top toasts are, instead of pushing the page down","supersedes":"b74e83e276c3ba87bd6adbbfc004287722a0bd74648ea457a232e70ff362578f","tags":["revisit:the draft banner's resize of the page shows as a jump or reflow on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.791002Z","id":"7b3a398cbd2f71ba90818b95146289bfa61174655d9a347ae69d654f28429de5","body":{"detail":"_pillState returns null while _toastUp is set. A shell notice with an action or error tone (AppScreen._stays) now shows with ClaxToast.show(stays: true) and stays until Try again, its close button or the next notice, so while a failed follow's notice waits the pill does not say Working, Building or New version. A New version toast that the notice replaced is offered again only once the notice goes (_offerNewer waits on ClaxToast.current.closed).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":581},"content_hash":"aff59d5de2775e59560d1a2bb69cbe30239e5a3cbfb5155d07f581a1053bb892"},"suggested_fix":"Let the pill show beside a notice that stays (place it clear of the notice card), or show the notice's state in the pill.","summary":"The Clax pill is hidden the whole time a shell notice that stays is up","supersedes":"2287426edba0be84298efa97ee897eddd008c2733240c4211b41ea4a95159c0f","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.845257Z","id":"073969596d6b872ba8ce15506f2298dda57d1819501ba1515cac77c57e69560d","body":{"detail":"HistoryMsg (lib/ui/host_protocol.dart) carries `back` only and there is no GoForward call, so docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §4.4's Forward (page history, then the app selection) has nothing to act on. Giving it one is a contract change (docs/contract.md, web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, the kit's fake host, the prompt copies).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1015},"end":{"line":1057},"content_hash":"2e5af19637c7293db38e9d2b8283809aa0ae4163d32df849ecd97a2642c5d22b"},"summary":"The toolbar's Forward is always disabled: the shell's history message reports only whether the page can go back","supersedes":"cc194284c155d0e8c1f119e7c32be9128cc71409019468dc24a011b5725dfef2","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.909592Z","id":"792752d77650441f92147218452b47d2b46a7e14b05ef199d2d32a617a55076a","body":{"detail":"The sidebar and its search arrive with the split layout (plan Tasks 46 and 47); Working opens the change popover and New Version replaces the pill's state, so the pill keeps both until those items exist. ToolbarItemSpec and Toolbar.swift take any SF Symbol item; NSSearchToolbarItem and a custom working item are not built.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1015},"end":{"line":1057},"content_hash":"2e5af19637c7293db38e9d2b8283809aa0ae4163d32df849ecd97a2642c5d22b"},"summary":"The toolbar carries Back/Forward, the title, Comment, Threads and Share; §4.4's Toggle sidebar, Working, New Version and Search items are not declared yet, and the Clax pill stays over the page on the Mac","supersedes":"e6f6fb7b0c71ab8e4ebb454897a9dab4c755ade2d06029eb5912e3b545bd874a","tags":["macos","revisit:the split layout's sidebar lands (plan Task 46)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.983135Z","id":"df595cdfd4f255102b8feaf29433ca2250e935cf579ea0598dd334557db38f16","body":{"detail":"The toolbar item shows whatever the pill says (the pill puts Working, Building and New version before Location and folds after 3 s), so a watch is always visible on the Mac; the pill's Location state is kept so the platforms share one pill rule and its tap still opens the same details toast. Hiding the pill's Location state on the Mac would remove the duplicate.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1037},"end":{"line":1044},"content_hash":"9afe5ccf80a1ef0c39d5e7de37c68142a947b54b9857eed1f54371133b466c4e"},"summary":"On the Mac the Clax pill keeps saying Location beside the toolbar's Location item, rather than leaving location to the toolbar","supersedes":"4fd19903d2f20588e3536816caf815a45db1c6c4ca3d28815b536e0fd23bde32","tags":["revisit:the Mac's toolbar carries the pill's other states (Working, New version)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.045129Z","id":"cf7c9b84dc4c86f2cb4615dc11f3a72c875a1d21817c167aa66c1f7ed396d952","body":{"detail":"Draft.at is where the pick was when it was made (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts pickElement/pickRange/pickArea pass the box at pick time); the popover stays there if the page scrolls or relayouts under it. CSS pixels are taken as logical pixels, which holds at page zoom 1 and no pinch (macOS has neither).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2848},"end":{"line":2874},"content_hash":"dd40718df3af6f8be4fc93eef4c318575a015ac87657b79395d3a09163edd214"},"summary":"The composer popover is checked only in widget tests: over the page's WKWebView in a running Mac app (drawn above the platform view, the keyboard in its field, Return through the macOS text input), and its place after the page scrolls are unverified","supersedes":"0422186cd44b5e62c022292ab1efe1d554679c6f59d58d0cc9684649098b0ea5","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.162648Z","id":"28e07701689eda601cefb5eeb6d6a916f75d183b764a3666635029acd1e4ab90","body":{"detail":"Matching a new item locally would mean reimplementing the daemon's inbox search (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs) in Dart, and a mismatch would show items the search excludes. A new matching item shows on the next refresh, pull to refresh, or query change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":374},"end":{"line":389},"content_hash":"cca6c0b1458cbbce5642aa10529e26474d7c1f4e538e9f40ecfb1275fb19872c"},"summary":"While a search is active, live inbox_item events update rows already shown but never add new ones","supersedes":"2ecff98ba13f64555d8e885cde3877e7b995fa7b5767d8fe38bb2d67898cad25","tags":["revisit:the owner expects searches to update live","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.231265Z","id":"46b87bc23c7499ad1901fce5d4a4d8ba1c0d0e9c63d59435325b1db84b05979a","body":{"detail":"lib/ui/kit/banner.dart draws the Apple family as a full-width inline bar with a hairline under it, meant for the top of a pane. The launcher wraps each banner in EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(16, 0, 16, 8) for the Material card, which the Mac form keeps (render: target/flutter-app/shots/launcher-banners-mac-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_screens_shots_test). The split layout (plan Task 46) is where the Mac banner's place gets settled.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":971},"end":{"line":973},"content_hash":"66d7206fab7750b0285d55fde5a68cff1848311e91bc005cfbddad1903e29361"},"summary":"On the Mac the key and recovery banners draw ClaxBanner's Apple bar inside the launcher's 16 dp side padding, so the bar is inset rather than the pane's full width under the toolbar","supersedes":"6d394e8120bb9058ad65cdf165e465440212e1eb8761bf33a10fe9b8c3e323de","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.635200Z","id":"93e1829145d823ecda297e659927b4c4601f413b5bb161d040e7548d73188d1f","body":{"detail":"ThreadView.stranded (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart) is the same condition: the app's worker took the change and never answered, for example after the app was killed mid-run. While the app runs, the worker reruns stranded threads at start, so 'Clax is working on it' is right then; but the thread page cannot tell a running change from one whose run died until the worker picks it up again. If stranded threads are ever left unrecovered, the page should read the worker's running threads (the change tracker's) instead of inferring from the feedback state.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"cdbae2cc61f7f7abb63b2af6b35e75fe440cd88cf76c3d78ec2141fa88acbebd"},"summary":"threadStatus reads a sent thread whose feedback is acknowledged and unanswered as working, also when no worker is running it (a stranded thread)","supersedes":"14d2ae32f6d7c68d0fd19ba684431ffcf74ad8ca507137687ddec9e7cefd78f8","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.161051Z","id":"8220d61c499e8d2429b56c948efc54102ce6e36a817ac9d162bf91194ec26e39","body":{"detail":"_handler maps only Settings, New App, Import App, Inbox, Comment, Show Threads, Back and Home; every other menu command answers null, so ClaxMenuBar sends setEnabled false. ClaxMenuBar.titles and MacMenu.setTitle exist, but AppRoot passes no titles: View › Show Threads reads 'Show Threads' while the panel is open, because CommentsCommand (lib/ui/app_menu.dart) does not know whether it is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":228},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"425fa35550c801b9d2d221d882b59ea5f253079d095c08348f6a8820edd17a90"},"suggested_fix":"Wire each command where its surface lands (the split layout's sidebar and selection, the toolbar, the app screen's reload and zoom), and give CommentsCommand the panel's open state for the title.","summary":"Share App…, Show Sidebar, Reload App, Actual Size, Zoom In, Zoom Out, Forward, Inspect, Versions…, Star and Resume Build stay disabled, and no item's title flips (Show/Hide Sidebar, Show/Hide Threads, Star/Unstar)","supersedes":"6b9a1d036613d848981ca5aba209260dbff608ebf341e13709946d7d1e0b68bd","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.241354Z","id":"037a16253704c709c661d16a816051834c5ed278d7f5976311be838b6cf1230e","body":{"detail":"Each pointer down and up over the page calls claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase, x, y}) by runJavaScript, after the WebView already handled the touch. The page converts physical pixels by window.devicePixelRatio, visualViewport.scale and its offset (host_protocol.dart AttestPointer). Widget tests check the Flutter side only (FakeAppSurface records the call); nothing has run a long-press in an Android WebView to confirm the shell takes the pick (record 8cc89df6 in web/bridge/src/.qual).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2337},"end":{"line":2353},"content_hash":"029ca55d91698c96622585f45f99365a570976a2eb2451e5e28e6220283478ba"},"suggested_fix":"Task F10 or a device run: long-press an element in app mode on Android and macOS and confirm the pick, with the attestation in place and without it.","summary":"Finger attestation and its CSS pixel conversion are unverified in a real WebView","supersedes":"86741946a5822ff25f5c663de4f4cd2c8da49498616a5114f2d54d3e54c9634c","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.322474Z","id":"be403ae689ca084933d263a5214f5ccd1a723a3c66a3ebc4e1f41dc50b4840f8","body":{"detail":"The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.7) describes the panel as a sheet over the lower 45%. Here the page is resized to the space above the panel instead, because the shell docks its composer at the bottom of the WebView (web/shell/src/app/app.css): an overlay would hide the composer and its Send button. The cost is a page relayout when the panel opens or shrinks to the peek.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2385},"end":{"line":2394},"content_hash":"01f32b22da5b399c0d8a5cf7a89b9e4495b316e11b0f9b741a7109bfcf1a94ba"},"summary":"Narrow-screen panel laid over the lower 45% of the page","supersedes":"4c2bfc9063e576c6ad98007072b6dbf8a6220e880b7f2f3a7dbff7feb3c6fecb","tags":["revisit:the shell's composer stops docking at the WebView's bottom, or the relayout on panel open proves janky on a device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.377710Z","id":"c260e2ccf652ee8c863df7d1857d12efe106178d9feb0681d9f09c2179c420da","body":{"detail":"The bar is laid out under the page instead (the WebView shrinks by its height, and it takes the bottom inset), and the floating button hides while it is up, its close standing in for a second tap. Over the page, the bar and the button would cover the page's bottom bar and lower-right corner exactly while the person is trying to hold on things there. The cost: the WebView resizes once when comment mode turns on and off.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2629},"end":{"line":2632},"content_hash":"b89b451f4344870748febc04cb73b3b1b6245d48afa6da7209c95568cd817106"},"summary":"Comment bar laid over the page, with the floating button kept above it","supersedes":"0fb89b9e1f117ba102288b32dfd546a12bd4d5399b61782e6fb34714b7ccb2b9","tags":["revisit:a page re-lays out badly or loses its scroll position when the bar appears","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.443047Z","id":"e15929b2400d352f8e7155b74b9f864ae4a70323302bba512fe25ce1b3c86aed","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§10.2 asks for a question badge on the comment button and for the sheet to open by itself. The comment button no longer exists, and the app screen draws nothing of Clax's over an app but the Working chip, brief toasts and the first-run hint (app_screen.dart class doc, 'No Clax control over the app'); an unprompted sheet over the app would break that. The open count still shows where Clax surfaces things: the change sheet's 'Clax has N questions for you' with Answer (change_sheet.dart _question). The agent waits at most 45 s on a change's question (AskTool maxWaitChange), so a missed toast leaves the question in the inbox and its late answer re-runs the change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1295},"end":{"line":1310},"content_hash":"daaf166dfbee7c5580780269a77a1799b4f4c9268477e15d3cddabbf74c1b933"},"summary":"The app screen does not open the shell's questions sheet by itself when a new question about the app lands in front, and shows no question badge; it shows the toast 'Clax has a question' (View: openQuestions) and a light haptic","supersedes":"e6aad054d0aa41f6bc9d7737c9ac14504019d3aafceb99fc8b1398b958f9e6c9","tags":["revisit:the owner wants the questions sheet to open over the app by itself, or a count on the open app's notice","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.499351Z","id":"b3d0d167e34538f782923da085660fc962bc536708c75c858a787ae3f53c8041","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"cc2a8277c1b678ad2425da6f067df6c3f1af7a02dc9a6b01c54878a245aeed9c"},"summary":"Changes is read as the kinds version, published and finished; replies show only under All and Unread. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.4 names the chips but not what Changes holds.","supersedes":"fe65f11c0e6ea980dda177e8e987669cb9e73be081b0200eceadfabe1fc50a13","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.555470Z","id":"3f5fb92fa8af42f6dce19f5ce082505727b572fc5fc0afe6512600efa51e1675","body":{"detail":"The tile's status line is one line wide (two lines overflow the cell by 18 px, seen in a render of test/ui/offline_shots_test.dart), and 'Waiting for connection' is cut to 'Waiting for …'. The tile shows a cloud-off icon and 'Offline'; its build view and its screen reader label say 'Waiting for connection'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":724},"end":{"line":734},"content_hash":"764a39c0d237684e46183441d354db65746efeb64828e0c1780c700f394b055e"},"summary":"A make waiting for the connection reads 'Offline' under its tile, not 'Waiting for connection'","supersedes":"7b568e1991b8276db425c9edd375d5c8a03a2a19fdb3569d8b48629c0f3447de","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:24.044596Z","id":"a3c01f4879d493f494456ed53e7e2cd8b6541138f534182d4cd35509e0bde69e","body":{"detail":"Observed in apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart with NSEvent clicks handed to the WKWebView (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift test input): attestPointer down before the click lets the shell take the pick (CSS pixel conversion correct at devicePixelRatio 2). With attestPointer up sent by runJavaScript right after the click, the page saw navigator.userActivation.isActive true in mousedown and false from pointerup on, and the shell answered clax:pick-refused; without it, isActive stayed true and the pick was taken. WebKit queues the mouseup behind the mousedown's acknowledgement, so the script runs between them. Whether the Flutter Listener over the platform view receives real macOS mouse events (so _attest runs mid-click) is not verified; if it does, clicks on macOS may be refused. Android (Chromium) is unaffected by this observation.","kind":"comment","references":"037a16253704c709c661d16a816051834c5ed278d7f5976311be838b6cf1230e","span":{"start":{"line":2337},"end":{"line":2353},"content_hash":"029ca55d91698c96622585f45f99365a570976a2eb2451e5e28e6220283478ba"},"summary":"On macOS WKWebView a press attestation counts (the pick is taken); a release attestation run between WebKit's mousedown and mouseup clears the shell's user activation and the pick is refused","supersedes":"7cbb2ab1609c8c479b74cf1b091f5a62ad27a9c86a0f1080423ff00774bd56d6","tags":["macos","webkit","f10","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:03.865337Z","id":"881bb15388a00b8fdb08b312a3ee2dd1f31ffa239138a11d3e13c927e3e2fe50","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: beside the rail the launcher's grid shows only what the list pane's search (HomeHost.query) holds, and the list pane's More offers Import app…; 'beside a wide Android rail the list pane's search filters the built-in home screen's grid' (test/app_test.dart) and 'the list pane's More offers Import app…' (test/ui/split/split_shell_test.dart) pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:app_test //apps/clax_app:ui_split_split_shell_test)","supersedes":"df4af55c174a6419efafce3f1b597dc4f7e54175d06df4f3c225377e1ba991f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:03.921877Z","id":"2f9b78f9e347431864fe1eaf10ed4e42ca6af5734d73c61ffa0c259c580c7197","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: in a list pane the filter chips wrap; 'in the 360 list pane every filter chip shows whole, also at 200% text' in test/ui/inbox_split_test.dart passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_inbox_split_test)","supersedes":"227863f5dc10b1aba932326d4945a68a304b14965571c111ad8e57bccef6da26","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_menu.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.128987Z","id":"3646e183b82f6ac79e06fab49685a29cdcf71ca2d05e866dfa2a3ccd9f65d78d","body":{"detail":"The Mac has the menu bar's key equivalents for this (record 05c0e170 covers what still misses there); Android has no menu bar, so ClaxMenuBar's Shortcuts are the only path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"328a17b5b0241bd09cb2df70aacf960c626bda61ba4b23658150f046701c5a4a"},"summary":"Off the Mac the Control (or iPad Command) shortcuts reach Clax only while a Flutter widget has the keyboard: with an app's page (its WebView) focused on a Chromebook, Control-K and the rest go to the page","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.129402Z","id":"4edda1eb568a7403eb03638573e5012652937ccf2b267b184a512305079babdd","body":{"detail":"One row would need about 8 points less padding on each chip than Material 3's filter chip, and still wraps at larger text.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":676},"end":{"line":684},"content_hash":"65aabac057d6ec9ac8689c4a796eb9ffb2c40eae821ecdd1a003c98129d37c97"},"summary":"In a 360 list pane the inbox's filter chips wrap (Changes on a second line) rather than fitting one row with tighter chip padding","tags":["revisit:a design asks for the four chips on one row in the list pane","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.182109Z","id":"3326098d38db6b80a880bc15a83a3faf60ec4dd8e47ee72b70d69367ed699370","body":{"detail":"Failure: on the Mac (or any _popsOver width), pick an element, then scroll the page until the pick leaves the viewport upward: the shell posts state.draft.at with a negative y (web/shell/src/app/host.ts pickAt, from the page's re-placing on scroll since f1c07f346b12), below = at.bottom + margin is negative, `below + childSize.height <= size.height - margin` holds, and y = below places the popover above the page's top edge. Scrolled past the bottom, `above` is past the page's height and is taken instead. Before f1c07f346b12 `at` was fixed at the pick, so this could not happen. The tests in apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart ('the popover goes above a pick near the page's bottom…') cover only a pick inside the page.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":3243},"end":{"line":3261},"content_hash":"59b1bb5c04e4ba722bcc691e16b0fe0c568b7da268390099ca534000aece1883"},"suggested_fix":"Clamp y into [margin, size.height - margin - childSize.height] in every branch (as clampX does for x), and add a widget test with at = Rect.fromLTWH(100, -500, 300, 40) and one past the page's bottom, both expecting the popover inside the page.","summary":"The composer popover follows its pick off the page: getPositionForChild never clamps y, so a scrolled-away pick takes the composer, its field and Send out of view","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.545612Z","id":"299943d30f3d243b14e9fb29181dd8900c05d4c257e8ead9612f57bf00b3c5bf","body":{"detail":"f1c07f346b12 documents iconChange as \"a sentence for the person\" on what became of a refused bundle icon (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart PublishedFiles.iconChange). Every caller drops it: bundle_sheets.dart:1311 (() async => (await installer.install(opened)).aid), home_install.dart:165, and this UpdateLanded case, which builds BundlePassed('Updated to v$version') with the truncated note only. The only trace is the version's note (\"...; its icon was redrawn (icon rule <code>)\"), which the person sees only in version history. Tests assert iconChange on the Installer and Updater results, not on any sheet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1395},"end":{"line":1399},"content_hash":"e3c8ddfa48ce3a28068cbf8d09511b718c76be2bb938f28c8f9a7274f911f6d3"},"suggested_fix":"Show iconChange in the install's and the update's success sheet (BundlePassed's note, beside the truncated note), and test it in test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart.","summary":"Installed.iconChange and UpdateLanded.iconChange reach no person: the install flow keeps only .aid and the update sheet's UpdateLanded case reads only version and truncated","tags":["review","bundles","icons","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:51.812272Z","id":"d056e14990d18cc158dd41b56faf335263ac57565dadd58c487e9224d849f32f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"ComposerPopoverLayout.getPositionForChild clamps y into [margin, height - margin - child height] in every branch. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test: 145 passed, including 'a pick scrolled above the page keeps the popover at the page's top, and one scrolled below it keeps the popover at its bottom' (at y -500 and 1500), which failed before the fix (Expected 32.0, Actual -428.0). The app-composer-scrolled shot (apps/clax_app/test/ui/shots/app_shots_test.dart, mac, light and dark) shows the popover at the page's top.","supersedes":"3326098d38db6b80a880bc15a83a3faf60ec4dd8e47ee72b70d69367ed699370","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:22:06.174294Z","id":"2e0662f25187fa6013204989c8084799e3a22321ba78abb17ea2d77d530c0fd3","body":{"detail":"Not taken: no version records its declaration, and the app knows one only for a base it changed itself, so the restore would roll back the title and capabilities for some versions and not others. They restore the version's files and keep the current title, icon and capabilities (test/home/home_recovery_test.dart 'Undo keeps the title, icon and capabilities the app has now'; test/ui/app_screen_test.dart's Restore and Undo assert restoreVersion carries no declaration). A restored page that uses a capability a later version dropped has those calls refused until the person adds it back.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2185},"end":{"line":2188},"content_hash":"43adfb328b6d69cf70c175d8190e13339c75cfc45f413de05c4de9f7e7884a55"},"summary":"Restore and Undo in the Versions tab (and the home screen's Undo, apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_recovery.dart undoLast) roll the declaration back to the restored version's","tags":["restore","ui","revisit:versions record their declaration in the core (the alternative on crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs restore_version_declaring_async)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:25:59.209596Z","id":"ae37943b8bbfbacb8ed41e1f9758dc625ef096bcde21c76f475e017f308e04c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: BundleSummary carries PublishedFiles.iconChange (\"Its icon broke Clax's icon rules, so Clax redrew it.\" / \"... left it out.\") and InstallSheet and UpdateSheet show it before the person agrees; Installed and UpdateLanded no longer carry the unread field. test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart's two icon tests failed before and pass now (//apps/clax_app:ui_bundle_flows_test); bundle-install-icon and bundle-update-icon shots (//apps/clax_app:ui_shots_bundle_sheets_shots_test) were looked at in light and dark.","supersedes":"299943d30f3d243b14e9fb29181dd8900c05d4c257e8ead9612f57bf00b3c5bf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:48.880397Z","id":"df1e6a58ff7ee28ca3455ffbfd522f44dff5e05493c74296bfe9904c737ae391","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 puts the build and change chips' content in a side sheet on Android wide. Working and Building are the bar's BarStatus, whose tap opens the change (showChangeSheet) or the plan (showBuildSheet side: true) in a side sheet; the outcome keeps WorkingChip's Retry, Retry send, the reply link and dismiss in a strip so none of them is behind a tap. The strip moves the page down while it shows and back up when dismissed.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2579},"end":{"line":2591},"content_hash":"31e66de89ad39c7e6c065bfbae6ae1829443dd80e6c4053ae29087adb0078eaf"},"summary":"In a pane, how a change ended (WorkingChip's outcome) is a strip between the top app bar and the page, pushing the page down, rather than shown only in a side sheet","supersedes":"6cb5b1b7a4617e9f2b4355399d0fc2417fd16d3d9bff5e84aee5ef303dfc7929","tags":["revisit:the owner wants the outcome in the side sheet only, or the page must never move","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:48.933113Z","id":"6a787176b6675a10a9ac235278b18c394c7888bb45316baae15a286fd9388a0a","body":{"detail":"The sheet and its scrim are inside the AppScreen body, so the app bar's Threads button stays usable to close it and the rail stays reachable. Material's modal side sheet normally covers the whole window with its scrim. The Mac's pane keeps its 280 to 420 resize edge.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2419},"end":{"line":2458},"content_hash":"a8788353b1515565b2260d3698a4cd30054e50e84ee1cc402b044ef6b86bc7b3"},"summary":"Below large width the threads modal side sheet lies over the page under the pane's top app bar, not over the whole window, and is a fixed 360 dp on Android (no resize edge; AppSettings.threadsWidth is the Mac's only)","supersedes":"bceec8301949596f09d7618f977d44a3d9139b655eb955039d86461a963d8ca2","tags":["revisit:a Chromebook or tablet session shows the sheet should cover the bar, or people want to resize it","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:48.985631Z","id":"6999a4f5c20b1abec703a98a5e314e14d01df0952c5bcf581174c53aca867655","body":{"detail":"split_shots_test.dart's split-app scene draws a stand-in detail, not AppScreen. Share from the bar uses PluginBundleFiles(toFile: false) with the share sheet anchored at the screen's centre. Phase 8 (device verification) should look at the bar beside the rail, the side sheets' scrims and the inline toasts' width in the split's detail.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2877},"end":{"line":2903},"content_hash":"c1b25106405a802e428bb421abae64e9a82aa08ca607c88b374e852366077321"},"summary":"The app in a pane is rendered only as AppScreen alone in the window (test/ui/shots/app_shots_test.dart app-pane-*), not inside SplitShell beside the rail and list pane, and is unverified on a tablet, foldable or Chromebook","supersedes":"51dd3a1a7fe0a79b8f745b7b9e85050fa938d3a1c7e6fb578672a50b6661d9d1","tags":["phase:8","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.037304Z","id":"f362355ec96cd8db9995ab39ffef69e6eafc4b4d96c4f21c05db9ce1ac2b580d","body":{"detail":"test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'More offers Inspect, Versions and Star…' runs without a HomeHost, so Star is not offered there. A test needs test/support/split_fixture.dart's HomeHost with a readable layout/main.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3011},"end":{"line":3053},"content_hash":"cb9773dc42fa3731f97deb1a74bd4f3f0ab3309372bd55f95f3f791463154f3f"},"summary":"The pane's More › Star and Unstar (HomeLayout.star/unstar through widget.home.layout) has no widget test; only Inspect and Versions are tested","supersedes":"789dd940fbccb12596daae0233671ac7331f4bc28bb4108cdaf92b0df1cb08ac","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.088861Z","id":"4838d4dc41c172d4aebbad2a22fed1af7800f7dde39d5692fdc79c5b98f0db7b","body":{"detail":"Escape is a CallbackShortcuts binding in the Flutter focus tree. After a tap in the page the platform WebView takes the keyboard focus on macOS and Flutter sees no key events, so Escape does nothing; Cmd-K still works there because it is the native menu item's key equivalent (app_screen.dart _menus). Unverified on the built macOS app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2516},"end":{"line":2520},"content_hash":"7331e446b7a2a1deeb35e3316b69cd118d0b19febdcb0ecc906cab18233b0c4f"},"summary":"Escape closes the panel only while Flutter has keyboard focus, not while the WebView does","supersedes":"2e8f40c811c6261a004b5a26e19fd41b6ab954b96beb38e2325bff13b6e70509","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.140133Z","id":"b106d0edd07b7a0fa3592e6ae93861980d87f32211d518ab9f83fa1e7503cf1d","body":{"detail":"While a draft is open the Scaffold does not resize for the keyboard (resizeToAvoidBottomInset: !composing) and the composer is positioned at viewInsets.bottom. Widget tests at 320x568, 390x844 and 1100x720 with a 260 dp inset and text scale 1.3 hold Send, Cancel and the field above the keyboard with the page rect unchanged. Not checked: that the Android platform-view WebView keeps its size (no relayout of the app's page) when the Flutter TextField raises the IME, and that focus moves cleanly from a page input to the composer field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2375},"end":{"line":2427},"content_hash":"87ca5a9043c738c9f404f6ad06f233b34d2e68ababf29420f8a5101376fa4a2b"},"summary":"The keyboard-over-the-page layout while composing is verified in widget tests and renders only, not on a phone","supersedes":"7aba6247bbb20a4d7fc4b6fc3640f5ba614b12d85dc8b5fbae3e035d9feb86a5","tags":["android","unverified-on-device","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.192410Z","id":"57d47a269ea6fbc70c6a596f6547d5c98f67898c42eb4cb53ddd74d0b81dc782","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 gives the hint's two lines for notifications off ('Turn on notifications to comment from the shade.' with Turn on) and refused ('Use the Comment tab on the right to comment.'). With notifications already on, _hintCard says 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.' with only the dismiss button. Until Task 29 adds the Comment tab, the refused line points at the edge handle's place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3085},"end":{"line":3103},"content_hash":"84de059562f7b0880d7b880b5c1366f99a106ade4242a46dcad75e6d0617d247"},"summary":"The first-run hint's line with notifications on, 'Pull down the shade to comment on this app.', is not in the spec","supersedes":"0105696682eaa7231bdfba53c5a2913deeae2811b127fd9d04ca23cdbbabaeb4","tags":["copy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.246705Z","id":"df02788fd2beabdcddad10810ea15544a373006cb30127508abd85e1b93300d8","body":{"detail":"_withBanners puts the 48 dp ClaxBanner in a bg strip above the page, which shrinks by the strip's height (about 64 dp on a phone) while an agent drafts or its draft shows. Laid over the page it would cover the page's heading for as long as the draft lasts, the defect record 8cded220 describes for the web banner (web/shell/src/ui/DraftBanner.svelte), so it moved to the foot of the stage there. The cost of pushing is a WebView resize when the banner comes and goes. Renders: target/flutter-app/shots from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_native_overlays_shots_test (app-drafting-*, app-draft-showing-*).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2673},"end":{"line":2705},"content_hash":"c50bb698913b605a72555959eef2b939d35bd4a5a08633af4ef391b6c46c01aa"},"summary":"The native draft banner laid over the page's top, as the Clax pill and top toasts are, instead of pushing the page down","supersedes":"8ebf96ab07bb7a93b823729c1a71b366c05e3d3bfb9fff509bf77357e879fbf0","tags":["revisit:the draft banner's resize of the page shows as a jump or reflow on a phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.300662Z","id":"e3cc0559a5f42e7a99e51d61c9312ada0571c66b8bf03f994911827f19a4cef5","body":{"detail":"Draft.at is where the pick was when it was made (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts pickElement/pickRange/pickArea pass the box at pick time); the popover stays there if the page scrolls or relayouts under it. CSS pixels are taken as logical pixels, which holds at page zoom 1 and no pinch (macOS has neither).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2851},"end":{"line":2877},"content_hash":"dd40718df3af6f8be4fc93eef4c318575a015ac87657b79395d3a09163edd214"},"summary":"The composer popover is checked only in widget tests: over the page's WKWebView in a running Mac app (drawn above the platform view, the keyboard in its field, Return through the macOS text input), and its place after the page scrolls are unverified","supersedes":"cf7c9b84dc4c86f2cb4615dc11f3a72c875a1d21817c167aa66c1f7ed396d952","tags":["macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.355280Z","id":"3c16d781b3bfc9f2dfbb07e93861be418e511414b42ce8f44083166314fc896a","body":{"detail":"Each pointer down and up over the page calls claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase, x, y}) by runJavaScript, after the WebView already handled the touch. The page converts physical pixels by window.devicePixelRatio, visualViewport.scale and its offset (host_protocol.dart AttestPointer). Widget tests check the Flutter side only (FakeAppSurface records the call); nothing has run a long-press in an Android WebView to confirm the shell takes the pick (record 8cc89df6 in web/bridge/src/.qual).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2340},"end":{"line":2356},"content_hash":"029ca55d91698c96622585f45f99365a570976a2eb2451e5e28e6220283478ba"},"suggested_fix":"Task F10 or a device run: long-press an element in app mode on Android and macOS and confirm the pick, with the attestation in place and without it.","summary":"Finger attestation and its CSS pixel conversion are unverified in a real WebView","supersedes":"037a16253704c709c661d16a816051834c5ed278d7f5976311be838b6cf1230e","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.410520Z","id":"cd930698050d664bee07bbb89f34b4c2bc1d6882fa4ef98f7b26f36db8577382","body":{"detail":"The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.7) describes the panel as a sheet over the lower 45%. Here the page is resized to the space above the panel instead, because the shell docks its composer at the bottom of the WebView (web/shell/src/app/app.css): an overlay would hide the composer and its Send button. The cost is a page relayout when the panel opens or shrinks to the peek.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2388},"end":{"line":2397},"content_hash":"01f32b22da5b399c0d8a5cf7a89b9e4495b316e11b0f9b741a7109bfcf1a94ba"},"summary":"Narrow-screen panel laid over the lower 45% of the page","supersedes":"be403ae689ca084933d263a5214f5ccd1a723a3c66a3ebc4e1f41dc50b4840f8","tags":["revisit:the shell's composer stops docking at the WebView's bottom, or the relayout on panel open proves janky on a device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.465251Z","id":"7967df6923fb048a611247201e4a2b3515e23593442ba44d2246adcd85ffe98d","body":{"detail":"The bar is laid out under the page instead (the WebView shrinks by its height, and it takes the bottom inset), and the floating button hides while it is up, its close standing in for a second tap. Over the page, the bar and the button would cover the page's bottom bar and lower-right corner exactly while the person is trying to hold on things there. The cost: the WebView resizes once when comment mode turns on and off.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2632},"end":{"line":2635},"content_hash":"b89b451f4344870748febc04cb73b3b1b6245d48afa6da7209c95568cd817106"},"summary":"Comment bar laid over the page, with the floating button kept above it","supersedes":"c260e2ccf652ee8c863df7d1857d12efe106178d9feb0681d9f09c2179c420da","tags":["revisit:a page re-lays out badly or loses its scroll position when the bar appears","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:49.520757Z","id":"7d93940aea6edd5767224ef4553d9c7d3736d54378b304700e55076981bf1e65","body":{"detail":"Unchecked: share_plus with XFile.fromData and the application/vnd.empathic.clax+zip type on Android (Files/Downloads targets), FilePicker.saveFile writing the bytes in the macOS sandbox, and FilePicker.pickFile with FileType.any on Android returning bytes. Widget tests drive the flows through test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart's FakeBundleFiles.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1057},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"ddceaf086448ec618d6c823fa4f5341b96162adf8f3752bce78b3c2220792f21"},"summary":"PluginBundleFiles (share sheet, save panel, picker) has run only behind FakeBundleFiles; nothing has shared, saved or picked a .clax file on a device","supersedes":"a22c402ec84c847fb362cb526842b88384f4b3b075b916aa7ea0d82215e71819","tags":["bundles","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:59.034987Z","id":"b38438f9dbb52b02e2c8c5c4d881a1fa9e5b55e9c1b745101c290d2191fdbc18","body":{"detail":"Observed in apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart with NSEvent clicks handed to the WKWebView (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift test input): attestPointer down before the click lets the shell take the pick (CSS pixel conversion correct at devicePixelRatio 2). With attestPointer up sent by runJavaScript right after the click, the page saw navigator.userActivation.isActive true in mousedown and false from pointerup on, and the shell answered clax:pick-refused; without it, isActive stayed true and the pick was taken. WebKit queues the mouseup behind the mousedown's acknowledgement, so the script runs between them. Whether the Flutter Listener over the platform view receives real macOS mouse events (so _attest runs mid-click) is not verified; if it does, clicks on macOS may be refused. Android (Chromium) is unaffected by this observation.","kind":"comment","references":"3c16d781b3bfc9f2dfbb07e93861be418e511414b42ce8f44083166314fc896a","span":{"start":{"line":2340},"end":{"line":2356},"content_hash":"029ca55d91698c96622585f45f99365a570976a2eb2451e5e28e6220283478ba"},"summary":"On macOS WKWebView a press attestation counts (the pick is taken); a release attestation run between WebKit's mousedown and mouseup clears the shell's user activation and the pick is refused","supersedes":"a3c01f4879d493f494456ed53e7e2cd8b6541138f534182d4cd35509e0bde69e","tags":["macos","webkit","f10","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:29:43.676767Z","id":"1b459fd9276cb195761966b080e84090f59cc6a1e17ae0f08c37650b2ecbd43f","body":{"detail":"The pin is the first ClaxHost message after the commit under a nonce of the navigation's set (apps/clax_app/lib/core/shell_link.dart ShellLoads.present). The shell's transport posts from boot (its stream hub's subscribe and its first calls), so the pin is expected before the load event; that it is, in a real WebView on Android and Apple, is unverified until plan Task 17 gives a surface a core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":243},"end":{"line":252},"content_hash":"dddf8382dacfa7102f0d461c5c492b6ef390880ec8c9a22b4e47cac0ffde5d4b"},"summary":"On the core claxHost.init waits for both the document's load and the pin: a shell document that posts no ClaxHost message before its load event gets no init until it posts one","tags":["unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:48:36.058790Z","id":"5d7fa9ae1fd0aef7150128d8ab5d2f5d08bff02ecb223e65ae92b9b4fe0933ea","body":{"detail":"Untested in the surface itself: no ClaxHost JavaScript channel is added when a core is given (line 109); every setNavigationDelegate goes through _setNavigationDelegate; load (lines 287-294) waits for the attach; _initOnCore (lines 245-252) runs claxHost.init once both the load (onPageFinished) and the pin have happened, in either order, with the pinned nonce; onPageStarted clears _loaded. load also still loads after it raised the not-attached fault (line 293), so an unattached WebView requests the shell URL from the network (Android: an .invalid host that does not resolve) instead of stopping.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"76a0e7e4e6fa305a4fecc8043bfbe91aa683f21301b241753131635a9fc782d4"},"suggested_fix":"Add a dev dependency on webview_flutter_platform_interface and a fake WebViewPlatform whose controller records runJavaScript and lets the test fire onPageStarted/onPageFinished; test the surface with a FakeCore and a recording SchemeHostPort: no addJavaScriptChannel, attach before loadRequest, init after load-then-pin and after pin-then-load, none before both. Return from load after the fault.","summary":"WebViewAppSurface on the core is not exercised by any test: the 'on the core' group of test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart drives CoreShellLink and SchemeAttachment directly","tags":["review","task:15","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:48:36.060478Z","id":"8256f69c7a3435addaa106f434fdf880def2851f57c377fe5af866cb8d51c0f2","body":{"detail":"runJavaScript runs in the committed main-frame document, the only shell-origin main frame, so its meta is the load's own nonce; ShellLoads.present(nonce) still requires it to be in the committed number's set, so a result that arrives after a newer commit pins nothing. No transport bytes. Tests: a surface test (fake WebViewPlatform, see the concern on webview_surface.dart:94:130) where onPageFinished comes with no message before it and the meta read answers the candidate: init runs with that nonce; one where the read answers a nonce of another number: no init; and the stand-in (web/e2e/app-scheme.ts) gains the same pin rule with an e2e case whose shell makes no call before load (a shell page with its stream hub held, e.g. hold() before goto and release() after load).","kind":"comment","references":"1b459fd9276cb195761966b080e84090f59cc6a1e17ae0f08c37650b2ecbd43f","summary":"Proposed fix: at onPageFinished, when no nonce is pinned, read the main document's clax-nonce meta with runJavaScriptReturningResult and pin it if it is a candidate, so init never depends on the shell posting first","tags":["review","task:15","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:12:04.085962Z","id":"9350a13f595240ff4e7d945cd519ab25e561a5017524a41d4e32bf53ec2df608","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The pill has a waiting state: _pillState and the pane bar give ClaxPillState.waiting while ChangeTracker.waitingForConnection, which reads 'Waiting for Claude' (spoken 'Clax is waiting for Claude') with the resting mark (lib/ui/working_chip.dart). Evidence: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test //apps/clax_app:ui_clax_pill_test PASSED ('a change waiting for Claude says so on the pill, its sheet and its thread page…', 'a change waiting for Claude says so in the top app bar, whose tap opens the change').","supersedes":"2713e7df182f3d8382826fc742c047a5598f3f4a4eb6cdb1bc8e1b728cf31172","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/launcher.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:12:04.859748Z","id":"edb4c50186599ad80d961fd0bbbf46dba4de7398ecb82b1ca50b1fac1f3ba0fb","body":{"detail":"The tile's status line is one line wide and ellipsizes (two lines overflow the cell by 18 px). 'Can’t reach Claude' (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §15) does not fit a four-column phone cell: the render offline-launcher-phone-*.png of test/ui/offline_shots_test.dart shows 'Can’t reach Cl…'. The home app's tile (apps/clax_app/home/home.js MAKE_STATUS, .h-line in home.css) ellipsizes the same way. The cloud-off glyph and the screen reader's 'Waiting for Claude' carry the rest. The split sidebar's row has room and shows the whole line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":724},"end":{"line":735},"content_hash":"db90f7267fc59e214fa0b8707e139d37cce612eb332b177b12c4ab358f82500f"},"suggested_fix":"A shorter tile line (the build view and screen reader keep the long words), a two-line status with a taller cell, or accept the ellipsis.","summary":"A make waiting for Claude reads 'Can’t reach Claude' under its tile, cut to 'Can’t reach Cl…' on a 412 dp phone","supersedes":"3f5fb92fa8af42f6dce19f5ce082505727b572fc5fc0afe6512600efa51e1675","tags":["ux","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/user_message.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:12:05.587154Z","id":"6752961f2681893cc193ea29812b1609b87bf0b3fa0acdfdcc6d310c65f77339","body":{"detail":"userMessage maps SocketException, HttpException and a WebView net::ERR_ fault to _noAnswer (lib/ui/user_message.dart:38, 41, 54). With the core in the process (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §15: no transport state for local work) these come from the Claude API or a page's own fetch, not from Clax; the line was left as it is because which failures still reach it depends on the daemon transport's removal (plan task 30).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"0f25d0c2005f5d5d3e9b6449792226da3f8ece5d1378ec5051ef09a705a13939"},"suggested_fix":"Once the HTTP transport is gone, map what remains to the Claude line (_unreachable) or to _unknown, and drop _noAnswer.","summary":"A socket or net::ERR_ failure reads 'Clax’s service didn’t answer.', words for a local service the in-process core no longer is","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:42:33.175741Z","id":"1b615035d2813284bd5280ff356be0cd67beafcacbaf0d1fc5e6748d37db0560","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart group 'WebViewAppSurface on the core' runs the surface over a fake WebViewPlatform (test/support/fake_webview.dart): no ClaxHost channel, attach after the delegate and before the load, init after load then pin and pin then load, once; load returns after the not-attached fault and loads nothing (ui_webview_surface_test: PASSED; analyzer and copy fixes in f1c07f346b12)","supersedes":"5d7fa9ae1fd0aef7150128d8ab5d2f5d08bff02ecb223e65ae92b9b4fe0933ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:42:35.273140Z","id":"661d5aed9e666888c28a8d97392bc9d6280fe45a9eb494d8d96220b79344e515","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed as proposed in 8256f69c: at onPageFinished with nothing pinned the surface reads the clax-nonce meta with runJavaScriptReturningResult and the link pins it only if it is a candidate. Tests: webview_surface_test.dart 'a document that posts nothing before its load is pinned by its clax-nonce meta…' and 'a meta read that answers another navigation's nonce pins nothing' (ui_webview_surface_test: PASSED); e2e case in 647958f22844 ('a shell that posts nothing before its load…': PASSED)","supersedes":"1b459fd9276cb195761966b080e84090f59cc6a1e17ae0f08c37650b2ecbd43f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/render_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:38:46.021127Z","id":"c48a2915b62818cd4c52816df7e3e410668961f4ac22103eb5c00c2b1408ee1a","body":{"detail":"The service has no API of its own: it loads <shell>/a/<draftId>?app=1&inspect=1 and reports what that shows. A draft written after the Render was emitted is rendered at its newer revision while the answer names the request's. The shell's Ready carries the version it shows (lib/ui/host_protocol.dart Ready.version); the inspector does not hand it out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"3b6a16c94d65534c49e1a790721e2ca8c2be4a60a93c147b2fa1d1f2390c702a"},"summary":"A render draws the draft as it is when loaded; RenderRequest.revision is not checked against what the page shows","tags":["render","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/render_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:38:46.021172Z","id":"5a40b9e4f0f564c101b461a3d6f301d9954197817a96589902d25839d533c0b4","body":{"detail":"Without it canRender stays true and only InspectorLost (WebViewInspector.dispose) or a cancel loses a render; a WebView torn down with the activity then ends only by the worker's 60 s deadline.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"e313e4b3ab9b653bb503039755defc68b95cd83ffbe43b85e04be6cdef201a18"},"summary":"Nothing passes RenderService its available listenable yet: the app's lifecycle (UI engine detached on Android, background on iOS) is the wiring's to give","tags":["render","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/make_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:37:27.468884Z","id":"b571f866a0da03759d550fb6e011139ef004740ee4ddd53beef28c5e9783e3e1","body":{"detail":"JobView (apps/clax_app/lib/queue/model.dart) holds id, kind, state, waitingFor, step, title, artifactId, error and offers. MakingScreen (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart) shows the run's narration, the page as it is written, the plan (by MakePlanKey) and the last render from MakeSession.log/updates/planKey, which read MakeNarration (MakeLive.narrationOf). With IsolateQueueClient (apps/clax_app/lib/queue/isolate_client.dart) as AppServices.queue and no MakeLive, a build view shows the job's state and offers only: no narration, an empty preview, no plan until the app exists, Try now hidden, and the stopped view's spend reads $0.00 (make_service.dart MakeSession.stopped). Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.2 names QueueState and send as all the UI knows of the queue, and says nothing of progress.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"072e9e0df8d9418100c1a4aad87906d31cb0eeacabab99db5c07e85073b42be6"},"suggested_fix":"Decide where a running job's progress reaches the UI: progress messages from the worker beside PublishState (a MakeLive the isolate client implements), the draft read from the core, or none.","summary":"QueueState carries no make's narration: the build view's log, page, plan key, render and stop account come only from MakeNarration, which only the in-isolate LocalQueueClient offers","tags":["queue","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:37:27.469144Z","id":"4cc73fb1936ad4a66570d7144609be21d98da11dfe602dce456c879d428e8ca8","body":{"detail":"JobView has no threads, landed version or narration, so ChangeTracker (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/change_tracker.dart) keeps workerWorking/workerLanded/workerReplied/workerProgress from AppScreen._onWorker, and the queue's change job (QueueStateJobs.changeOf, by artifact) drives only waitingForConnection, Stop (Cancel), Retry and Keep going. The thread page's Cancel stays FeedbackWorker.cancelThread (one thread alone, as resolve 10b0994e fixed it) and its Retry and Send again stay FeedbackWorker.retry, because Cancel and Retry name a job, and a change job can carry several threads. Once the worker isolate runs changes these events stop and the change UI loses its steps, landing timing and per-thread actions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1663},"end":{"line":1730},"content_hash":"6f11617079ebf53f4092b710ef3947e3a223f4b2e41854f23d1994356d1eef2a"},"suggested_fix":"Add the change's threads (and its published version) to JobView, and a per-thread intent or a rule that a thread's cancel cancels its job; then drive ChangeTracker from QueueState alone.","summary":"The app screen still takes a change's threads, steps and landed version from the feedback worker's events; the queue's job gives only its state, waiting for Claude and offers","tags":["queue","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/local_queue.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:37:27.469229Z","id":"3d5ec73998c7ff0a337ea68a2f92a855256b26a9153650d69aafc09348ba7e31","body":{"detail":"Each WorkerWorking for threads that are not the open failed or queued job's starts a new job 'change-<aid>-<n>' and cancels the one before; Retry of a change is FeedbackWorker.retry per thread, answered queued or failed with nothing_to_retry; makes run in this isolate (LocalMakes). lib/app.dart uses it whenever AppServices.queue is null, so until IsolateQueueClient is injected the app's makes still run on the UI isolate.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"23ac0fe2b6f3cc0908d79c911ca3d2f04a0250704b7581be873a86e5cbef121d"},"suggested_fix":"Delete it (and LocalMakes) once lib/app.dart builds IsolateQueueClient, with the narration question of the make_service.dart record settled.","summary":"LocalQueueClient is a stand-in: its change jobs are made from FeedbackWorker events with IDs that last one launch, it ignores Change intents, and it keeps every ended job in memory","tags":["queue","status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/making_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:37:27.469314Z","id":"0f4baf72cfc074ce1e0c2518dbb6eebb0db1c2b20ab8cfaec65a32978c52a820","body":{"detail":"MakeService.start sends Make and the queue starts the run; the build view (pushed a frame later) starts sayFirstOutput in _attempt. say-usable still starts at Make (lib/app.dart). The two timings no longer start together (test/app_test.dart 'New runs the agent…' now expects them unordered), so say-first-output reads slightly shorter than the person's wait.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":695},"end":{"line":710},"content_hash":"822ebdbc7c669d8684dcfec294b15cd256bff91327bb48b995eef6b7233fc0b8"},"suggested_fix":"Start sayFirstOutput where the Make is sent (with say-usable), or accept the frame of difference.","summary":"say-first-output now starts when the build view shows, not when the run starts: a make runs from Make, before its build view is up","tags":["timings","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/error_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:11:43.880257Z","id":"aec2b9362f23a99d6650547ad7ad79843070678558c014c992414c44d1e110dc","body":{"detail":"CoreHost.open runs once and its state never leaves CoreFailed (lib/core/core_host.dart _on). ErrorScreen.failed shows Copy details only. A retry would need CoreHost to open again after a failed open, which CoreClient allows (a failed core released the home, spec section 2.5).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"3cb25021c207f6563d4a203a7774903e1b397d531cfaaa55a674432806c5de60"},"suggested_fix":"Give CoreHost a retry() for CoreFailed with code home_in_use or internal, and pass it as onRestart for those codes.","summary":"A core that did not open has no Try again: a home_in_use failure (a second Mac instance, a close still running) needs the person to quit and open Clax","tags":["core","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/render_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:31:32.888663Z","id":"7cca0cf115dc1f5c47af062bfb05e3288ef8bf9cae718f74d511826f37ba0184","body":{"detail":"Without it canRender stays true and only InspectorLost (WebViewInspector.dispose) or a cancel loses a render; a WebView torn down with the activity then ends only by the worker's 60 s deadline.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"825e2755adb83972cc1f4e94c169b343261958f4542d593902d27fe29d5ae69a"},"summary":"Nothing passes RenderService its available listenable yet: the app's lifecycle (UI engine detached on Android, background on iOS) is the wiring's to give","supersedes":"5a40b9e4f0f564c101b461a3d6f301d9954197817a96589902d25839d533c0b4","tags":["render","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/render_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:31:32.966368Z","id":"9cfe572e8840bca1c1bc4985a213893b4f8687c074ade3a46e241d6ee06a52c9","body":{"detail":"The service has no API of its own: it loads <shell>/a/<draftId>?app=1&inspect=1 and reports what that shows. A draft written after the Render was emitted is rendered at its newer revision while the answer names the request's. The shell's Ready carries the version it shows (lib/ui/host_protocol.dart Ready.version); the inspector does not hand it out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"97bb934ed6ab16e8e35be4c80db88d31f22e4c9ff100137957e427a5189bc745"},"summary":"A render draws the draft as it is when loaded; RenderRequest.revision is not checked against what the page shows","supersedes":"c48a2915b62818cd4c52816df7e3e410668961f4ac22103eb5c00c2b1408ee1a","tags":["render","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.113223Z","id":"fa0ecd60754e955ed866f03e394cc078f95882ba43ab713cc5d363fb3e04486b","body":{"detail":"Spec section 7 asks for a reload when the WebView process goes away. WKWebView's web content process ending arrives as a main-frame WebResourceError (webview_flutter_wkwebview), which this handles; webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 exposes no render-process-gone callback through NavigationDelegate, and Android's default for an unhandled renderer crash kills the app process.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"e4d122a72b9e0aac5e82ce2aad83f625e63d119945acd7e7fdc5454b1268bef6"},"suggested_fix":"Handle onRenderProcessGone through webview_flutter_android's platform controller (AndroidWebViewController) if a later version exposes it, or in the app's Kotlin MainActivity.","summary":"An Android WebView renderer crash is not handled","supersedes":"1ee688df3a5b126d6b15fab47a78837d45e08c5943d36b8f7789b2153056221e","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.591260Z","id":"6b6e8df96ad946ed9c0f205f461065b0a8c899e3ef038f4a4181f89828f336ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart is deleted and WebViewAppSurface sets no key cookie: on the core the WebView loads from the app's scheme and the core gives the shell document the owner's credential.","supersedes":"18cb7cff96af19d765c9dd603aadfc03fe8e61475ef0203d4f4471deeccf805c","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.703973Z","id":"dab1d53fbc1c5c63a7e8e4a79779bf169fed09248ded2cfeb685e33d2cb1e234","body":{"detail":"lib/main.dart, integration_test/rig.dart, ios_rig.dart, tool_loop.dart and tool/eval/live_build.dart all pass core and origins; only test/ui/webview_surface_test.dart's static decide() tests and the `core == null` branches (the ClaxHost JavaScript channel, _onMessage, coreShellBase's null) remain for a WebView that loads from an http base.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"9b790d0ab49b92736515e6aa5fd29790dada1f6e1b23ed374414628c8ed2e0fe"},"suggested_fix":"Make core and origins required and delete the JavaScript-channel path and its doc lines.","summary":"WebViewAppSurface's mode without a core (the loopback daemon's) has no caller in the app any more","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/local_queue.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:17:14.348949Z","id":"00b30904fbcf83ab4ed0a6222455bb51b74f373e46b951f9431a56471766130e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3d5ec73998c7ff0a337ea68a2f92a855256b26a9153650d69aafc09348ba7e31","summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 the app runs makes in the queue's worker isolate whenever AppServices.startQueue is given (lib/main.dart gives it unless a debug build's scripted agent is set). lib/app.dart builds LocalQueueClient only for services with neither queue nor startQueue: the app-level tests (test/app_test.dart, test/app_background_test.dart) and MakeService.local's users (test/ui/make_service_test.dart and the shots tests) still need it, so it stays until they move to FakeQueueClient or the worker.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/render_service.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T01:22:43.609539Z","id":"162a8dcde6807b7a1959ae1c423e91faefddc1a909e4caebba1183e8c481f435","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7cca0cf115dc1f5c47af062bfb05e3288ef8bf9cae718f74d511826f37ba0184","summary":"Proposed for close by the owner: apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _startQueue builds RenderService with available: _renderable, which the lifecycle handler sets false on detach (all platforms) and on paused or hidden on iOS.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/build_plan.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T18:57:50.813766Z","id":"d35745e2153b3548cd53c93ea6085927b929177c2aec939603dc54fdf4f7850f","body":{"detail":"HomeHost.buildOf (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart:495) counts an app's going queue job by JobView.progress before BuildLink; the launcher's app tiles (BuildWatch over BuildLink), the Working chip (lib/ui/working_chip.dart:625-660) and the build view count only the UI isolate's PlanStore and FeedbackWorker's BuildState. Today no queue job carries an app ID while it builds (only makes run on the queue, and a make's row gets its app ID when it is done), so nothing is missed yet; a change or continue build moved to the queue would show its ring on the home app only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"0e8cd2874efc0af0698c59ffec00bd0e05bbd92cb6d58a13b94712154f6316fc"},"summary":"The native launcher's app tiles, the Working chip and the build view read builds only from BuildLink, not from a queue job's progress","tags":["queue","build","ui","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_cover.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:03:54.596856Z","id":"2487637f70b9f015f14aa6d69ac9c4c31022f64c4e894ea71cdb1e5032a0e8e1","body":{"detail":"The cover is the plain surface for AppCover.markAfter (100 ms) and then only the mark, so a quick load shows nothing. Drawing the icon and title at once would show something on every load; drawing them with the mark at 100 ms is the option kept open. The failed cover still shows the icon (AppCover._failed).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"5802a70d771c7a195211843cacf6446c4ff067152322c4d5e47b24b9cc9c049c"},"summary":"Loading shows the working mark alone on the plain surface; the app's icon and title, which showed from the first frame before, are not drawn while loading","tags":["ui","revisit:the person finds a loading app hard to tell apart without its icon and title","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_cover.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:03:54.598346Z","id":"10bb9f992e2dcd3de4a808412f28b1c0cdec5e6ebf8ebb104b37d7aa5a483a06","body":{"detail":"With MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf the ClaxMark draws still and AnimatedOpacity has no fade, so holding it for AppCover.markHold would only delay the page. A still mark shown for a few milliseconds can still read as a flash. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'under reduced motion the still mark is not held'.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"e916bbfaa64b14fdbecb14070b3d907899f0bf3454d18d907ba15bbf3468bc58"},"summary":"Under reduced motion the cover lifts as soon as the page is up, even with the mark showing: the still mark has no breath to finish","tags":["ui","accessibility","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:52:05.767536Z","id":"607334f7dfa47dc697cfdb71dc8d340ddcde44c04a9b16f2805f6d24030c8a31","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"57d47a269ea6fbc70c6a596f6547d5c98f67898c42eb4cb53ddd74d0b81dc782","summary":"Owner's decision: drop the app screen's first-run hint entirely, in every case (the notifications-on line, 'Turn on notifications to comment from the shade.' with Turn on, and the refused line pointing at the Comment tab). Commit f1c07f346b12 removes it: AppScreen.firstRunHint, onHintShown and the hint card, AppSettings.appHintSeen, and AppNotice.turnOn, which only the hint called; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md §5.2 records the hint as removed.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:52:05.767824Z","id":"27773ba12941b549cb34ff0cda1e7ca645edcce2f6ab9d13238c3a62d8248395","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Obsolete: the first-run hint this concerns is removed in f1c07f346b12 by the owner's decision (see the reply on this thread). bazelisk test via `just test-affected f1c07f346b12` at f1c07f346b12: 136 tests pass, among them //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test, //apps/clax_app:app_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_settings_test, //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_app_shots_test, //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze and //apps/clax_app:apk_test; `git grep -n -e first-run-hint -e firstRunHint -e turnOn -- apps/clax_app/lib apps/clax_app/android ':!*.qual'` finds nothing (exit 1).","supersedes":"57d47a269ea6fbc70c6a596f6547d5c98f67898c42eb4cb53ddd74d0b81dc782","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.320563Z","id":"ef58f5b1d4caac04409a98cd75184600306f952408014d83c729b1aa8ea9c5a7","body":{"detail":"A 40 dp strip would give the page 8 dp more, but the pill's 48 dp target (ClaxLayout.target; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md: 'Targets: 48 dp on Android everywhere') would then reach 4 dp over the page below the strip, or the target would need an asymmetric pad reaching up into the status bar's band. 48 dp keeps the target whole inside the strip and the pill where it was (8 dp under the top inset). Renders: target/flutter-app/shots/app-working-phone-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_app_shots_test.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":65},"content_hash":"0fa2e0e22a8d51c3c8b264d4694da6fa84c5c61c166be19e32655faa4a5b9010"},"summary":"The pill's strip is 48 dp at 100% text (the pill's 48 dp target, the 32 dp pill 8 dp from each edge) rather than a slimmer 40 dp","tags":["revisit:the strip reads as too tall on a phone, or the pill's target rule changes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.320657Z","id":"c66f86802ea6f675bb81e7562c9568b8d61104827cd6572ba9bbe9a9b961efc8","body":{"detail":"The strip is on bg with the pill 8 dp from its lower edge, so the shadow's lower blur paints over the top of the page (visible as a dark smudge on a dark header in target/flutter-app/shots/app-building-phone-dark-200.png). It covers nothing a person reads or taps, but the page is no longer entirely clear of Clax. A level-1 shadow in the strip, or clipping the shadow to the strip, would keep it off the page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":549},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"5381293d7b09121b6250e24d2d1be6f8dfa7e5f552e089f0b0df413d1e698074"},"summary":"In the pill's strip the pill keeps its level-2 shadow (blur 24, 8 dp down), which falls a few dp onto the page's header under the strip","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.320787Z","id":"3365bdf28c0d574d59d0ddb37b5cfb4bc2e32d53a631b37990f3de17c4594439","body":{"detail":"_top draws only the hint now; the pill moved into PillStrip (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart). With both showing, the hint card covers the strip's pill. The hint is due to be removed; if it stays, it should sit under the strip.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3160},"end":{"line":3185},"content_hash":"8edf1c2232aed0b105b1adcded398bef69c2ba84a4f7bd698fc7a2a1fe434bf7"},"summary":"The first-run hint still lies over the page's top at 8 dp under the top inset, so while the pill's strip is open it lies over the strip and the pill","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.320884Z","id":"4214279f7ab547d09a7af3eff7341e6f85867c54ed7ffeb6ef8433e6685583c7","body":{"detail":"While the outcome chip or a toast is up the pill shows nothing (_pillState), so the strip closes after PillStrip.grace and the chip or toast then covers the page's header, as the pill used to. A change that ends with its New version toast slides the page up, then down again when the pill says Working until the frame shows the version.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2877},"end":{"line":2883},"content_hash":"35a08c8e20c226e93df22725a9d4a0d91e8ee7c0e55935de0c562f7a0cead7cc"},"summary":"How a change ended (the outcome chip) and the top toasts still lie over the page's top on a phone and the Mac; only the Clax pill has a strip","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.320922Z","id":"3ea07e88b5f5445177eb65d2f4169744fd805d8cba509af9bc39cedd511d8847","body":{"detail":"Unverified on a device: that Android's WebView and macOS's WKWebView relayout once as the strip opens and closes (a single resize event, window.innerHeight the strip's height shorter), that env(safe-area-inset-top) stays 0 (the WebView sits under the top inset either way), that a platform view moved by the strip's Positioned slides without jank, and that the clip while it slides does not cost a frame. Tests: apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_device_test.dart group 'the pill's strip'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":216},"content_hash":"e4a53f989b4c6884c7626dd7d8116abc1213fe3516800eb297b3fad9bcda8db5"},"summary":"The strip's resize of the page is checked in widget tests and renders only, not with a real WebView on a phone or the Mac","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.321515Z","id":"0d6bd46ab019612672349b3a6b60aa583d03e72f6c4cc89fdc15597859058308","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"08d98af838521a0a053a9c20d007c31a481eeaffd153bccf839de2489aafd937","summary":"The pill no longer sits over the page's header: it is in its own bg strip above the page (PillStrip, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart), so in the light theme its fg fill stands on bg, not on a dark header (target/flutter-app/shots/app-working-phone-light.png). Proposed close as fixed.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.321819Z","id":"46f0580b431a9a28590a1d90de2d497c06aa1838bb106596d69b6adae9a6d1a3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"792752d77650441f92147218452b47d2b46a7e14b05ef199d2d32a617a55076a","summary":"The Clax pill on the Mac is no longer over the page: it sits in the same strip as on a phone (PillStrip, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart), under the window's toolbar, and the page moves down by the strip's height while it shows (target/flutter-app/shots/app-working-mac-light.png).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:25:36.322096Z","id":"2aef864d6cf3511c27fe5580ff7e00fdcd8f135e15b2d3a26fef8b72087967ab","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"df02788fd2beabdcddad10810ea15544a373006cb30127508abd85e1b93300d8","summary":"The Clax pill no longer lies over the page's top: it has its own strip that pushes the page down while it shows (PillStrip, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/pill_strip.dart). The draft banner and the top toasts are unchanged by it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/versions_tab.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:55:09.785206Z","id":"915ee4dc5f32843a7302812789c103d41ffc9a4af86cd9bd398f129c92cd80ca","body":{"detail":"versionMarks marks the last entry of link.published as public and earlier ones as was public. An app pulled as an author starts with published empty, so no row is marked until this device publishes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"60bb778879c76c7358dc90771b7cb2529a7ea94c94e02a6070ab7b639916c94b"},"summary":"Version marks come from AppLink.published only: a version someone published from the web, or one this device took on a pull, is never marked public","tags":["area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:13:38.338186Z","id":"13a86c3c9934aac233a629dcf1fcd39819cd88a3a8b574b5d79d90d24de64b8d","body":{"detail":"AppScreen.linkedHead (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:316) is read in initState only: comments switched off on the remote while the app is open are not seen until it opens again, and a head that cannot be read (offline, signed out) counts as comments on, which the remote then refuses. No caller passes linkedHead yet (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart builds AppScreen without it), so hiding the composer is inert until the app wires it to the linked app's RemoteHead (RemoteApi.head or anonymousHead for LineageEntry.link).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1206},"end":{"line":1222},"content_hash":"58b9b4559fcb48bb6744bf92f314e645b8d87610a145156178f99383dde7e218"},"summary":"The linked head is read once when the screen opens and a missing or failed read leaves the composers on; nothing passes linkedHead yet","tags":["deferred-wiring","spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.11","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:43:06.868640Z","id":"43767d26e6d3f1eaf418f997bef303549b5aebfdc5c179b5ba7bbbb3bca4d89d","body":{"detail":"_readHead cancels an open draft (CancelDraft) when the head says comments are off; a person who started typing before the head was read loses the text with no notice. Only AppAction.comment, a pushed StateMsg draft and the thread page's reply bar are pinned (apps/clax_app/test/ui/thread_detail_remote_test.dart:199-256); the pane's Comment button, the Mac toolbar item, the Comment tab's menu and a head arriving with a draft open are not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1218},"end":{"line":1222},"content_hash":"5d017aed78bfa9cef914d7c567c8298c05a7e7e93e7af9939487add87abfb071"},"suggested_fix":"Say why the composer closed (a toast: comments are off on <remote>), and add widget tests for the toolbar, pane button, tab menu and late-head paths.","summary":"A comments-off head arriving while a composer is open discards its text without a word","tags":["review","spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.11","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:14:04.001713Z","id":"c8339335099f572c1c0ca67bc65b7a883dc51047f9b34adfffbe2150323f147c","body":{"detail":"The ahead and update states are ClaxPill states (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/working_chip.dart), and the pill is the phone layout's. In a pane the screen shows the 'Claude made vN' and 'vN is ready' toasts inline once each, and Versions' Publish, but the bar (BarStatus) has no lasting ↑ v5 here · v4 public or ↓ v6 ready.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3177},"end":{"line":3186},"content_hash":"e962e5292a565513634f97333f26ab96acb0597b0098920c7fb1ee463d74837b"},"summary":"An app in a pane (tablet, foldable, Chromebook, Mac) shows no ↑ or ↓ state: the pane's bar status has only Working and Building","tags":["spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.4","area:remote","ux","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:15:17.426727Z","id":"ff05434fb3cd0e765aebe702ab55d48d8c1d7e586589a541715029588c56778a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b9fb6c6a4","summary":"The app passes AppScreen.linked (LinkedAppHooks over LinkedChecker.status); the screen follows each status, taking the composers away when the head says comments are off and back when on, with no second head read. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:app_remote_test PASSED at b9fb6c6a4: 'a linked app opened reads its head once, and comments off take away its composer' fails both cases with linked: _linkedHooks removed from app.dart; test/ui/app_screen_remote_test.dart 'the composer goes when the checker’s head says comments are off…' fails with _onLinkedHead() removed. The no-head-yet case remains as a new record.","supersedes":"13a86c3c9934aac233a629dcf1fcd39819cd88a3a8b574b5d79d90d24de64b8d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:15:17.495922Z","id":"0bc4d2e901d1e61bcd065f65976ff8fa80f43b17b8db71a6ab8328a8f32213ff","body":{"detail":"_onLinkedHead takes comments from LinkedStatus.head only; LinkedChecker keeps no head across launches, so an app opened offline whose copy has comments off offers Comment, and the remote refuses what is then posted when the link syncs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1300},"end":{"line":1302},"content_hash":"1cd52aa40c3595e44e0fe6774262366fddbace2dde36abe0f3e8b3916f93bd0c"},"summary":"Until a head has been read (offline at first open, or signed out of a Restricted copy), a linked app's composers stay on","tags":["spec:2026-10-21-app-push-pull#5.11","area:remote","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.380434Z","id":"725e011325f3c7c60752e4cf635662ce91c135b886b7309923b87589f4955378","body":{"detail":"BundleFlows routes both the plain update and Merger.bringIntoMine through this UpdateCheckFailed case. When bring is true, the version that failed is Claude's combination of vN and the person's version, not vN. The sheet still says 'vN didn't pass its checks on your data: <reason>', and Tell @owner (tellOwnerDraft) offers to report it to the owner as vN's failure. A merge that broke a test therefore produces a wrong bug report to another person, prefilled.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1786},"end":{"line":1800},"content_hash":"57477c98297a2c789366b1c4bd40a4de766bc39dce9ec6f225e3ca7335e25d47"},"suggested_fix":"When bring is true, say the combined version failed ('Your version with vN didn't pass its checks: <reason>. Your app is unchanged.') and offer no Tell @owner.","summary":"After Bring vN into mine fails its checks, the sheet blames vN and offers Tell @owner prefilled 'vN didn't pass its checks on my data'","tags":["review","copy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:46.380726Z","id":"5309394e1484f5f67e22c516afe024a942e693ea4a6b81ac78abe43ea280a9ff","body":{"detail":"BundleFlows (lib/ui/bundle_sheets.dart:1752) and RemoteFlows._resolve (lib/ui/remote/remote_flows.dart:458) build MergedOfferSheet without truncated. The confirm callback gets only Merged, not the draft check's docsTruncated, so a merge checked against a truncated copy of the documents is offered as 'Checked against a copy of your data'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":827},"end":{"line":850},"content_hash":"190aabffdfe72044ac5b67060517d0ddb2cb14869becea352e2e3746c031ca9e"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the check's truncated flag into confirm (Updater.update and takeFiles know draft.docsTruncated before asking).","summary":"MergedOfferSheet's 'Checked against part of your data' never shows: neither caller passes truncated","tags":["review","copy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.102463Z","id":"f9623a0fb4db1e4f69513a9e7a3e63107b9a55fa5412ebcfa8538b8ccdcbef30","body":{"detail":"_change copies the settings loaded when the screen opened and saves the copy whole. AuthorTrust._ask (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/author_trust.dart:150-158) and ensureInstallId (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/settings_store.dart:219-228) write the same file from other flows: a Continue at the trust sheet for a run started by a comment, or a first pull, while Settings is open (a Mac split window keeps it open beside the app). The next toggle in Settings drops the Continue, so the sheet asks again, or drops the install ID, so the next pull mints another and the remote counts the install twice. AppRoot._keep (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart:2988-2997) already reloads before saving.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":433},"content_hash":"b111bd434edd6d19f72c78bae17812c2bcc59b931b96ee556df000d5dce087c4"},"suggested_fix":"Make _change load, apply f, and save, as AppRoot._keep does.","summary":"Settings saves its whole copy of AppSettings, undoing trustedAuthors and installId written while it is open","tags":["review","concurrency","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:08:05.211732Z","id":"a3a6bd319051637116a5fd6e88c7947def0c9a1731982ba6eeb5a102e2e1d3dd","body":{"detail":"The core publishes approval_request on the inbox topic when a request changes (crates/clax-http/src/views/approval.rs listen); InboxScreen does not handle it, so a request decided on the web still shows its four choices until one is tapped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":470},"end":{"line":492},"content_hash":"61af4196891a95444fb85f7f3e6987b9470448016b4a9b3e7a8118b9279cf5b0"},"summary":"An approval row learns of a decision made elsewhere only when its sheet's Allow is refused (409 request_closed) or the inbox reloads","tags":["ux","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682847Z","id":"be500f0b2d280daaedf3e6115d98037c19d1e2f7d2965092629a65b035fdde96","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.2 says Disconnect revokes the token on the remote. DELETE /api/remotes/{id} (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:253-286) forgets the remote here even when the revoke failed (offline, or the remote refused) and answers {remote, revoked: false}; the token then stays valid on clax.dev until revoked on its People page. RemoteApi.removeRemote (lib/remote/remote_api.dart:222-224) drops the answer and _disconnect shows nothing, so the person believes the device can no longer act as them on clax.dev.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":258},"content_hash":"cb92dea668e923e5bc2702f446d8e4ddf619acc0c1ec2bcbd7e1fa0a16e15977"},"suggested_fix":"Have removeRemote answer revoked, and when false show 'Disconnected here. <host> still lists this device: remove it on <host>’s People page.' (or keep the remote and offer Try again). Add a settings_sharing_test case with revoked false.","summary":"Disconnect reports success when clax.dev did not revoke the device's token","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/approval_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.682885Z","id":"0bf8b717953eca13e2e402c957d06083bee7f8c7abad629c63d0f4e23353985a","body":{"detail":"The title, the held comments' prefix and the buttons 'Always allow <who> on this app' / 'Always allow <who> everywhere' all use r.author.name ('Bob (on clax.dev)'). CardPerson (lib/clax/models.dart:742-754) carries a public ID and a name, no login; a display name on a hosted Clax is chosen by its holder, so two different people named alike, or a stranger named like a trusted collaborator, read the same on the card, while the grant goes to the public ID. 'Everywhere' is the widest grant the card offers and it is made on this one string.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"c8459b91323e2248fbda8f1618e6ebae6f2878e1d3def5e8aadc7615d43d47c9"},"suggested_fix":"Show a stable handle beside the name (the remote person's GitHub login when the mirrored author has one, else a short form of the public ID), at least on the 'everywhere' choice; this needs the approval card's author to carry it.","summary":"The approval card asks the person to trust a stranger by display name alone","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.683044Z","id":"2bb6759643c0417eac61e50d5d659b5f3eb8500d9c0e81a8f0a83aa80c7321ac","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.11: 'Send to Claude on such threads runs the approval card.' In apps/clax_app/lib/ui nothing reads ThreadComment.withheld or WithheldNotice: the worker asks for approval in the background (lib/agent/worker.dart:803-838) and showApprovalSheet is reachable only from an inbox row (inbox_screen.dart _approve). On the thread page and in the app's threads panel a stranger's mirrored thread looks sent to Claude, with nothing saying Claude cannot read it until the person allows its author, nor a way to decide there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":986},"end":{"line":991},"content_hash":"82785aec0b3fccdcfa805ea9b533139b91ddef9f1f8e9d7b211150a3b41f2b8f"},"suggested_fix":"On a thread with withheld comments, show a line above the reply bar ('Clax keeps Bob’s comments from Claude until you allow them') with Review…, which opens showApprovalSheet for the thread's open request.","summary":"A thread whose comments are withheld until the person approves their author shows no sign of it, and offers no way to the approval card","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:01.683097Z","id":"c48c471f828cfebf8704833034a0b6b392cd51fc65646643345699f2a6d28877","body":{"detail":"replies: false (app_screen.dart and inbox_split.dart pass it from the head's comments flag) removes _composer, leaving the page with no reply control and no explanation; the person may think the page failed to load it. The publish sheet and the share sheet already have the words for it ('Off: nobody can comment, whatever their access').","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":991},"end":{"line":991},"content_hash":"8246893920a5ada6ac457d300372e6a7219bdf0f40039c8165fade33b98e5070"},"suggested_fix":"In the composer's place show a muted line: 'Comments are off on <host>. Turn them on in Share….'","summary":"With comments off on the public copy, the thread page drops its reply bar without saying why","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.467786Z","id":"f49a2694887ea63453d3c18706cf8d14ed6632ec027bd18f7034c5f541656f30","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:253-286 removes the remote whatever public::revoke answered and returns {remote, revoked}; apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:222-224 `await _json('DELETE', …)` returns void; apps/clax_app/lib/ui/settings_screen.dart:249-258 shows a snackbar only on a throw, then reloads the list without the remote. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md:157 says Disconnect revokes the token on the remote.","kind":"comment","references":"be500f0b2d280daaedf3e6115d98037c19d1e2f7d2965092629a65b035fdde96","summary":"confirmed: revoked:false from DELETE /api/remotes/{id} is dropped and Disconnect reads as done","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/approval_sheet.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.468053Z","id":"671cb41efdbdf0b8c15ceefe913bdb8e78611e86e027b42ce468e92650fe6a84","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/approval_sheet.dart:61 (title), :127 (`final who = r.author.name;`), :200 and :206 ('Always allow $who on this app' / 'everywhere'). CardPerson (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart:742-754) carries publicId, name and owner only; publicId is never shown on the sheet.","kind":"comment","references":"0bf8b717953eca13e2e402c957d06083bee7f8c7abad629c63d0f4e23353985a","summary":"confirmed: the approval sheet names the author only by display name, including on 'everywhere'","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.468842Z","id":"25b3a31a760517fbf6e7ac61c7ae149134c6e685eb176b5bc132ffaa6f6fd337","body":{"detail":"grep -rn 'withheld\\|WithheldNotice' apps/clax_app/lib/ui --include='*.dart' finds only doc comments in approval_sheet.dart:48-49; grep -rn 'showApprovalSheet(' apps/clax_app/lib finds only the definition and apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart:480. ThreadComment.withheld exists (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart:556-567). thread_detail.dart:989-991 shows only the held-reply card (publish-and-reply, :570) and the composer. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md:502-503: 'Send to Claude on such threads runs the approval card.'","kind":"comment","references":"2bb6759643c0417eac61e50d5d659b5f3eb8500d9c0e81a8f0a83aa80c7321ac","summary":"confirmed: no UI reads withheld comments, and the approval sheet opens only from the inbox","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:24:23.469104Z","id":"9fd8cddc1e424adbeb65d2331d74a411ea4364b8ca9ec988bccfcfcf06c47def","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/thread_detail.dart:991 `if (widget.replies) _composer(context),` has no else branch; replies is passed from apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:2146 (`replies: !_commentsOff`) and apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox/inbox_split.dart:253 (the record's 'inbox_split.dart' is at lib/ui/inbox/). Kind suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"c48c471f828cfebf8704833034a0b6b392cd51fc65646643345699f2a6d28877","summary":"confirmed: replies false removes the composer with nothing in its place","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
